  code_action {
    action_spec {
      create_file {
        instruction: "# LittleSteps \342\200\224 Step 0 Architecture & Implementation Plan\n\nLittleSteps is a calm, guided early-childhood parenting platform helping mothers and caregivers support babies from 0 to 24 months through bite-sized daily activities across six developmental domains, with private video practice submissions and constructive, rubric-based caregiver feedback.\n\n---\n\n## User Review & Critical Decisions\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> The four foundational architectural decisions below reflect your confirmed choices. One minor project configuration update is flagged for confirmation before Step 1 begins.\n\n- **Confirmed \342\200\224 Database & Backend Architecture**: Local SQLite with Express for the early prototype, isolated behind a clean Repository Layer and versioned REST API (`/api/v1`) so migrating to PostgreSQL / Cloud SQL and supporting future Android & iOS apps requires zero rewrite of UI or business logic.\n- **Confirmed \342\200\224 Children\'s Video Privacy & Retention**: Private, authenticated access via short-lived signed streaming tokens (never public URLs) with **30-day automatic deletion** plus immediate parent-initiated deletion at any time.\n- **Confirmed \342\200\224 Localization Strategy**: English first with an **i18n-ready architecture** (centralized translation keys, locale-aware age/date formatters, and translation-ready curriculum fields) to support Hindi and regional Indian languages cleanly in future releases.\n- **Confirmed \342\200\224 Visual Aesthetic Direction**: **Warm Calm Montessori Editorial** \342\200\224 serene, unhurried, high-legibility layout with generous whitespace and progressive disclosure so mothers are never overwhelmed.\n- **Confirmation Before Step 1 \342\200\224 Project Config Updates**: To support full-stack Express + SQLite APIs alongside React on port 3000 while preserving your existing Vite setup and asset-copying plugin, Step 1 will:\n  1. Keep all existing frontend tooling (React 19, Vite 8, Tailwind CSS v4, Motion, Lucide) untouched.\n  2. Add an Express server entry serving `/api/v1/*` and mounting Vite middleware in development (and built static assets in production) on port 3000.\n  3. Enable strict TypeScript type-checking (`strict: true`) and install only essential runtime dependencies (`better-sqlite3`, `multer`, `zod`, `cookie-parser`) when Step 1 is approved.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview, Core Concept & Workspace Inspection\n\n### Existing Workspace Audit\n- **Frontend Stack**: React 19.0.1, Vite 8.3.0, TypeScript 7.0.2, Tailwind CSS v4.3.3 (`@tailwindcss/vite`), `lucide-react` icons, and `motion` for gentle transitions.\n- **Backend Readiness**: Express 4.21.2, `tsx` 4.21.0, and `dotenv` 17.2.3 are already installed; the current dev script serves Vite standalone without an API server or database yet.\n- **Environment Constraints**: Port 3000 single-origin serving, HMR disabled cleanly via `DISABLE_HMR`, and existing asset-copy build hook preserved.\n\n### Core Product Concept\n- **Primary Audience**: Mothers and caregivers in India (responsive mobile-first web initially; API-ready for Android & iOS and global expansion).\n- **8 Age Groups (0\342\200\22324 Months)**:\n  `0\342\200\2233m` \302\267 `3\342\200\2236m` \302\267 `6\342\200\2239m` \302\267 `9\342\200\22312m` \302\267 `12\342\200\22315m` \302\267 `15\342\200\22318m` \302\267 `18\342\200\22321m` \302\267 `21\342\200\22324m`\n  Babies are automatically mapped to their exact 3-month band using their date of birth, smoothly unlocking the next stage as they grow.\n- **6 Learning Domains**:\n  1. Cognitive Development\n  2. Language and Communication\n  3. Physical Development\n  4. Social and Emotional Development\n  5. Sensory Development\n  6. Early Independence and Everyday Skills\n- **Non-Diagnostic Instruction-Match Principle**:\n  Reviewers evaluate **only the caregiver\'s demonstrated execution of activity steps** using an objective, weighted rubric that produces a percentage-based **Instruction-Match Score**. LittleSteps explicitly never scores, diagnoses, or ranks a baby\'s intelligence, developmental level, or health.\n\n---\n\n## 2. User Experience, User Journeys & Visual Design\n\n### Visual Identity & Theme \342\200\224 Warm Calm Montessori Editorial\nDesigned to feel like a serene, sunlit Montessori parenting journal rather than a noisy clinical dashboard or overstimulating toy store.\n\n- **60-30-10 Color System**:\n  - **60% Dominant Neutral Canvas**: Warm Chalk (`#FAF9F6`, `--background`) paired with pure Crisp Linen surfaces (`#FFFFFF`, `--surface`) and Deep Charcoal Forest Ink (`#1F2421`, `--foreground`).\n  - **30% Structural Surfaces**: Soft Oat recessed panels (`#F3F1EC`, `--surface-muted`), Warm Stone 1px hairlines (`#E6E3DC`, `--border`), and Slate Olive secondary text (`#57605A`, `--muted-foreground`).\n  - **10% Accent Budget**: Deep Botanical Eucalyptus (`#2F5D50`, `--primary`) for primary actions and active navigation states; Warm Honey Ochre (`#B87D2B`, `--accent`) strictly for gentle highlights and pending-review cues. All semantic states (Reviewed, Pending, Action Needed) pair color with explicit text labels and icons \342\200\224 never color alone.\n- **Typography & Hierarchy (2+1 Font Discipline)**:\n  - *Display & Editorial Headings*: `Fraunces` (warm, expressive literary serif with `text-wrap: balance` to eliminate orphan headline words).\n  - *Body & Interface Controls*: `Plus Jakarta Sans` (clear, human sans-serif at 15\342\200\22316px with 1.6 line-height for effortless one-handed mobile reading).\n  - *Scores, Timestamps & Metrics*: `IBM Plex Mono` with `tabular-nums` strictly for percentage match scores, video durations, age-month indicators, and audit timestamps.\n- **Layout & Restraint Rules**:\n  - **Top Bar Contract**: Single-row, three-zone header (`LittleSteps` wordmark \342\200\224 4 concise single-line links \342\200\224 1 primary action). Mobile sticky chrome stays strictly under 15% of viewport height.\n  - **Zero-Pill Metadata**: Domain names, age bands, durations, and statuses render as quiet unboxed typography separated by `\302\267` (e.g., `Sensory \302\267 6\342\200\2239 months \302\267 5 min`), reserving styled buttons strictly for interactive filters and CTAs.\n  - **Single-Elevation & Calm Pacing**: Flat surfaces separated by generous whitespace and 1px hairline borders \342\200\224 no nested cards-within-cards, no thick left accent borders, no decorative pulsing dots, and no wall-of-text paragraphs.\n  - **Motion Budget**: Subtle compositor-only transitions (`opacity`, `transform`) settling within 180ms (`prefers-reduced-motion` respected).\n\n### Complete User Journeys\n\n#### A. Parent / Caregiver Journey\n1. **Gentle Onboarding**: Create account (email + password, optional mobile number & locale) \342\206\222 Add child profile (name + date of birth) \342\206\222 System computes age in months and places the family into the exact 3-month age band.\n2. **Today\'s Calm Daily Journey**: Opens to a single focused focal anchor \342\200\224 *Today\'s 2\342\200\2233 Recommended Activities* (progressive disclosure: one primary card in focus, remaining cards quiet below). Caregiver can switch between Today, Weekly Progress, and Feedback History.\n3. **Guided Activity Session**: Opens an activity \342\206\222 Watches concise instructional video \342\206\222 Scans everyday India-friendly household items and safety reminders \342\206\222 Follows numbered step-by-step instructions one card/step at a time.\n4. **Practice & Private Video Submission**: Marks activity complete OR chooses to record in-browser / upload a short video clip (max 2 min / 50 MB) with optional reflection note \342\206\222 Sees clear inline privacy notice (*Private to you and your reviewer \302\267 Auto-deletes in 30 days \302\267 Delete anytime*) and confirms consent before upload.\n5. **Constructive Feedback Loop**: Views reviewer\'s **Caregiver Instruction-Match Score (%)**, step-by-step rubric breakdown (e.g., *Setup & Safety: Met*, *Calm Pacing: Met*, *Verbal Cueing: Partially Met*), warm strengths note, and one practical tip for next time \342\206\222 Can delete the uploaded video immediately while keeping the written coaching notes.\n\n#### B. Reviewer Journey\n1. **Structured Review Queue**: Signs into Reviewer Workbench \342\206\222 Sees prioritized queue filtered by status (`Queued`, `In Review`, `Completed`) and age band, ordered FIFO with clear wait-time timestamps.\n2. **Split-Screen Evaluation Workbench**: Claims a submission \342\206\222 Left pane renders the private, stream-only video player alongside the exact Activity Steps reference (showing only child\'s age band \342\200\224 zero parent contact PII); Right pane renders the activity\'s weighted **Caregiver Execution Rubric**.\n3. **Objective Scoring & Attestation**: Selects `Met`, `Partially Met`, or `Not Observed` per caregiver step \342\206\222 Percentage instruction-match score auto-calculates live with tabular numerals \342\206\222 Writes encouraging *What Went Well* + *Gentle Next-Time Tip* \342\206\222 Confirms mandatory non-diagnostic attestation (*\"This feedback evaluates caregiver instruction execution only, not the child\"*) \342\206\222 Submits review.\n\n#### C. Admin Journey\n1. **Curriculum Coverage Overview**: Views matrix of published activities across all **8 age groups \303\227 6 learning domains** to identify content gaps.\n2. **Curriculum & Rubric Authoring**: Creates/edits Activities (domain, age group, summary, household materials, safety notes, instructional media, ordered steps, and weighted rubric criteria summing to 100%) and assigns them into sequenced **Daily Plans**.\n3. **Operations & Privacy Governance**: Manages user roles (promoting/deactivating reviewers), monitors video queue volume, inspects automated 30-day retention sweep status, and reviews immutable media access audit logs.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Key Product Decisions, Role Governance & Child Video Security\n\n### Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) Matrix\n\n| Capability / Resource | Parent / Caregiver | Reviewer | Admin |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Manage own profile & children | Full (own family only) | None | Read (masked) |\n| Browse age-matched daily activities | Read (published) | Read (reference) | Full CRUD |\n| Log completions & upload videos | Full (own children) | None | None |\n| Stream caregiver activity videos | Own videos only | Assigned/claimed queue only | Restricted (audit-logged) |\n| Delete uploaded video immediately | Yes (own videos) | No | Moderation/retention purge |\n| Score rubrics & write feedback | Read own feedback | Create/submit on assigned | Read aggregate metrics |\n| Manage curriculum, plans & roles | No | No | Full CRUD |\n| View media access audit logs | Own deletion history | None | Full read-only audit |\n\n### Child Video Security & Privacy Architecture (DPDP Act 2023 & Global Readiness)\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> Children\'s videos are high-sensitivity personal data. Every video path must be private-by-default, non-enumerable, access-audited, and automatically expired.\n\n1. **Zero Public Exposure**: Uploaded videos are stored in a private media vault **outside** the Vite public/static bundle using random opaque UUID keys (never original filenames or sequential IDs).\n2. **Short-Lived Signed Streaming Tokens**: Playback requests require a valid authenticated session and an HMAC-SHA256 signed stream token (5-minute TTL) scoped to `actor_user_id + submission_id`. The Express streaming endpoint enforces RBAC, supports HTTP `Range` requests for smooth mobile seeking, and sends `Cache-Control: private, no-store`, `Content-Disposition: inline`, and `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`.\n3. **Strict Upload Hardening**: Server enforces MIME allowlist (`video/mp4`, `video/webm`, `video/quicktime`), binary magic-byte header validation, 50 MB file cap, and 120-second duration limit (friendly for Indian mobile bandwidth and safe against storage exhaustion).\n4. **30-Day Automatic Deletion + Instant Right-to-Delete**: Every submission sets `expires_at = created_at + 30 days`. A background retention worker periodically purges expired video files from disk and marks records `deleted` (`deletion_reason = \'retention_30d\'`). Parents can also tap **Delete Video** at any time for immediate physical deletion while optionally retaining their written feedback summary.\n5. **Reviewer Data Minimization**: Reviewers see only the child\'s age band (e.g., `6\342\200\2239 months`), activity guidelines, and the video stream \342\200\224 never parent email, phone number, address, or full legal identifiers.\n6. **Immutable Audit Trail & Auth Hardening**: Every upload, stream open, review submission, parent delete, and auto-purge writes an entry to `media_access_audit_logs`. Authentication uses Node native `crypto.scrypt` per-user salted password hashes, `HttpOnly` + `SameSite=Lax` signed session cookies, Zod input validation, parameterized SQL queries, and endpoint rate limiting.\n\n### Key Architectural Trade-Offs\n- **Local SQLite Behind a Repository Interface**:\n  - *Chosen Approach*: `better-sqlite3` (WAL mode + strict foreign keys enabled) wrapped in domain repository modules.\n  - *Why*: Zero external provisioning friction for rapid prototype validation, full relational integrity for rubrics and audit trails, and clean SQL portability to Cloud SQL PostgreSQL before public launch.\n- **Storage Adapter Abstraction for Media**:\n  - *Chosen Approach*: `MediaStorageAdapter` interface implemented with private local disk storage in the prototype.\n  - *Why*: Lets us prove the full upload \342\206\222 signed stream \342\206\222 30-day auto-purge lifecycle immediately while making production migration to GCS/S3 signed URLs a single adapter swap.\n- **Versioned REST API (`/api/v1`) from Day One**:\n  - *Chosen Approach*: Stateless JSON DTO contracts shared between React client and Express server.\n  - *Why*: Directly prepares LittleSteps for future Android and iOS native/cross-platform clients without duplicating business logic or RBAC rules.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Technical Architecture, Data Model & Phased Milestones *(Technical Reference)*\n\n### System & Modular Architecture Diagram\n\n```text\n\342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n\342\224\202  CLIENT APPLICATION (React 19 \302\267 TypeScript \302\267 Tailwind v4 \302\267 i18n Catalog)   \342\224\202\n\342\224\202                                                                            \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220  \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220  \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220  \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  \342\224\202  Parent Journey  \342\224\202  \342\224\202 Reviewer Workbench \342\224\202  \342\224\202   Admin Curriculum     \342\224\202  \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  \342\224\202  \302\267 Onboarding    \342\224\202  \342\224\202 \302\267 Queue & Filters  \342\224\202  \342\224\202   \302\267 8x6 Coverage Grid  \342\224\202  \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  \342\224\202  \302\267 Today\'s Plan  \342\224\202  \342\224\202 \302\267 Split Video View \342\224\202  \342\224\202   \302\267 Activity & Rubric  \342\224\202  \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  \342\224\202  \302\267 Activity Mode \342\224\202  \342\224\202 \302\267 Weighted Rubric  \342\224\202  \342\224\202   \302\267 Daily Plan Builder \342\224\202  \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  \342\224\202  \302\267 Video Capture \342\224\202  \342\224\202 \302\267 Non-Diag Attest  \342\224\202  \342\224\202   \302\267 Roles & Audit Logs \342\224\202  \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230  \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230  \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230  \342\224\202\n\342\224\202           \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\274\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230               \342\224\202\n\342\224\202                                  \342\226\274                                         \342\224\202\n\342\224\202                   Typed API Client & Auth Session Store                    \342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n                                   \342\224\202 HTTPS / JSON + Range Video Stream\n                                   \342\226\274\n\342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n\342\224\202  EXPRESS API SERVER (/api/v1 \302\267 Port 3000 \302\267 Single Origin with Vite SPA)    \342\224\202\n\342\224\202                                                                            \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200 Middleware \342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220  \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  \342\224\202 Auth Session Verification \302\267 RBAC Guards \302\267 Zod Validation \302\267 RateLimit \342\224\202  \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230  \342\224\202\n\342\224\202                                  \342\226\274                                         \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200 Domain Services \342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220  \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  \342\224\202 Identity \342\224\202 Child & AgeBand \342\224\202 Curriculum \342\224\202 Submissions \342\224\202 RubricEngine \342\224\202  \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  \342\224\202 AuditLog \342\224\202 RetentionWorker (30-day auto-purge scheduler)             \342\224\202  \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230  \342\224\202\n\342\224\202                  \342\226\274                                   \342\226\274                     \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220       \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220  \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  \342\224\202   Repository Layer (DAL)  \342\224\202       \342\224\202      MediaStorageAdapter         \342\224\202  \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  \342\224\202   SQLite (WAL + FK ON)    \342\224\202       \342\224\202  Private Vault (outside public/) \342\224\202  \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  \342\224\202   \342\206\222 Portable to Postgres  \342\224\202       \342\224\202  HMAC Short-Lived Stream Tokens  \342\224\202  \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230  \342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n```\n\n### Logical Workspace & Module Organization\nTo keep the codebase modular, strictly typed, and easy to extend toward mobile and multi-language support, code is separated into five clear boundaries:\n1. **Shared Domain Contracts & i18n**: Shared TypeScript interfaces, Zod schemas, age-band/domain constants, rubric score calculator, and locale dictionaries (`en` baseline, ready for `hi` and additional languages).\n2. **Design System Primitives**: Reusable Warm Montessori Editorial layout primitives (Top Bar, Section Header, Empty/Loading/Error states, Accessible Stepper, Secure Video Player, Rubric Checklist).\n3. **Role-Isolated Frontend Feature Modules**: Independent feature domains for Authentication/Onboarding, Parent Daily Journey & Progress, Reviewer Evaluation Workbench, and Admin Curriculum & Audit Console.\n4. **Express API & Domain Services**: Route controllers grouped by module (`/auth`, `/children`, `/curriculum`, `/journey`, `/submissions`, `/reviews`, `/admin`), RBAC middleware, pure business services, and the 30-day retention scheduler.\n5. **Data Persistence & Private Media Vault**: SQLite schema migrations, deterministic curriculum seeders (all 8 age groups, 6 domains, sample daily plans, steps, and rubrics), Repository implementations, and an isolated private media storage directory excluded from version control and static hosting.\n\n### Database Entities & Relational Model\n\n```text\nusers (parent|reviewer|admin) \342\224\200\342\224\2001:N\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 user_consents\n  \342\224\202\n  \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\2001:N\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 children \342\224\200\342\224\200N:1\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 age_groups (8 bands: 0\342\200\2233m ... 21\342\200\22324m)\n  \342\224\202            \342\224\202                   \342\224\202\n  \342\224\202            \342\224\202                   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\2001:N\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 daily_plans \342\224\200\342\224\2001:N\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 daily_plan_items\n  \342\224\202            \342\224\202                   \342\224\202                                   \342\224\202\n  \342\224\202            \342\224\202                   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\2001:N\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 activities \342\227\204\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n  \342\224\202            \342\224\202                                \342\224\202  \342\224\202  \342\224\202\n  \342\224\202            \342\224\202                                \342\224\202  \342\224\202  \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200N:1\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 learning_domains (6 domains)\n  \342\224\202            \342\224\202                                \342\224\202  \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\2001:N\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 activity_steps\n  \342\224\202            \342\224\202                                \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\2001:N\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 activity_rubric_criteria\n  \342\224\202            \342\224\202\n  \342\224\202            \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\2001:N\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 activity_completions (child \303\227 activity \303\227 plan_date)\n  \342\224\202                             \342\224\202\n  \342\224\202                             \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\2000:N\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 video_submissions (storage_key, expires_at +30d, status)\n  \342\224\202                                          \342\224\202       \342\224\202\n  \342\224\202                                          \342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\2001:N\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 media_access_audit_logs\n  \342\224\202                                          \342\224\202\n  \342\224\202                                          \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\2000:1\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 submission_reviews (instruction_match_score_pct)\n  \342\224\202                                                        \342\224\202\n  \342\224\202                                                        \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\2001:N\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\226\272 review_rubric_scores\n  \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\2001:N (as reviewer)\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n```\n\n#### Core Entity Highlights\n- **`users` & `user_consents`**: Role-typed accounts (`parent`, `reviewer`, `admin`), locale preference, and timestamped privacy/video consent records.\n- **`age_groups` & `learning_domains`**: Seeded reference tables for all 8 age bands (`min_months`, `max_months`) and 6 developmental domains with translation-key hooks.\n- **`children`**: Linked to `parent_user_id`, storing `display_name`, `date_of_birth`, and computed active age band.\n- **`activities`, `activity_steps`, `activity_rubric_criteria`**: Structured activity definition including household materials, safety notes, instructional media, ordered caregiver steps, and weighted observable rubric items (strictly scoped to caregiver technique).\n- **`daily_plans` & `daily_plan_items`**: Curated day-by-day sequences per age group (2\342\200\2233 focused activities/day across rotating domains) preventing caregiver overwhelm.\n- **`activity_completions` & `video_submissions`**: Tracks completion progress, optional caregiver reflections, opaque private media storage keys, review queue assignment, and automatic `expires_at` (30-day retention) + `deleted_at` / `deletion_reason`.\n- **`submission_reviews` & `review_rubric_scores`**: Stores criterion-level ratings (`met` = 100%, `partially_met` = 50%, `not_observed` = 0%), weighted **Caregiver Instruction-Match Score (%)**, strengths note, next-time coaching tip, and reviewer non-diagnostic attestation timestamp.\n- **`media_access_audit_logs`**: Immutable ledger of every video upload, playback stream, review access, parent deletion, and automated 30-day purge.\n\n### Interactive Component & State Mapping\n- **Auth & Role Routing**: Session hydration checks `/api/v1/auth/me` on boot and routes users strictly to their permitted workspace (Parent, Reviewer, or Admin) with graceful unauthorized fallback.\n- **Child Age-Band Calculation**: Creating or editing a baby\'s DOB immediately recalculates age in months on both client preview and server validation, updating Today\'s Journey dynamically.\n- **Activity Stepper & Submission Flow**: Interactive step completion toggles persist locally during practice; submitting a video validates MIME/size/duration client-side before multipart upload, shows real progress, enforces consent checkbox, and transitions card status cleanly to `Submitted for Review`.\n- **Reviewer Rubric Engine**: Toggling any rubric criterion (`Met` / `Partially Met` / `Not Observed`) recalculates the weighted caregiver instruction-match percentage live; submission stays disabled until all criteria are rated, coaching notes are entered, and the non-diagnostic attestation checkbox is checked.\n- **Retention & Instant Delete**: Clicking `Delete Video` opens an inline confirmation (never `window.confirm`), calls `DELETE /api/v1/submissions/:id/video`, immediately unlinks the file, refreshes the UI state to `Video Deleted (Feedback Preserved)`, and records the audit entry.\n\n---\n\n### Phased, Independently Testable Implementation Milestones\n\n| Milestone | Scope & Deliverables | Independent Verification Criteria |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Milestone 1 (Step 1): Core Foundation, DB, Auth & Editorial Shell** | Express + Vite unified server on port 3000; strict TypeScript; SQLite schema, migrations, Repository layer & seed data (8 age groups, 6 domains, realistic starter curriculum + demo accounts for Parent, Reviewer, Admin); Auth + RBAC middleware; i18n dictionary setup; Warm Calm Montessori Editorial design tokens & shell. | Register/login works for all 3 roles; RBAC blocks cross-role API calls (`403`); seeded age groups and domains load from SQLite; responsive editorial layout passes type-check and build. |\n| **Milestone 2 (Step 2): Parent Onboarding, Child Profiles & Today\'s Daily Journey** | Add/switch child profile with auto age-band calculation; Today\'s Journey calm daily view (2\342\200\2233 focused activities); Activity Detail experience with instructional video player, materials, safety notes, step-by-step guide, and completion logging; gentle domain-balance progress summary. | Adding a baby with any DOB (0\342\200\22324m) maps to the exact 3-month band; caregiver can complete daily activities, add notes, and see persisted progress across reloads. |\n| **Milestone 3 (Step 3): Private Video Submission & 30-Day Media Vault** | In-browser camera recording (`MediaRecorder`) + file upload with consent capture; server-side MIME/magic-byte/size validation; private non-public storage vault; short-lived HMAC-signed `Range` video streaming; instant parent delete; scheduled 30-day auto-purge worker + audit logging. | Uploaded video streams only with valid signed token and authorized role; direct unauthenticated access returns `401/403`; parent delete physically removes file; retention sweep removes expired videos and logs audit rows. |\n| **Milestone 4 (Step 4): Reviewer Workbench & Caregiver Rubric Scoring** | Reviewer Queue with age-band & status filters and claim workflow; split-screen secure video + activity reference + weighted rubric checklist; live caregiver instruction-match % calculator; non-diagnostic attestation; Parent Feedback Detail view. | Reviewer claims submission without seeing parent PII, scores rubric, verifies weighted % math, submits feedback; parent immediately views score, rubric breakdown, and coaching tip. |\n| **Milestone 5 (Step 5): Admin Curriculum CMS, Audit Console & Hardening** | Admin 8\303\2276 curriculum coverage matrix; full Activity, Step, Rubric, and Daily Plan editor; Reviewer account management; Media Access Audit Log & Retention monitor; accessibility, mobile touch-target, and end-to-end verification across all 3 roles. | Admin creates a new activity + weighted rubric + daily plan item and it immediately appears in matching parents\' daily journey; audit log accurately tracks uploads, streams, and deletions; full lint & production build pass cleanly. |\n"
