            lines {
              text: "### Logical Workspace & Module Organization"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "To keep the codebase modular, strictly typed, and easy to extend toward mobile and multi-language support, code is separated into five clear boundaries:"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "1. **Shared Domain Contracts & i18n**: Shared TypeScript interfaces, Zod schemas, age-band/domain constants, rubric score calculator, and locale dictionaries (`en` baseline, ready for `hi` and additional languages)."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "2. **Design System Primitives**: Reusable Warm Montessori Editorial layout primitives (Top Bar, Section Header, Empty/Loading/Error states, Accessible Stepper, Secure Video Player, Rubric Checklist)."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "3. **Role-Isolated Frontend Feature Modules**: Independent feature domains for Authentication/Onboarding, Parent Daily Journey & Progress, Reviewer Evaluation Workbench, and Admin Curriculum & Audit Console."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "4. **Express API & Domain Services**: Route controllers grouped by module (`/auth`, `/children`, `/curriculum`, `/journey`, `/submissions`, `/reviews`, `/admin`), RBAC middleware, pure business services, and the 30-day retention scheduler."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "5. **Data Persistence & Private Media Vault**: SQLite schema migrations, deterministic curriculum seeders (all 8 age groups, 6 domains, sample daily plans, steps, and rubrics), Repository implementations, and an isolated private media storage directory excluded from version control and static hosting."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "### Database Entities & Relational Model"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
