  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Confirming Next Steps**\n\nI\'m moving forward with the implementation! The green light is on the plan. Right now, I\'m focusing on synthesizing the key requirements. This includes using a local SQLite database with Express, employing `better-sqlite3`, and building a clean Repository Layer. Additionally, I\'m integrating private video access using short-lived HMAC-signed streaming tokens.\n\n\n**Defining Project Scope**\n\nI\'ve got the project scope solidified! I\'m now integrating instant parent deletion and 30-day automatic deletion. I\'m also ensuring the application is English-first with an i18n-ready architecture. The editorial design direction is also set, using the Warm Calm Montessori style. The `implementation_plan.md` has been approved, and I\'m pursuing a full implementation across all five milestones for a seamless LittleSteps application. I\'m working from the planning-mode spec to ensure that every task is fully implemented.\n\n\n**Clarifying Application Features**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the LittleSteps platform\'s core features. It will support eight age groups across six learning domains with daily structured learning. The app will include instructional videos and guidance, plus caregiver video upload and reviewer feedback. I\'m focusing on user roles (Parent, Reviewer, Admin), proper auth, RBAC, and video security. I also aim to maintain a clean architecture, with modularity, strict TypeScript, a retention worker, and an audit trail. Lastly, I will be checking frontend design rules.\n\n\n**Creating Visuals Now**\n\nI\'m now generating visual assets! I\'m planning a batch run of four images using `generate_image`. Specifically, I\'m focusing on creating cohesive, Warm Calm Montessori Editorial photographs in a single parallel batch. The plan is to create timestamped paths, which will flow through two phases to optimize generation. I\'ve got detailed descriptions for each image, including aspect ratios, and the photographic style.\n\n\n**Generating More Images**\n\nI\'m now generating more visual assets. I\'m focusing on creating two more images. The first is a natural daylight editorial photograph of a safe low wooden Montessori floor mirror. The second is a warm sunlit tabletop Montessori editorial still life showing a baby-safe stainless steel open cup. I\'m also preparing for a single batched `install_applet_package` call.\n\nI\'ll be installing `better-sqlite3`, `@types/better-sqlite3`, `multer`, `@types/multer`, `cookie-parser`, `@types/cookie-parser`, and `zod`. Furthermore, I\'ve confirmed I can use Node\'s built-in `crypto` for password hashing, signed tokens and UUIDs, as well as use clean custom SVG/Tailwind bars for charts and visuals, which is perfect!\n\n\n**Integrating Design Decisions**\n\nI\'m now integrating design decisions, and I\'ve confirmed some key details. I\'ll be using `tabular-nums` for charting to avoid bloated dependencies. I\'m also loading Google Fonts, specifically `Fraunces`, `Plus Jakarta Sans`, and `IBM Plex Mono`, directly in `index.html`. Furthermore, I\'ve confirmed that I can run `install_applet_package` and my batch of four `generate_image` calls in parallel, which keeps the workflow extremely clean! I will also update `metadata.json` and `index`.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "anEAa9LuEJD8nsEPiueBqQk"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_13718355001594044215"
