  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Visuals: Montessori**\n\nI\'m captivated by those four generated Montessori images. The sunlit chalk plaster, dhurrie, wooden spoon, steel katori, muslin scarf, floor mirror, and open steel cup create such an authentic Indian Montessori feel. I\'ve noted their exact URL paths and will reference them.\n\n\n**Planning Modular Architecture**\n\nI\'m now deep in planning the modular architecture for LittleSteps. I\'ve updated the project configuration, including metadata.json with the name, description, and permission requests. I\'ve confirmed that the parent component can record a video in-browser using `MediaRecorder`, meaning adding \"camera\" and \"microphone\" to `requestFramePermissions` in `metadata.json` is a good decision, to allow iframe seamless camera/mic recording! I\'m also syncing the title and OG meta tags in index.html, and loading Google Fonts. The next step is detailed component breakdown.\n\n\n**Refining Package Configuration**\n\nI\'m currently updating the project\'s configuration files, aiming for optimal structure. I\'ve configured the package.json scripts for development and production, opting for `tsx server.ts` for dev and `node server.ts` for start, as suggested. I\'ve also implemented strict TypeScript rules with `\"strict\": true` in tsconfig.json, and added crucial `.gitignore` entries to exclude local databases and private media. I\'ve also added placeholders for necessary secrets in the `.env.example` file, and I\'m updating Tailwind CSS.\n\n\n**Defining Design System Elements**\n\nI\'m now establishing the design system\'s core elements. I\'ve selected typefaces (`IBM Plex Mono`), color palette (Warm Chalk, Crisp Linen, etc.), and typography defaults. Also, I\'ve incorporated `tabular-nums`, focus-visible rings, and `prefers-reduced-motion` handling. The goal is a cohesive, accessible visual language.\n\n**Outlining Shared Contracts**\n\nI\'m structuring the shared domain contracts within `/src/shared/*`. I\'ve defined strict TypeScript interfaces in `/src/shared/types.ts` for entities like `UserRole`, `Activity`, `VideoSubmission`, and DTOs. `/src/shared/domain.ts` includes age calculations, canonical age groups/domains, and a weighted instruction match score calculator.\n\n\n**Constructing i18n & DB Layers**\n\nI\'m making progress building the backend. I\'ve designed a clean i18n-ready dictionary in `/src/shared/i18n.ts` for easy language additions. I\'ve also established the SQLite database connection, enabling WAL and foreign keys in `/server/db/connection.ts`. I\'ve created a relational schema in `/server/db/schema.ts` with all 15 tables.\n\n\n**Populating Initial Database**\n\nI\'m now populating the seed database file `/server/db/seed.ts`. I\'m focused on creating a deterministic, idempotent seed that runs only if the tables are empty, and it includes all eight age groups and six learning domains. I\'m adding realistic, culturally sensitive, India-friendly activities across all ages, with detailed steps and safety notes. Each activity leverages common household items and offers four caregiver steps alongside weighted execution instructions, with significant depth in the most crucial age ranges.\n\n\n**Finalizing Database & Demo**\n\nI\'ve finalized the database with a 100-point rubric focusing on caregiver setup, pacing, cueing, and responsive pauses. I\'m linking the editorial poster image URLs to our generated Montessori images and curating `daily_plans` & `daily_plan_items`. I\'ve set up ready-to-test demo accounts: Parent (`meera@littlesteps.in`), Reviewer (`ananya.reviewer@littlesteps.in`), and Admin (`kavita.admin@littlesteps.in`). I\'ve also added a sample video submission.\n\n\n**Refining Video File Handling**\n\nI\'m now refining the video file handling logic for parent uploads and demo submissions. I\'ve ensured that real videos written to `./private_media/` are handled with clean streaming and deletion. I\'m focusing on providing consistent playback. I\'m choosing to mark seeded submissions as \"deleted\" if a real file doesn\'t exist. This will enable us to render a visual storyboard OR generate a tiny WebM on seed.\n\n\n**Improving Video Management**\n\nI\'m presently focused on enhanced video file management. I\'ve set `deletion_reason = \'parent_deleted\'` to demonstrate the privacy feature: \"Video deleted by caregiver \302\267 Written coaching feedback preserved\". To fully test the reviewer queue, I\'m integrating a \"Record or Upload Practice Video\" button on \"Today\'s Journey,\" ensuring real binary private storage and HTTP Range streaming. I\'m also considering the edge case of Reviewer login before Parent upload, and plan to handle this by allowing Reviewers to review uploaded clips or even a tiny base64 MP4. I\'m also planning an Instructional Visual Step Walkthrough player.\n\n\n**Enhancing Video Uploads**\n\nI\'m now integrating robust video handling. I\'m ensuring real camera recording and file uploads are functional across devices, along with a canvas-based sample clip generator for devices without webcams. This will create genuine `.webm` files. All three methods will use the same backend for multipart upload, magic-byte validation, secure storage, and streaming proxy.\n\n\n**Securing Data: Robust Crypto**\n\nI\'ve just added robust security measures. I\'ve implemented password hashing and session token management using Node.js\'s `crypto` module. Additionally, I\'ve integrated video stream token generation and validation with a strict TTL. I\'m verifying magic bytes for all video uploads and using a local media storage adapter for secure file handling, strictly within `./private_media/`.\n\n\n\n**Refining Data Access Layers**\n\nI\'m currently structuring the data access layers to promote maintainability. I\'m focusing on clean, parameterized SQLite queries, isolating them from Express routes within `journeyRepository.ts`, `submissionRepository.ts`, and `auditRepository.ts`. This design will allow a straightforward transition to PostgreSQL. I\'ve also implemented a periodic retention sweep in `/server/services/retentionWorker.ts` to manage video submissions, including media file deletion via `MediaStorageAdapter`, database updates, and audit logging. I\'ve also incorporated authentication middleware in `/server/middleware/auth.ts`, along with rate limiting. Lastly, versioned API routes (`/api/v1`) are being developed for authentication and user/child management.\n\n\n**Defining API Endpoints**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the API endpoints and have listed the routes, including those for curriculum meta, activities, and today/history journeys, alongside completions and submissions. I\'ve detailed the POST endpoints for submissions, with multipart uploads, Zod validation, and security measures like magic-byte checks and expiry. Secure video streaming with token generation, HTTP Range streaming, and the ability for parent instant deletes and Admin purges are also outlined. Furthermore, reviewer queue and review endpoints are included.\n\n\n**Constructing Admin Interface**\n\nI\'m now in the process of building the admin interface, with defined routes for a curriculum coverage matrix, the reviewer queue metrics, and the retention status. I\'m also planning administrative control over activities, daily plans, users, and audit logs, including a route to manually trigger the retention sweep. On the backend, I\'m setting up a unified Express server on port 3000, configuring SQLite, migrations, the seed process, and the retention worker.\n\n\n\n**Designing Interface Components**\n\nI\'m presently building out crucial interface components. I\'ve focused on `/src/components/EditorialImage.tsx`, ensuring resilient image handling with a zero-broken-image policy, and descriptive `alt` attributes. I\'ve also built `/src/components/InstructionalGuidePlayer.tsx` for a calm, interactive walkthrough experience with Montessori visuals. Furthermore, I\'ve designed `/src/components/SecureVideoPlayer.tsx` for private video streaming with secure token handling and clear privacy indicators. I\'m also planning the `/src/pages/LandingAuthView.tsx` with a serene design.\n\n\n**Implementing User Flows**\n\nI\'m now integrating critical user flows, specifically focusing on `/src/pages/RegisterView.tsx` with a one-click role selector for instant demo access. In `/src/pages/ParentJourneyView.tsx`, I\'ve created a gentle onboarding form if no child exists. I\'ve also incorporated a child switcher with age metadata. I\'m focusing on \"Today\'s Journey,\" designing bite-sized activity cards with clear completion status and the core \"Record or Upload Practice Video\" flow.\n\n\n**Implementing Review Workflow**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the Reviewer Workflow. I\'ve designed a detailed review feedback view, displaying the Caregiver Instruction-Match Score with explicit reminders about the evaluation focus. I\'m adding a rubric breakdown, strengths, coaching tips, and a \"Delete Video Now\" feature that preserves coaching notes. Also, I\'m making progress on the Reviewer Workbench view.\n\n\n\n**Designing Review Features**\n\nI\'m now building out key review features. I\'m focusing on segmented buttons for caregiver execution rubric, a live auto-calculated caregiver instruction-match score, *What Went Well* and gentle next-time coaching tips, and a mandatory attestation checkbox for review submission. I\'m also starting the Admin Console view.\n\nI am now designing and adding the Admin Console view with the following tabs: curriculum matrix, daily plans, users and roles, and privacy & retention audits. I\'m now making progress on the create/edit activity modal/form.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "o3EAa-qtI5D8nsEPiueBqQk"
