  planner_response {
    response: "**LittleSteps** has been built and verified end-to-end across all five milestones of your approved plan.\n\n### What Was Built\n\n- **Backend, SQLite Persistence & Strict RBAC**\n  - Unified Express API (`/api/v1`) and Vite frontend running together on port `3000` with strict TypeScript enabled.\n  - Normalized relational SQLite schema (WAL mode, foreign keys enforced) isolated behind a Repository Layer for straightforward future migration to PostgreSQL and mobile API clients.\n  - Real authentication (`crypto.scrypt` salted password hashes, `HttpOnly` signed session cookies) and server-side RBAC isolating **Parent**, **Reviewer**, and **Admin** routes.\n  - Seeded starter curriculum covering all **8 age groups** (`0\342\200\2233m` through `21\342\200\22324m`), all **6 developmental domains**, India-friendly household activities, numbered steps, weighted caregiver rubrics, and daily plans.\n\n- **Parent Daily Journey & Activity Studio**\n  - Gentle child onboarding and multi-child support that automatically computes age in months and maps each baby to their 3-month age band.\n  - Calm **Today\342\200\231s Journey** view surfacing 2\342\200\2233 age-appropriate activities per day without visual clutter, paired with a step-paced **Guided Demonstration Player**, everyday household materials, safety reminders, checkable step progression, and private reflection logging.\n  - Non-judgmental **6-Domain Progress** overview and dedicated **Feedback** tab displaying reviewer scores, rubric breakdowns, and coaching tips.\n\n- **Private Children\342\200\231s Video Vault & 30-Day Retention**\n  - Supports in-browser camera recording, file upload (`MP4`, `WebM`, `MOV` up to 50 MB / 2 min), and a 3-second test-clip recorder for devices without a webcam, gated by explicit privacy consent.\n  - Validates binary video magic bytes server-side, stores files outside public static directories using random UUID keys, and streams exclusively through 5-minute HMAC-signed `Range` tokens (`Cache-Control: private, no-store`).\n  - Automatic 30-day retention purge worker plus instant parent **Delete Video Now** (physically removing the video while preserving written feedback), with every upload, stream, and deletion logged in the audit trail.\n\n- **Reviewer Workbench & Caregiver-Only Rubric Scoring**\n  - PII-minimized review queue (showing age band and activity details without parent contact info) with status and age-group filters.\n  - Split-screen workbench pairing the private non-downloadable stream and activity guidelines with weighted caregiver-execution rubric criteria (`Met`, `Partially Met`, `Not Observed`), live **Instruction-Match Score (%)** calculation, warm coaching notes, and mandatory non-diagnostic attestation confirming only caregiver execution is evaluated.\n\n- **Admin Curriculum CMS & Privacy Governance**\n  - Interactive **8 \303\227 6 Curriculum Coverage Matrix**, full Activity/Step/Rubric editor (enforcing 100-point rubric totals), **Daily Plan Sequencer**, user role management, manual **30-Day Retention Sweep** trigger, and live **Media Access Audit Log**.\n\n### Seeded Accounts for Testing\nYou can create a new parent account or use the one-click role buttons on the sign-in screen (password for all seeded accounts: `LittleSteps123!`):\n- **Parent**: `meera@littlesteps.in` (Baby Aarav, 6\342\200\2239 months stage)\n- **Reviewer**: `ananya.reviewer@littlesteps.in`\n- **Admin**: `kavita.admin@littlesteps.in`"
    message_id: "OncAa9D7Oq6Q3boPr5-XmQc"
    modified_response: "**LittleSteps** has been built and verified end-to-end across all five milestones of your approved plan.\n\n### What Was Built\n\n- **Backend, SQLite Persistence & Strict RBAC**\n  - Unified Express API (`/api/v1`) and Vite frontend running together on port `3000` with strict TypeScript enabled.\n  - Normalized relational SQLite schema (WAL mode, foreign keys enforced) isolated behind a Repository Layer for straightforward future migration to PostgreSQL and mobile API clients.\n  - Real authentication (`crypto.scrypt` salted password hashes, `HttpOnly` signed session cookies) and server-side RBAC isolating **Parent**, **Reviewer**, and **Admin** routes.\n  - Seeded starter curriculum covering all **8 age groups** (`0\342\200\2233m` through `21\342\200\22324m`), all **6 developmental domains**, India-friendly household activities, numbered steps, weighted caregiver rubrics, and daily plans.\n\n- **Parent Daily Journey & Activity Studio**\n  - Gentle child onboarding and multi-child support that automatically computes age in months and maps each baby to their 3-month age band.\n  - Calm **Today\342\200\231s Journey** view surfacing 2\342\200\2233 age-appropriate activities per day without visual clutter, paired with a step-paced **Guided Demonstration Player**, everyday household materials, safety reminders, checkable step progression, and private reflection logging.\n  - Non-judgmental **6-Domain Progress** overview and dedicated **Feedback** tab displaying reviewer scores, rubric breakdowns, and coaching tips.\n\n- **Private Children\342\200\231s Video Vault & 30-Day Retention**\n  - Supports in-browser camera recording, file upload (`MP4`, `WebM`, `MOV` up to 50 MB / 2 min), and a 3-second test-clip recorder for devices without a webcam, gated by explicit privacy consent.\n  - Validates binary video magic bytes server-side, stores files outside public static directories using random UUID keys, and streams exclusively through 5-minute HMAC-signed `Range` tokens (`Cache-Control: private, no-store`).\n  - Automatic 30-day retention purge worker plus instant parent **Delete Video Now** (physically removing the video while preserving written feedback), with every upload, stream, and deletion logged in the audit trail.\n\n- **Reviewer Workbench & Caregiver-Only Rubric Scoring**\n  - PII-minimized review queue (showing age band and activity details without parent contact info) with status and age-group filters.\n  - Split-screen workbench pairing the private non-downloadable stream and activity guidelines with weighted caregiver-execution rubric criteria (`Met`, `Partially Met`, `Not Observed`), live **Instruction-Match Score (%)** calculation, warm coaching notes, and mandatory non-diagnostic attestation confirming only caregiver execution is evaluated.\n\n- **Admin Curriculum CMS & Privacy Governance**\n  - Interactive **8 \303\227 6 Curriculum Coverage Matrix**, full Activity/Step/Rubric editor (enforcing 100-point rubric totals), **Daily Plan Sequencer**, user role management, manual **30-Day Retention Sweep** trigger, and live **Media Access Audit Log**.\n\n### Seeded Accounts for Testing\nYou can create a new parent account or use the one-click role buttons on the sign-in screen (password for all seeded accounts: `LittleSteps123!`):\n- **Parent**: `meera@littlesteps.in` (Baby Aarav, 6\342\200\2239 months stage)\n- **Reviewer**: `ananya.reviewer@littlesteps.in`\n- **Admin**: `kavita.admin@littlesteps.in`"
