  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Website Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently meticulously examining the requirements for the LittleSteps public website, particularly focusing on STEP 2. I\'m taking the task very seriously. I\'m reviewing the nine required public pages, ensuring the client-side URL/route navigation, scroll-to-top functionality, and working links are all in place. I have completed the requirements for the homepage, and started looking at the next page, which is the About LittleSteps page.\n\n\n**Analyzing New Pages**\n\nI\'ve moved on to analyzing new pages. I\'m deep diving into the \"How It Works\" and \"Our Approach\" sections next. I\'m focusing on the functionality of the pages and trying to create a list of requirements to complete each page. I am specifically reviewing the Contact Us page, which will need a validated form and backend endpoint. I\'ll need to persist the inquiries in SQLite and provide a toast confirmation. I am also planning the Privacy Policy and Terms and Conditions pages and I\'ll carefully consider the legal and safety aspects and ensure the messaging is very clear.\n\n\n**Adding Login & Registration**\n\nI\'m now integrating login and registration features. I\'m focusing on the `/auth/login` page, including those quick-login options for demo accounts. I\'m also implementing the `/register` page using the Step 1 Design System components and connecting it to the backend. Plus, I\'ll include that quiet link in the footer to the `/design-system`.\n\n\n\n**Defining \"How It Works\"**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the \"How It Works\" section, outlining the core steps with visuals. I\'ve broken it down into three concise, numbered steps, each with accompanying icons: Choose Age, Follow Daily Activities, and Learn/Track. I\'m also planning a clean link to a detailed `/how-it-works` walkthrough. The development areas will be represented using six calm cards, built with our Step 1 Card component. They\'ll represent key domains, with subtle accent colors.\n\n\n**Designing Activity Previews**\n\nI\'m now designing engaging activity previews for different age groups, focusing on the landing page\'s interactive experience using the `AgeGroupSelector`. I\'m also preparing an interactive activity showcase with a video player and materials, and explaining the activity showcase including progress indicators in a non-judgmental way. I\'m focusing on the *Household Texture Basket* activity example, which will utilize our `VideoPlayer` and `ActivityCard`.\n\n\n**Refining Page Details**\n\nI\'m now refining crucial page elements. I\'m prioritizing age appropriateness, safety reminders, and ensuring private videos auto-delete after 30 days. Caregiver instruction-match feedback will be included. I\'m focusing on the integrity rule, promising zero fake testimonials, statistics, or endorsements. Also, LittleSteps will not make health or developmental claims. Lastly, I\'m working on the final CTA, and have incorporated a quiet footer.\n\n\n**Confirming Consistent Visuals**\n\nI\'m verifying the visual consistency across the pages. My focus is on ensuring a cohesive aesthetic. I\'ve considered adding an image of a mother and baby, but the existing photographs provide excellent consistency. The four existing images ensure visual cohesion, which is excellent. I\'m prioritizing using those consistent images across the nine pages, avoiding any potential aesthetic mismatch.\n\n\n**Implementing Client Router**\n\nI\'m now implementing a zero-dependency client router helper, `/src/lib/router.ts`, with full URL support and browser back/forward functionality. I\'m also ensuring automatic scroll-to-top on route changes. I\'ve verified the Top Bar Contract on the public website, including the three zones and concise nav links for both desktop and mobile views.\n\n\n**Adding Contact Form Persistence**\n\nI\'m now adding persistence to the contact form. I\'m focusing on creating a lightweight `contact_inquiries` table in SQLite, along with a `POST /api/v1/contact` endpoint featuring Zod validation for genuine message persistence. I\'m also ensuring a real confirmation reference is returned. I\'m structuring these edits into two batches: updating server files for persistence and establishing client-side routing, and creating a public website layout component.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "sn4Aa8KVF7SE28oPqfLZ6A8"
    tool_calls {
