  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Skill Relevance**\n\nI\'ve been analyzing the relevance of specific skills for authentication and parent onboarding implementation. I\'ve already reviewed the `frontend-design` skill documentation, specifically `SKILL.md` and related references, which seems pertinent.\n\n\n**Reviewing Design Requirements**\n\nI\'m focused on the design requirements for the authentication pages, ensuring full WCAG 2.2 AA compliance and clean integration of Design System components. I\'ve pinpointed that the \"firebase-integration-rpc\" and \"cloudsql-setup\" skills aren\'t relevant to this step. I have begun reviewing every single requirement of Step 3, with a sharp focus on authentication and component usage.\n\n\n**Implementing Authentication Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing the authentication logic, starting with email verification. I\'m focusing on security, using SHA-256 for hashed token storage in SQLite, with appropriate expiry times for both verification and reset tokens. I am working on the `/login` endpoint, including validation and \"Forgot password?\" functionality. The forgot password flow is designed for security and includes a prototype mail preview link for testing.\n\n\n**Finalizing Endpoint Security**\n\nI\'m finalizing the security for the `/reset-password`, `/verify-email`, and `/logout` endpoints. I\'ve designed the `/reset-password` endpoint to verify the token hash, check its expiry and unused state, validate the new password, and update the salted password hash. It also revokes prior sessions. For `/verify-email`, I\'ve created the `POST` endpoints and marked the `users.email_verified_at` field. Finally, the `/logout` functionality will clear cookies and invalidate sessions by incrementing the `session_version` field.\n\n\n**Upgrading SQLite Schema**\n\nI\'m now focused on the SQLite schema upgrades to support Step 3. I\'m adding `email_verified_at`, `profile_photo_url`, `preferred_activity_time`, `notification_preference`, and `onboarding_completed_at` to the `users` table, using safe `ALTER TABLE` checks to ensure data integrity during upgrades. Also, I\'ll be implementing `session_version` bumping on password reset to invalidate all devices. Logout now clears cookies and redirects.\n\n\n**Defining Database Schemas**\n\nI\'m expanding the SQLite schema based on parent and child data requirements, focusing on onboarding and authentication. For the `users` table, I\'m defining `onboarding_completed_at` to control the onboarding flow, and a `session_version` for session invalidation on password reset. For the `children` table, I am including `profile_photo_url` and `activity_preferences`. I am also adding a new `auth_tokens` table for secure token management, including types, hashes, expiry, and short codes.\n\n\n**Implementing Profile Uploads**\n\nI\'m now working on the profile photo upload endpoint. I have implemented authentication and rate limiting, including validation of image MIME types (`image/jpeg`, `image/png`, `image/webp`) and magic bytes to confirm file integrity. The images are stored securely in a private media vault with unique UUID keys and served via an authenticated endpoint. I\'ve ensured parents can only access their own or their children\'s profile photos by verifying `user_id` ownership.\n\n\n\n**Designing Onboarding Stepper**\n\nI\'m now designing the onboarding stepper for new parents with a focus on a clear and accessible user experience. The process uses a 6-step stepper design, with inline validation and optional fields clearly marked for parents. The implementation will include accessible design system components and mobile-friendly input controls.\n\n\n**Defining Onboarding Details**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining onboarding details to match calm daily activities to baby\'s age and rhythm. I\'m prioritizing clarity and user experience on key screens. On Screen 1, if email verification is pending, I\'ll provide a clear reminder with a one-click verification option. Screen 2 focuses on Parent Information with optional profile photo upload. Screen 3 requires Baby Information with an age-based match preview and accessibility preferences.\n\n\n**Defining Onboarding Screens**\n\nNow I\'m designing specific screens for the onboarding flow. Screen 4 explains the six development areas in simple terms, reassuring users about the LittleSteps approach. Screen 5 allows personalizing the daily activity time, notification preferences, and preferred language. Finally, Screen 6 completes the setup with a warm welcome, personalized details, and a clear call to action to move the user on to today\'s dashboard.\n\n\n**Planning Dashboard Integration**\n\nI\'m now planning the integration of the onboarding flow with the parent dashboard. I\'ve broken it down into two batches. Batch 1 will focus on shared types, backend authentication, secure schema migrations, photo upload APIs, and the onboarding APIs themselves. I\'ll include the necessary database seeds so existing demo accounts will continue logging straight into their dashboards. Batch 2 will add the rest!\n\n\n**Defining API Implementation**\n\nI\'m now implementing the API endpoints for both batches. Batch 1 is underway, including backend authentication, secure schema migrations, and photo upload APIs. I\'m focusing on the `sessionVersion` validation to securely revoke stale sessions with password resets in `/server/middleware/auth.ts`. I am currently working on the `/auth` and `/profile` API endpoints to ensure proper user authentication and management. Batch 2 is next.\n\n\n**Executing Frontend Changes**\n\nI\'m now focused on the frontend implementation for Batch 1. I\'m exposing `verificationPreviewToken` in `AuthContext` for verification testing. I\'m adding a \"Forgot Password\" link to the `LoginPage` and implementing the `ForgotPasswordPage`, `ResetPasswordPage`, and `VerifyEmailPage`, along with inline field errors and confirm password validation. I\'m also building the 6-screen onboarding flow, including the stepper and route hooks. I\'m ensuring all of the required public routes are available.\n\n\n"
