  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "<summary>\n## 1. Task Overview\nWe are building **LittleSteps**, a parenting and early-childhood development web platform for mothers and caregivers of babies aged 0\342\200\22324 months (India-first, global-ready, responsive web now, API-ready for future Android/iOS).\n\nThe user is progressing through numbered steps:\n- **Step 0 (Completed)**: Inspected project, gathered architectural confirmations, produced `implementation_plan.md` at `/.aistudio/artifacts/brain/18054ee1-e310-4a02-8241-5541c74f7bd8/implementation_plan.md`, and built the initial end-to-end backend + app upon `Proceed`.\n- **Step 1 (Completed)**: Built the complete reusable LittleSteps Design System (`/src/design-system/*`, 20 components, design tokens, showcase page, and 7 passing component tests).\n- **Step 2 (Completed)**: Built the responsive public website with all 9 required pages (`/`, `/about`, `/how-it-works`, `/our-approach`, `/contact`, `/privacy`, `/terms`, `/login`, `/register`, plus `/design-system`) using the Step 1 design system, with Contact Us backed by SQLite (`POST /api/v1/contact`).\n- **Step 3 (CURRENT \342\200\224 IN PROGRESS)**: Implement complete **authentication** and **6-screen parent onboarding**:\n  - **Auth pages required**: (1) Registration, (2) Login, (3) Forgot password, (4) Reset password, (5) Email verification, (6) Logout.\n  - **Parent onboarding journey (after registration)** with stepper, back-and-edit navigation, inline field validation, clearly marked optional fields, mobile one-handed friendliness, and explanations of why info is collected:\n    - Screen 1: Welcome \342\200\224 Heading `\"Let\'s get to know your little one.\"`\n    - Screen 2: Parent information \342\200\224 Parent\'s name, Email, Preferred language, Optional profile photo.\n    - Screen 3: Baby information \342\200\224 Baby\'s name or preferred nickname, Date of birth, Optional profile photo, Optional accessibility or activity preferences.\n    - Screen 4: Development journey \342\200\224 Explain the six development areas in simple language.\n    - Screen 5: Personalization \342\200\224 Preferred daily activity time, Notification preference, Preferred language.\n    - Screen 6: Completion \342\200\224 Welcoming success screen taking parent to the dashboard.\n  - **Security**: Parents access only their own profiles/children; strict server-side validation; never log passwords or sensitive tokens; proper session management.\n\n### Confirmed User Decisions (from Step 0 & Step 1)\n- **Database**: Local SQLite (`better-sqlite3`, WAL mode, foreign keys ON) behind Repository Layer (`LittleStepsRepository`) on Express (`/api/v1`).\n- **Child Video Privacy**: Private non-public storage vault (`./private_media`), 5-minute HMAC signed stream tokens, 30-day automatic deletion worker + instant parent delete, immutable audit logs.\n- **Localization**: English first with i18n-ready architecture (`en` / `hi` ready).\n- **Visual Design (Step 1 approved tokens)**:\n  - Primary: Soft Sage Green (`#446E5A`, `--color-sage`, hover `#375A49`, soft `#EBF2EE`, border `#C5D8CE`)\n  - Secondary: Warm Cream (`#F6F1E7`, `--color-cream`)\n  - Background: Off-White (`#FAF9F6`, `--color-offwhite`)\n  - Cards: White (`#FFFFFF`, `--color-surface`)\n  - Accent: Muted Peach (`#E8B99B`, soft `#FBF1EA`, AA ink `#844825`)\n  - Highlight: Soft Lavender (`#D6CEE9`, soft `#F3F0FA`, AA ink `#4F4278`)\n  - Text: Dark Charcoal (`#222624`, `--color-charcoal`), Secondary: Muted Grey (`#5C635E`, `--color-muted`)\n  - Fonts: `Nunito` (display/headings), `Plus Jakarta Sans` (body/controls), `IBM Plex Mono` (`tabular-nums`).\n- **Core Product Rules**: 8 age groups (`0-3m` through `21-24m`), 6 development domains (Cognitive, Language & communication, Physical, Social & emotional, Sensory, Early independence & everyday skills). Reviewer instruction-match scores evaluate **caregiver activity execution ONLY** \342\200\224 never baby intelligence, developmental level, or health. Do NOT invent testimonials, stats, certifications, or expert endorsements.\n\n## 2. Progress\n### Completed Previously (Steps 0, 1, 2)\n- **Generated Montessori editorial image assets** (in `/src/assets/images/`, referenced via `EDITORIAL_IMAGES` in `/src/shared/domain.ts`):\n  - `hero_montessori_play_1795191199446.jpg`\n  - `activity_sensory_linen_1795191186954.jpg`\n  - `activity_tummy_mirror_1795191186302.jpg`\n  - `activity_everyday_cup_1795191187309.jpg`\n- **Installed packages**: `better-sqlite3`, `@types/better-sqlite3`, `multer`, `@types/multer`, `cookie-parser`, `@types/cookie-parser`, `zod`.\n- **Config files updated**: `/metadata.json`, `/index.html`, `/package.json` (`\"dev\": \"tsx server.ts\"`, `\"start\": \"node server.ts\"`), `/tsconfig.json` (`strict: true`, `types: [\"vite/client\", \"node\"]`), `/.gitignore`, `/.env.example`, `/src/index.css`.\n- **Design System (`/src/design-system/`)**: All 20 reusable components + `tokens.ts` + `index.ts` + `/src/design-system/__tests__/designSystem.test.tsx` (7/7 tests passing via `npx tsx --test src/design-system/__tests__/designSystem.test.tsx`).\n- **Public Website (`/src/pages/public/`)**: `HomePage.tsx`, `InfoPages.tsx`, `SupportLegalPages.tsx`, `AuthPages.tsx`, `PublicLayout.tsx`, `src/lib/router.ts`.\n- **Authenticated App Views**: `ParentJourneyView.tsx`, `ReviewerWorkbenchView.tsx`, `AdminConsoleView.tsx`, `DesignSystemShowcasePage.tsx`.\n- **Skills read**: `planning-mode`, `frontend-design` (`SKILL.md`, `references/6_education_simulations.md`, `references/3_saas_dashboard.md`, `references/10_mobile_touch_apps.md`, `references/2_landing_marketing.md`).\n\n### Completed in Step 3 (Batch 1 \342\200\224 Backend & Shared Types DONE)\n1. `/src/shared/types.ts`: Added `PreferredActivityTime`, `NotificationPreference`, and extended `UserProfile` (`profilePhotoUrl`, `preferredActivityTime`, `notificationPreference`, `emailVerifiedAt`, `onboardingCompletedAt`) and `ChildProfile` (`profilePhotoUrl`, `activityPreferences`).\n2. `/server/security/crypto.ts`: Added `sessionVersion` to HMAC session tokens, `generateOneTimeToken()`, `hashOneTimeToken()` (SHA-256), and `validateImageMagicBytes()` (JPEG/PNG/WebP).\n3. `/server/db/schema.ts`: Added `auth_tokens` table (`email_verification`, `password_reset` with `token_hash`, `expires_at`, `used_at`) and idempotent `ensureColumn` SQLite migrations for `users` (`email_verified_at`, `profile_photo_url`, `preferred_activity_time`, `notification_preference`, `onboarding_completed_at`, `session_version`) and `children` (`profile_photo_url`, `activity_preferences`), marking seeded demo accounts verified & onboarded.\n4. `/server/middleware/auth.ts`: Updated `requireAuth` to call `repo.findUserAuthById()` and verify `authRecord.sessionVersion === payload.sessionVersion` so password resets revoke stale sessions.\n5. `/server/repositories/index.ts`: Updated `UserRow`/`mapUser`, `findUserByEmail`, `findUserAuthById`, `createUser`, `listChildrenByParent`, `createChild`, `updateChild`; added `createAuthToken`, `consumeAuthToken`, `markEmailVerified`, `updateUserPasswordAndBumpSession`, `updateParentProfileAndPreferences`, `userOwnsPhotoKey`.\n6. `/server/routes/api.ts`:\n   - Updated `POST /api/v1/auth/register` (generates email verification token, returns `verificationPreviewPath` in non-production preview so verification can be tested without SMTP) and `POST /api/v1/auth/login` (embeds `sessionVersion`).\n   - Added `POST /api/v1/auth/forgot-password` (generic anti-enumeration response + `resetPreviewPath` in non-production), `POST /api/v1/auth/reset-password` (validates hashed token, updates password, bumps `session_version`, clears cookie), `POST /api/v1/auth/verify-email`, `POST /api/v1/auth/resend-verification`.\n   - Added `POST /api/v1/profile/photo` (validates MIME + magic bytes, stores in private vault) and `GET /api/v1/profile/photo/:key`.\n   - Added `PUT /api/v1/onboarding/parent` and `POST /api/v1/onboarding/complete`.\n   - Updated `POST /api/v1/children` and `PATCH /api/v1/children/:id` to accept optional `profilePhotoUrl` and `activityPreferences`.\n\n### Still Remaining for Step 3 (Batch 2 \342\200\224 Frontend + Security Check + Verification)\n- **NOT YET EDITED**:\n  - `/server/routes/api.ts` (security hardening check on `GET /api/v1/profile/photo/:key` \342\200\224 see Active Context below!)\n  - `/src/lib/router.ts`\n  - `/src/lib/api.ts`\n  - `/src/context/AuthContext.tsx`\n  - `/src/pages/public/AuthPages.tsx`\n  - `/src/pages/ParentOnboardingView.tsx` (new file to create)\n  - `/src/App.tsx`\n- **NOT YET VERIFIED**: Step 3 edits have NOT been compiled, linted, restarted, or runtime-tested yet.\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n- **Zod v4 syntax**: Installed Zod is v4. Use `{ message: \'...\' }` on `z.literal(true, { message: \'...\' })` rather than `errorMap`.\n- **SQLite live migration**: Existing `./data/littlesteps.db` is persisted across dev server restarts; all new columns use idempotent `PRAGMA table_info` + `ALTER TABLE` in `/server/db/schema.ts`, and seeded demo accounts (`meera@littlesteps.in`, `ananya.reviewer@littlesteps.in`, `kavita.admin@littlesteps.in`, password `LittleSteps123!`) are automatically marked `email_verified_at` and `onboarding_completed_at` so demo logins still go directly to their dashboards while newly registered parents enter the 6-screen onboarding flow!\n- **Private Photo Ownership Security**: In `POST /api/v1/profile/photo`, a photo is uploaded *before* the user submits the parent/child form. To ensure a parent can **strictly ONLY access their own profile/child photos** even before saving, embed the owner\'s `userId` in a short prefix or track uploaded photo keys in a small `user_media_assets` table (or signed query token / userId-scoped filename or table `profile_photos(storage_key PRIMARY KEY, owner_user_id TEXT NOT NULL)`) and check ownership strictly inside `GET /api/v1/profile/photo/:key`! Currently `GET /api/v1/profile/photo/:key` only checks `requireAuth` without verifying `owner_user_id === req.authUser.id` \342\200\224 tighten this in the next step before finishing Step 3!\n\n## 4. Errors & Fixes\n- **Error 1 (Resolved in Step 0)**: `server/routes/api.ts(69,5): error TS2769: \'errorMap\' does not exist` on `z.literal(true)` due to Zod v4. **Fix**: Replaced `errorMap` with `message`.\n- No unresolved errors exist; Step 3 Batch 1 has not been compiled yet.\n\n## 5. Active Context\n- Server runs on port `3000` via `tsx server.ts` (Express `/api/v1/*` + Vite middleware).\n- After completing Batch 2 edits, `restart_dev_server` MUST be called so Express loads the updated SQLite migrations and new `/api/v1/auth/*` and `/api/v1/onboarding/*` endpoints.\n- Seeded demo accounts (password `LittleSteps123!`):\n  - Parent: `meera@littlesteps.in`\n  - Reviewer: `ananya.reviewer@littlesteps.in`\n  - Admin: `kavita.admin@littlesteps.in`\n- Note: Check `/server/db/seed.ts` as well \342\200\224 fresh empty DB seed inserts users without explicitly setting `email_verified_at` / `onboarding_completed_at`, and `runMigrations` runs BEFORE `seedDatabaseIfEmpty`! So on a brand-new DB, the `UPDATE users SET ... WHERE id IN (...)` in `schema.ts` would run before `seedDatabaseIfEmpty` inserts those users. Therefore, also set `email_verified_at` and `onboarding_completed_at` directly inside `seedDatabaseIfEmpty` in `/server/db/seed.ts` so both existing and fresh databases behave identically.\n\n## 6. Next Steps (In Priority Order)\n1. **Tighten photo ownership & fresh-seed parity**:\n   - In `/server/db/schema.ts`, add `profile_photos (storage_key TEXT PRIMARY KEY, owner_user_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE, created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (strftime(\'%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ\', \'now\')))`.\n   - In `/server/repositories/index.ts`, add `registerProfilePhoto(storageKey, ownerUserId)` and update `userOwnsPhotoKey(userId, storageKey)` to check `profile_photos` (plus `users`/`children`).\n   - In `/server/routes/api.ts`, call `repo.registerProfilePhoto(storageKey, req.authUser!.id)` on `POST /profile/photo`, and enforce `if (!repo.userOwnsPhotoKey(req.authUser!.id, key)) return res.status(403)...` on `GET /profile/photo/:key`.\n   - In `/server/db/seed.ts`, set `email_verified_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP` and `onboarding_completed_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP` on the 3 seeded demo users.\n2. **Update frontend router (`/src/lib/router.ts`)**:\n   - Add `\'/forgot-password\'`, `\'/reset-password\'`, and `\'/verify-email\'` to `PublicRoute` and `VALID_ROUTES`.\n   - Support reading query string parameters (e.g. `search` / `getQueryParam(\'token\')`) and navigating with query strings (e.g. `navigate(\'/reset-password?token=...\')`).\n3. **Update frontend API client (`/src/lib/api.ts`)**:\n   - Update `register` return type to `{ user: UserProfile; verificationPreviewPath?: string }`.\n   - Add `forgotPassword(email)`, `resetPassword(token, newPassword)`, `verifyEmail(token)`, `resendVerification()`, `uploadProfilePhoto(file)`, `saveOnboardingParent(payload)`, `completeOnboarding(payload)`.\n   - Update `createChild` and `updateChild` to accept optional `profilePhotoUrl` and `activityPreferences`.\n4. **Update `/src/context/AuthContext.tsx`**:\n   - Store `verificationPreviewPath: string | null` in state (populated on `register` or `resendVerification`, cleared on verification/logout) so newly registered parents can easily test verifying their email in the preview environment without SMTP.\n   - Expose `setUser`, `verificationPreviewPath`, `setVerificationPreviewPath`, and `logout` (ensuring logout clears user and preview state cleanly).\n5. **Complete all 6 Authentication Pages in `/src/pages/public/AuthPages.tsx`**:\n   - **`LoginPage`**: Add `\"Forgot password?\"` link \342\206\222 `/forgot-password`, field-level validation messages next to email/password inputs, and demo workspace buttons.\n   - **`RegisterPage`**: Add password confirmation input, field-level inline validation next to each input, clear optional label on mobile number, and on success smoothly enter onboarding (while storing `verificationPreviewPath`).\n   - **`ForgotPasswordPage`** (`/forgot-password`): Validates email, calls `POST /api/v1/auth/forgot-password`, displays calm confirmation message + prototype preview button linking directly to `resetPreviewPath` when provided.\n   - **`ResetPasswordPage`** (`/reset-password`): Reads `token` from query string (with fallback manual token input if absent), collects new password + confirm password with inline validation, calls `POST /api/v1/auth/reset-password`, and navigates cleanly to `/login` on success with toast confirmation.\n   - **`VerifyEmailPage`** (`/verify-email`): Reads `token` from query string and verifies automatically via `POST /api/v1/auth/verify-email` (or allows pasting a token / clicking \"Resend verification link\" when signed in), updates `AuthContext` user state, and offers a clear button to continue to Onboarding or Dashboard.\n6. **Create 6-Screen Parent Onboarding Journey (`/src/pages/ParentOnboardingView.tsx`)**:\n   - Accessible 6-step horizontal/compact mobile stepper (`1. Welcome`, `2. Parent`, `3. Baby`, `4. Journey`, `5. Preferences`, `6. Complete`) using Step 1 Design System components (`Card`, `Input`, `Select`, `DatePicker`, `Button`, `Badge`, `ProgressIndicator`).\n   - **Screen 1 (Welcome)**: Heading `\"Let\'s get to know your little one.\"`, warm explanation of why onboarding personalizes daily activities, plus optional gentle Email Verification status card if `!user.emailVerifiedAt` (with quick Verify link or Resend button).\n   - **Screen 2 (Parent information)**: Parent\'s name, Email, Preferred language (`en` / `hi`), and Optional profile photo upload (`POST /api/v1/profile/photo` with preview & remove), explaining why each detail is collected. Saves via `PUT /api/v1/onboarding/parent`.\n   - **Screen 3 (Baby information)**: Baby\'s name/nickname, Date of birth (`DatePicker` with `showBabyAgePreview`), Optional profile photo upload, Optional accessibility or activity preferences textarea. Creates/updates child via `POST /api/v1/children` or `PATCH /api/v1/children/:id` (so going back to edit updates the existing child rather than duplicating it!).\n   - **Screen 4 (Development journey)**: Explains all 6 development areas in warm, simple language with reassuring non-diagnostic note.\n   - **Screen 5 (Personalization)**: Preferred daily activity time (`Morning`, `Afternoon`, `Evening`, `Flexible`), Notification preference (`Gentle daily reminder`, `Weekly summary`, `No reminders`), Preferred language (synced with Screen 2).\n   - **Screen 6 (Completion)**: Welcoming summary screen showing baby\'s name, matched 3-month age band, and preferences; `\"Go to Today\342\200\231s Dashboard\"` button calls `POST /api/v1/onboarding/complete`, updates `AuthContext`, and transitions seamlessly to the Parent Dashboard.\n   - Ensure Back buttons on steps 2\342\200\2235 allow editing previous steps cleanly, every field has inline validation, and all optional fields are explicitly labeled `(Optional)`.\n7. **Wire routes & onboarding gate in `/src/App.tsx`**:\n   - Allow `/verify-email` and `/reset-password` to work cleanly whether logged in or logged out.\n   - When `user.role === \'parent\' && !user.onboardingCompletedAt` (and not currently on `/verify-email` or `/design-system`), render `ParentOnboardingView` automatically (with a top bar containing `LittleSteps` + `Sign Out`).\n   - On Logout from any role workspace, navigate cleanly back to `/` (or `/login`) with a confirmation toast.\n   - In `AuthenticatedWorkspace` for parents, if `!user.emailVerifiedAt`, show a subtle, calm non-intrusive notice banner with a `\"Verify Email\"` button leading to `/verify-email`.\n8. **Verify Everything End-to-End**:\n   - Co-execute `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` (must pass with 0 TypeScript strict errors and clean Vite build).\n   - Run `restart_dev_server` so Express loads the updated schema and routes.\n   - Run a live `curl` end-to-end API verification test (register new parent \342\206\222 verify email token \342\206\222 forgot password \342\206\222 reset password + confirm old session cookie returns `401` \342\206\222 login with new password \342\206\222 complete parent onboarding + add child \342\206\222 confirm cross-parent photo/child isolation returns `403/404` \342\206\222 clean up test user from SQLite if desired) AND re-run `npx tsx --test src/design-system/__tests__/designSystem.test.tsx`.\n\n## 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- Follow strict TypeScript (`strict: true`), Tailwind CSS v4 (`@import \"tailwindcss\";` in `src/index.css`, no inline style hacks), WCAG 2.2 AA contrast, `>= 44px` touch targets, `prefers-reduced-motion`, and Step 1 Design System components (`Button`, `Input`, `Select`, `DatePicker`, `Card`, `Badge`, `ProgressIndicator`, `Toast`).\n- Never use `window.alert`, `window.confirm`, or `window.open`.\n- Never log passwords, raw reset/verification tokens, or sensitive user info on the server.\n- Never invent testimonials, stats, certifications, or medical/developmental claims.\n- Keep final response concise, scannable, and free of internal file paths or hype.\n</summary>"
