  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Core Auth Flows**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the authentication flows. I\'m carefully reviewing every requirement for the six authentication flows. Specifically, I\'m starting with the registration flow and the `/register` path in `AuthPages.tsx`, focusing on those initial field requirements. I\'m working from the list in step 3 to make sure I don\'t miss anything.\n\n\n**Analyzing Auth Flows Details**\n\nI\'ve moved on to the login and forgot password flows. I\'m focusing on the field requirements, validation, and API interactions for each. The \"Forgot password\" flow now includes that anti-enumeration confirmation state, along with the preview reset link button. I\'m paying close attention to the quick prototype workspace buttons, making sure they\'re preserved in this authentication state.\n\n\n**Examining Password Reset Details**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the reset password and email verification flows within `AuthPages.tsx`. I\'ve outlined the core functionality: reading the reset token, collecting new password data with inline validation, and the API calls. I\'m noting the success confirmation and redirection to login. For email verification, I\'ve got the token handling and API interaction figured out, including the logged-in/logged-out scenarios and CTA guidance.\n\n\n**Defining Logout & Onboarding**\n\nI\'m now detailing the logout functionality, ensuring it\'s accessible and user-friendly. I\'m focusing on the `POST /api/v1/auth/logout` call, and the clean navigation back to either `/login` or `/` with a reassuring toast confirmation. I\'m also mapping out the 6-screen onboarding journey at `/src/pages/ParentOnboardingView.tsx`, starting with the welcome screen and its calm explanation of the process. I\'m making sure to include the email verification reminder if the user has not verified their email.\n\n\n**Mapping Onboarding Details**\n\nI\'m now detailing Screens 2 and 3 of the onboarding flow. Screen 2 focuses on collecting parent details: name, email, language preference, and an optional profile photo that uploads immediately. The \"Continue\" button saves these with a `PUT /api/v1/onboarding/parent` call. Screen 3 covers baby information, automatically matching the date of birth to one of 8 age groups. I\'m loading any existing child data with `api.listChildren`. There is an email verification status card at the top, without blocking the flow!\n\n\n**Detailing Onboarding: Screen 4**\n\nI\'m now detailing the child onboarding flow\'s Screen 4, where the user can detail the child\'s development journey. I\'m focusing on the presentation of the six development areas using language from `CANONICAL_LEARNING_DOMAINS`, ensuring clear and simple explanations. I\'m making sure it uses calming icons and relatable everyday scenarios. I am now focused on making sure the app is able to `PATCH /api/v1/children/:id` on the completion of screen 3!\n\n\n**Outlining Onboarding\'s Screen 5**\n\nI\'m currently fleshing out Screen 5 of the onboarding process, the personalization stage. I\'m focusing on crafting concise explanations of why the collected preferences matter for a gentle daily flow, avoiding unnecessary interruptions. Specifically, I\'m defining the activity time options (morning, afternoon, evening, flexible), notification preferences (daily reminder, weekly summary, or none), and the preferred language (with the prepopulated value from Screen 2). Finally, I\'m ensuring all is saved with `POST /api/v1/onboarding/preferences` upon continuing.\n\n\n**Finalizing Onboarding Completion**\n\nI\'m now detailing the final onboarding screen (Screen 6), the success state. It\'s a welcoming screen that summarizes key preferences. I\'m ensuring it allows for easy adjustments with the \"Back to Edit Preferences\" button.  The primary CTA, \"Go to Today\342\200\231s Dashboard,\" triggers the final API call marking the onboarding as complete and entering the parent dashboard. I\'ve thought about how to keep a user from leaving the page before completing onboarding, but am now focused on an optimal user experience.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "9IwAa-nUAovm4t4PvZqZiQo"
