  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Initiating System Verification**\n\nI\'m currently focused on automated verification. I\'ve formulated a verification script leveraging `run_command` that will execute the design system\'s test suite via `npx tsx`, focusing on the design system. I am designing the testing to cover the Step 3 authentication, onboarding, and security isolation flow.\n\n\n**Defining Test Sequences**\n\nI am now structuring the test scenarios for the authentication, onboarding, and security isolation flow. I\'m building out a series of API requests, including registration, email verification, onboarding steps (parent and child profiles), photo uploads, and completion, to be performed using `fetch`. The aim is to establish robust automated tests focusing on the expected HTTP status codes and responses, specifically validating access control for photo retrieval between users.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "040Aa53oOMaI694P2Puz0AE"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_8360716195475992481"
      name: "run_command"
      arguments_json: "{\"CommandLine\":\"npx tsx --test src/design-system/__tests__/designSystem.test.tsx && node -e \'\\nconst fs = require(\\\"fs\\\");\\nconst BASE = \\\"http://localhost:3000/api/v1\\\";\\n\\nasync function req(path, opts = {}, cookie = \\\"\\\") {\\n  const headers = { ...(opts.headers || {}) };\\n  if (cookie) headers[\\\"Cookie\\\"] = cookie;\\n  const res = await fetch(`${BASE}${path}`, { ...opts, headers });\\n  const setCookie = res.headers.get(\\\"set-cookie\\\");\\n  const nextCookie = setCookie ? setCookie.split(\\\";\\\")[0] : cookie;\\n  let body = null;\\n  const ct = res.headers.get(\\\"content-type\\\") || \\\"\\\";\\n  if (ct.includes(\\\"application/json\\\")) body = await res.json();\\n  else body = await res.arrayBuffer();\\n  return { status: res.status, body, cookie: nextCookie };\\n}\\n\\nfunction assert(cond, msg) {\\n  if (!cond) { console.error(\\\"FAIL:\\\", msg); process.exit(1); }\\n}\\n\\n(async () => {\\n  const email = `step3_${Date.now()}@littlesteps.in`;\\n\\n  // 1. Register new parent\\n  const reg = await req(\\\"/auth/register\\\", {\\n    method: \\\"POST\\\",\\n    headers: { \\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\" },\\n    body: JSON.stringify({ fullName: \\\"Priya Nair\\\", email, password: \\\"Password123!\\\" }),\\n  });\\n  assert(reg.status === 201, `register expected 201 got ${reg.status}`);\\n  assert(reg.body.user.emailVerifiedAt === null, \\\"new user should be unverified\\\");\\n  assert(reg.body.user.onboardingCompletedAt === null, \\\"new user should not be onboarded\\\");\\n  assert(reg.body.verificationPreviewPath, \\\"expected verificationPreviewPath\\\");\\n  const oldSessionCookie = reg.cookie;\\n\\n  // 2. Verify email & confirm single-use token\\n  const verifyToken = new URL(\\\"http://x\\\" + reg.body.verificationPreviewPath).searchParams.get(\\\"token\\\");\\n  const ver1 = await req(\\\"/auth/verify-email\\\", {\\n    method: \\\"POST\\\",\\n    headers: { \\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\" },\\n    body: JSON.stringify({ token: verifyToken }),\\n  });\\n  assert(ver1.status === 200 && ver1.body.user.emailVerifiedAt, \\\"email verification failed\\\");\\n  const ver2 = await req(\\\"/auth/verify-email\\\", {\\n    method: \\\"POST\\\",\\n    headers: { \\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\" },\\n    body: JSON.stringify({ token: verifyToken }),\\n  });\\n  assert(ver2.status === 400, \\\"reused verification token should fail with 400\\\");\\n\\n  // 3. Upload private PNG photo (valid PNG magic bytes)\\n  const pngBytes = Buffer.from(\\\"89504e470d0a1a0a0000000d49484452000000010000000108060000001f15c4890000000a49444154789c63000100000500010d0a2db40000000049454e44ae426082\\\", \\\"hex\\\");\\n  const form = new FormData();\\n  form.append(\\\"photo\\\", new Blob([pngBytes], { type: \\\"image/png\\\" }), \\\"avatar.png\\\");\\n  const up = await req(\\\"/profile/photo\\\", { method: \\\"POST\\\", body: form }, oldSessionCookie);\\n  assert(up.status === 201 && up.body.photoUrl, `photo upload failed: ${up.status}`);\\n  const photoUrl = up.body.photoUrl;\\n\\n  // 4. Owner can read photo; another parent (Meera) is blocked with 403\\n  const ownPhoto = await req(photoUrl.replace(\\\"/api/v1\\\", \\\"\\\"), { method: \\\"GET\\\" }, oldSessionCookie);\\n  assert(ownPhoto.status === 200, \\\"owner should access own photo\\\");\\n\\n  const meeraLogin = await req(\\\"/auth/login\\\", {\\n    method: \\\"POST\\\",\\n    headers: { \\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\" },\\n    body: JSON.stringify({ email: \\\"meera@littlesteps.in\\\", password: \\\"LittleSteps123!\\\" }),\\n  });\\n  assert(meeraLogin.status === 200 && meeraLogin.body.user.onboardingCompletedAt, \\\"demo parent should be onboarded\\\");\\n  const otherPhoto = await req(photoUrl.replace(\\\"/api/v1\\\", \\\"\\\"), { method: \\\"GET\\\" }, meeraLogin.cookie);\\n  assert(otherPhoto.status === 403, `other parent should get 403 on photo, got ${otherPhoto.status}`);\\n\\n  // 5. Save onboarding parent info + create & edit baby profile + complete onboarding\\n  const pSave = await req(\\\"/onboarding/parent\\\", {\\n    method: \\\"PUT\\\",\\n    headers: { \\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\" },\\n    body: JSON.stringify({ fullName: \\\"Priya R. Nair\\\", email, preferredLocale: \\\"en\\\", profilePhotoUrl: photoUrl }),\\n  }, oldSessionCookie);\\n  assert(pSave.status === 200 && pSave.body.user.fullName === \\\"Priya R. Nair\\\", \\\"parent onboarding save failed\\\");\\n\\n  const cCreate = await req(\\\"/children\\\", {\\n    method: \\\"POST\\\",\\n    headers: { \\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\" },\\n    body: JSON.stringify({ displayName: \\\"Diya\\\", dateOfBirth: \\\"2026-04-01\\\", profilePhotoUrl: photoUrl, activityPreferences: \\\"Prefers quiet floor play\\\" }),\\n  }, oldSessionCookie);\\n  assert(cCreate.status === 201 && cCreate.body.child.activityPreferences === \\\"Prefers quiet floor play\\\", \\\"child create failed\\\");\\n\\n  // Cross-parent child access check\\n  const crossPatch = await req(`/children/${cCreate.body.child.id}`, {\\n    method: \\\"PATCH\\\",\\n    headers: { \\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\" },\\n    body: JSON.stringify({ displayName: \\\"Hacked\\\", dateOfBirth: \\\"2026-04-01\\\" }),\\n  }, meeraLogin.cookie);\\n  assert(crossPatch.status === 404, `cross-parent child edit should return 404, got ${crossPatch.status}`);\\n\\n  const comp = await req(\\\"/onboarding/complete\\\", {\\n    method: \\\"POST\\\",\\n    headers: { \\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\" },\\n    body: JSON.stringify({ preferredActivityTime: \\\"morning\\\", notificationPreference: \\\"daily_gentle\\\", preferredLocale: \\\"en\\\", markComplete: true }),\\n  }, oldSessionCookie);\\n  assert(comp.status === 200 && comp.body.user.onboardingCompletedAt, \\\"onboarding complete failed\\\");\\n\\n  // 6. Forgot password -> Reset password -> verify old session cookie is revoked (401) -> login with new password\\n  const fp = await req(\\\"/auth/forgot-password\\\", {\\n    method: \\\"POST\\\",\\n    headers: { \\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\" },\\n    body: JSON.stringify({ email }),\\n  });\\n  assert(fp.status === 200 && fp.body.resetPreviewPath, \\\"forgot password failed\\\");\\n  const resetToken = new URL(\\\"http://x\\\" + fp.body.resetPreviewPath).searchParams.get(\\\"token\\\");\\n\\n  const rp = await req(\\\"/auth/reset-password\\\", {\\n    method: \\\"POST\\\",\\n    headers: { \\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\" },\\n    body: JSON.stringify({ token: resetToken, newPassword: \\\"NewPassword456!\\\" }),\\n  });\\n  assert(rp.status === 200, \\\"reset password failed\\\");\\n\\n  const staleMe = await req(\\\"/auth/me\\\", { method: \\\"GET\\\" }, oldSessionCookie);\\n  assert(staleMe.status === 401, `stale session after password reset should be 401, got ${staleMe.status}`);\\n\\n  const newLogin = await req(\\\"/auth/login\\\", {\\n    method: \\\"POST\\\",\\n    headers: { \\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\" },\\n    body: JSON.stringify({ email, password: \\\"NewPassword456!\\\" }),\\n  });\\n  assert(newLogin.status === 200, \\\"login with new password failed\\\");\\n\\n  const lo = await req(\\\"/auth/logout\\\", { method: \\\"POST\\\" }, newLogin.cookie);\\n  assert(lo.status === 200, \\\"logout failed\\\");\\n\\n  // Clean up test user & uploaded file\\n  const Database = require(\\\"better-sqlite3\\\");\\n  const db = new Database(\\\"./data/littlesteps.db\\\");\\n  db.prepare(\\\"DELETE FROM users WHERE email = ?\\\").run(email);\\n  db.close();\\n  const key = photoUrl.split(\\\"/\\\").pop();\\n  if (fs.existsSync(`./private_media/${key}`)) fs.unlinkSync(`./private_media/${key}`);\\n\\n  console.log(\\\"ALL STEP 3 END-TO-END AUTH, ONBOARDING & SECURITY ISOLATION CHECKS PASSED!\\\");\\n})();\\n\'\", \"Cwd\":\"/app/applet\", \"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":10000, \"toolAction\":\"Running unit and end-to-end auth verification tests\", \"toolSummary\":\"Run Step 3 verification suite\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\336\021\n\333\021\001i\024}\023\346\203L\317\305))\262\275p\201-8E\206\237\362*/\345\344p;\026\230?\310\000\240\347\244;L\rK\326\017\353\313\322\336\205\335\200`\306\231PA\\\254\253\240z\226\005\216\353s^\354)E\204\2214\301\232ie\276n\216A??EL\211f\344@Z\374S\3707\026\327\235h\311|\026dk\301\332\017\361\210H[W,\250\367\235\227\3143\356W\220\202s\265o\327\343\252wS\244+\275\213sIo\341\207\033U8&\333\343\3573\371\235\204\337\340\343\234\314A\343rd\356_\233\215Q>p\313\276y\201&\226A\"l\371\257\036\000V\036\322\354\3511\316\270\327tS3=\v\371\363S:E\273\016\r\210!\321\225\266\262zs\264\241\215`\025\271\367\031\243\215%\242\300\232\302V\200\022<\"(\377\250\032.>\3024E\255\002\027\217\001<\204\372}\264eS\213\\ \354\204\037\203\006\270\251\n\332\257f\301\327\323\2476noDo\214p\r\330\017Z\231\224\211~\264{\246?\027F pV\v\372Y\303\354p\333\213\'\027Q\373r\016\251k@]fnj\214o<\to\241b\275\335\r\230\0034\231^\21294\226\206\363\225\3018oe\236W+\270\026\233*\345\376\030\023dhQ\314\f\267\016*~\016\223\236\250\267\257\322G\225%Xp\024\375\346\241G\376\326\rC\377&\025Il\356:\274|\016\265\032MV\355R\030\311~\222\271\246\325@[>\317O\031!\022\033\363\211\t\030\031\bMH/\0269\005\271D2\346v\234\272\220\242j\\\334/\326.,\211\357\250\217\301\222\275\a\244\r\032\000\272\177/\256\314\244\311\006d\303\325\364\363.\345\306S\r\245\363?\352=v\266\307\200\357\036\253\200\313\341\375\250|\262\375\025\243\234\000\231u\a\220\312\220\365_\371k\027&f\244\033\337\244\231\202\357\251w\027\347\357U\332\210?\f~\254\3055\032\216u]\033\t\236\343|\344\362\202`\307H%O$(p\245\313\221\260\327\324\325.\351\2425H\270\255=\270\336\023D=\350 \036\027(*rN\240:\n\017\217Sj\357\0259TW\234\336S\000(e4\253?\001\320\333\235\220\200\237D\b8\035G\255\325\325Qo\"\362.\344\250\301\306\f\362CV+\352\354\335\325\265\004\271\341\261=;\206\260}!&,_e\305\326:\253\335E\237\235&\006\244\363\336\3109\bg_\034F\371J\306l#\fPf\000.a\245\264\211_D\207\202\266\216\363\224\357,#/\265[]\205~\230\360\207\252]\342