  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the LittleSteps Dashboard**\n\nI\'m focused on designing the LittleSteps parent dashboard. I want to make sure it satisfies every single requirement of the project prompt. Also, I need to guarantee it will integrate smoothly and directly with all the data from our Express + SQLite backend.\n\n\n**Mapping Data to Architecture**\n\nI\'m currently mapping backend data to the frontend architecture for the LittleSteps dashboard. Specifically, I\'m enriching `TodayJourneyResponse` to include `todaySummary` for real-time progress and a `weeklyProgress` array showing the last 7 days of activity. This includes adding an activities library endpoint, so that all published activities are visible to the parent via an accessible API. I\'m focusing on the `GET /api/v1/activities` and `GET /api/v1/activities/:id` endpoints, ensuring activities can be filtered by age and domain.\n\n\n**Refining Data Queries**\n\nI\'m now refining data queries for the LittleSteps dashboard to enhance the user experience. I\'m focusing on ensuring accurate and meaningful progress indicators. I\'m working on queries to provide a child\'s domain progress, a \"continue learning\" feature that remembers their last viewed activity, and relevant parenting tips, all derived deterministically for their current age band.\n\n\n**Implementing Real Notifications**\n\nI\'m now implementing real, computed notifications based on user/child state, such as caregiver coaching reviews and unverified email reminders, tied to actual records. I\'m also addressing demo data handling; if Meera is signed in, a \"Demo account\" badge will appear, while all values stay live and updated in SQLite. I am also checking `POST /api/v1/completions` in `/server/repositories/index.ts` to ensure that data is not overwritten.\n\n\n**Validating Completion States**\n\nI\'m now implementing logic to prevent down-grading a completion state in `activity_completions`. If a completion is `\'completed\'`, `\'submitted_for_review\'`, or `\'reviewed\'`, a `\'started\'` state cannot replace it. Also, I\'ll add a `last_opened_at` column, or appropriately update the timestamps, to accurately track the \"Continue learning\" activity.\n\n**Defining Desktop Navigation**\n\nI\'ve moved on to designing the desktop layout. I am focused on the left sidebar: a fixed-height, warm Montessori-style area with a brand mark and child profile switcher. Primary navigation includes \'Today\' (main dashboard), \'My Plan\' (structured journey), and \'Activities\' (browse all).\n\n\n**Defining Desktop Navigation**\n\nI\'m now diving into secondary navigation, separated from the main sidebar. I\'m imagining parenting guides, a notification center, parent/baby profiles, and settings. Also, I\'m sketching a top header: a welcoming greeting, a notification bell, and a user profile button, all contextually aware. The breadcrumb will also sit in the header. Lastly, the main content area will sit in a comfortable max width of `max-w-5xl`.\n\n\n**Planning Mobile Layouts**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the mobile layout considerations. I\'m focusing on the responsive design, especially for the `< lg` breakpoint, starting at 320px. My current priorities include the no-sidebar design and compact top header with the `LittleSteps` brand mark, child chip, notification bell, and drawer menu. The primary layout consideration is the single-column main content with a bottom navigation fixed at the bottom.\n\n\n**Visualizing Daily Activities**\n\nI\'m now visualizing Aarav\'s daily activities. I\'m focusing on the \"Today\'s Learning Journey\" hero card to show completed vs. total activities, and a progress ring. A prominent \"Continue Today\'s Journey\" button will direct the parent to the next activity. I\'m also building an \"Activities Grid\" to display each activity card, with titles, domains, durations, age groups, and completion statuses. The CTA will be \"Start Activity\".\n\n\n**Visualizing Domain Progress**\n\nI\'m now visualizing Aarav\'s weekly and domain-specific progress. I\'m focusing on a clean, uncluttered 7-day bar chart showing completed activities per day, derived from SQLite, with \"tabular-nums\" counts, a highlight for today, and a total weekly sessions summary. If there are no sessions this week, there will be a meaningful empty message. I\'m also planning calm cards representing all 6 development domains, each with a real `ProgressIndicator` and session count.\n\n\n**Designing UI States**\n\nI\'m now focusing on UI states for a smooth parent experience. I\'m adding loading skeletons for data fetching, meaningful empty states when content is unavailable, and friendly error messages with retry options. I\'m creating several shared types: `WeeklyProgressDay`, `LastOpenedActivity`, `ParentingTip`, `ParentNotificationItem`, extending `DomainProgressStat` with `availableCount`, and adding to `TodayJourneyResponse`.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "M_UAa43AM7_U-8YPkqDK6Ao"
