  planner_response {
    response: "I have built the responsive **LittleSteps Parent Dashboard**, connected end-to-end to the SQLite + Express application data layer.\n\n### Layout & Navigation\n- **Desktop (`lg+`)**: Sticky left sidebar with the baby profile switcher, primary navigation (**Today**, **My Plan**, **Activities**, **Progress**), and secondary navigation (**Parenting Guides**, **Notifications**, **Profile**, **Settings**), paired with a top header showing a time-of-day greeting, live notification badge, and profile quick access over a centered `max-w-5xl` content area.\n- **Mobile (`320px+` to `<1024px`)**: Compact single-row header with notification access and a secondary menu drawer, single-column layout, and a fixed bottom navigation bar for the four primary tabs with `>= 44px` touch targets.\n\n### All 7 Dashboard Sections (on **Today**)\n1. **Welcome Area**: Dynamic time-of-day greeting (e.g., *\"Good morning, Meera!\"*), *\"Ready for today\342\200\231s little moments?\"*, and the active baby\342\200\231s name, age in months, and matched age group (with a transparent *\"Sample demo data\"* badge shown only on the pre-seeded demo account).\n2. **Today\342\200\231s Learning Journey**: Prominent card showing actual completed vs. total activities for today, a linear + ring daily completion indicator, and a **Continue Today\342\200\231s Journey** CTA that opens the next pending activity.\n3. **Today\342\200\231s Activities**: Responsive grid of activity cards displaying title, development domain, estimated duration, age group, thumbnail, live completion status, and **Start Activity** / **Continue Activity** / **Review Activity** CTAs leading into the interactive Activity Studio.\n4. **Weekly Progress**: 7-day visual bar chart driven directly by SQLite completion records across the past week, with a calm prompt when no sessions have been logged yet.\n5. **Development Areas**: Six domain cards (Cognitive, Language & Communication, Physical, Social & Emotional, Sensory, and Early Independence & Everyday Skills), each with its own real progress bar and click-through into that domain\342\200\231s activities.\n6. **Continue Learning**: Automatically tracks the last activity a parent opened or started (without downgrading completed or reviewed statuses) so mothers can resume in one tap, or shows a clear empty state before the first session.\n7. **Parenting Tip**: Displays one short, practical Montessori tip tailored to the baby\342\200\231s current 3-month age band.\n\n### Supporting Views & UI Resilience\n- **My Plan, Activities, & Progress**: Day-by-day plan selector, full published activity library filterable across all 8 age bands and 6 domains, and a combined Progress & Caregiver Coaching Feedback view (preserving private video playback and instant deletion).\n- **Secondary Sections**: Practical **Parenting Guides**, live **Notifications**, **Profile** (parent/baby editing, child switching, and private photo uploads), and **Settings** (activity time, reminder cadence, language, email verification, password reset, and sign out).\n- **States & Verification**: Includes loading skeletons, meaningful empty states, and retryable friendly error messages. Verified with strict TypeScript checking, production build, all 7 design system tests, and live API checks covering weekly progress aggregation, 6-domain ratios, status preservation, and the published activities library."
    message_id: "Y_cAa5PmMcLA_uMPttDz6Ac"
    modified_response: "I have built the responsive **LittleSteps Parent Dashboard**, connected end-to-end to the SQLite + Express application data layer.\n\n### Layout & Navigation\n- **Desktop (`lg+`)**: Sticky left sidebar with the baby profile switcher, primary navigation (**Today**, **My Plan**, **Activities**, **Progress**), and secondary navigation (**Parenting Guides**, **Notifications**, **Profile**, **Settings**), paired with a top header showing a time-of-day greeting, live notification badge, and profile quick access over a centered `max-w-5xl` content area.\n- **Mobile (`320px+` to `<1024px`)**: Compact single-row header with notification access and a secondary menu drawer, single-column layout, and a fixed bottom navigation bar for the four primary tabs with `>= 44px` touch targets.\n\n### All 7 Dashboard Sections (on **Today**)\n1. **Welcome Area**: Dynamic time-of-day greeting (e.g., *\"Good morning, Meera!\"*), *\"Ready for today\342\200\231s little moments?\"*, and the active baby\342\200\231s name, age in months, and matched age group (with a transparent *\"Sample demo data\"* badge shown only on the pre-seeded demo account).\n2. **Today\342\200\231s Learning Journey**: Prominent card showing actual completed vs. total activities for today, a linear + ring daily completion indicator, and a **Continue Today\342\200\231s Journey** CTA that opens the next pending activity.\n3. **Today\342\200\231s Activities**: Responsive grid of activity cards displaying title, development domain, estimated duration, age group, thumbnail, live completion status, and **Start Activity** / **Continue Activity** / **Review Activity** CTAs leading into the interactive Activity Studio.\n4. **Weekly Progress**: 7-day visual bar chart driven directly by SQLite completion records across the past week, with a calm prompt when no sessions have been logged yet.\n5. **Development Areas**: Six domain cards (Cognitive, Language & Communication, Physical, Social & Emotional, Sensory, and Early Independence & Everyday Skills), each with its own real progress bar and click-through into that domain\342\200\231s activities.\n6. **Continue Learning**: Automatically tracks the last activity a parent opened or started (without downgrading completed or reviewed statuses) so mothers can resume in one tap, or shows a clear empty state before the first session.\n7. **Parenting Tip**: Displays one short, practical Montessori tip tailored to the baby\342\200\231s current 3-month age band.\n\n### Supporting Views & UI Resilience\n- **My Plan, Activities, & Progress**: Day-by-day plan selector, full published activity library filterable across all 8 age bands and 6 domains, and a combined Progress & Caregiver Coaching Feedback view (preserving private video playback and instant deletion).\n- **Secondary Sections**: Practical **Parenting Guides**, live **Notifications**, **Profile** (parent/baby editing, child switching, and private photo uploads), and **Settings** (activity time, reminder cadence, language, email verification, password reset, and sign out).\n- **States & Verification**: Includes loading skeletons, meaningful empty states, and retryable friendly error messages. Verified with strict TypeScript checking, production build, all 7 design system tests, and live API checks covering weekly progress aggregation, 6-domain ratios, status preservation, and the published activities library."
