  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Relevant Skills**\n\nI\'m focusing on \"frontend-design,\" identified as relevant. It was already reviewed earlier. I\'m considering how to integrate these skills into a structured daily learning journey. The goal is to build a robust system.\n\n\n**Analyzing Current Status**\n\nI\'m now auditing the requirements for Step 5, focusing on displaying \"My Plan.\" I\'m reviewing the current baby age display, learning week calculation, and formatted date requirements. I need to ensure a clean implementation of these elements on the main page. This includes building a display for week calculations for the current baby, with an adaptable date output.\n\n\n**Structuring Daily Plans**\n\nI\'m now focused on generating a more structured and realistic daily plan. I\'m prioritizing the daily completion metrics, including a visual progress bar and percentage display for the user. I\'m working to include a filtered list of activities for each day, strictly based on the baby\'s age group. I\'m also looking into how to distribute activities across all six developmental domains, making sure to avoid an excessive workload on any single day. I\'m checking the existing seed data, specifically the `/server/db/seed.ts` file, to identify where to insert and organize age-appropriate activities. I want to build a flexible plan, that dynamically creates a multi-day plan.\n\n\n**Refining Multi-Day Plans**\n\nI\'m now focused on refining the multi-day plans, specifically for the `6-9m` age group, ensuring it covers all six domains without repetition within a day or consecutive days. I\'m building idempotent migration for new and existing databases. I\'m adding a curriculum enrichment migration in `server/db/seed.ts` that runs after `seedDatabaseIfEmpty(db)`. I\'m focused on the ability to add new activities and multi-day plans without deleting user data.\n\n\n**Visualizing Activity States**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the visual states for activities. I\'m focusing on the distinct borders, badges, and icons for each state: Not started, In progress, Completed, Submitted for review, and Reviewed. Each state will have a unique visual identity, and corresponding CTAs. Also, I\'m working to integrate them into \"My Plan\" to give parents a clear view. I\'m prioritizing the design and functionality. I plan to ensure a good experience viewing today\'s and upcoming activities.\n\n\n**Implementing Activity Display**\n\nI\'m now focusing on displaying activities, specifically on Day 4. I\'m prioritizing preview cards with domain coverage, activity duration, and material information. I\'m also building the ability to view details. I\'m working on a persistent history section for previously completed activities, querying `activity_completions`, and preserving historical age-group snapshots. I\'m also including the ability to open activity details, which opens `ParentActivityStudio`, including full steps, materials, and notes. Also, I\'m integrating a way to resume unfinished activities.\n\n\n**Enforcing Completion Rules**\n\nI\'m now implementing rules around activity completion. I\'m focusing on ensuring daily plans don\'t duplicate activities, using database constraints and deduplication logic during plan generation. Also, I\'m working to persist snapshots of the age group and plan day number when an activity is completed. I\'m also now implementing the rule that a completed activity can\'t be marked as \"reviewed\" without an actual review record.\n\n\n**Enforcing Strict Statuses**\n\nI am now focusing on enforcing strict activity statuses. I\'m ensuring \'reviewed\' status is only assigned if there\'s a corresponding review record, both in the `upsertActivityCompletion` and `getJourneyForChild` calls.  I\'m making sure that the `/api/v1/completions` endpoint only accepts \'started\' or \'completed\' statuses. I am working to ensure data integrity through the query layer to derive effective activity statuses.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "GfsAa8-aLe-tz7IPiuiAsQ8"
