  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 1
    session_summary: "<summary>\n## 1. Task Overview\nWe are building **LittleSteps**, a parenting and early-childhood development web platform for mothers and caregivers of babies aged 0\342\200\22324 months (India-first, global-ready, responsive web now, API-ready for future Android/iOS).\n\nSteps completed so far:\n- **Step 0**: Architecture + initial SQLite (`better-sqlite3`, WAL mode, foreign keys ON) + Express (`/api/v1`) + React/Vite prototype.\n- **Step 1**: Reusable Design System (`/src/design-system/*`, 20 components, design tokens, showcase `/design-system`, 7 passing unit tests).\n- **Step 2**: Responsive 9-page public website (`/`, `/about`, `/how-it-works`, `/our-approach`, `/contact`, `/privacy`, `/terms`, `/login`, `/register`).\n- **Step 3**: Complete authentication (Registration, Login, Forgot password, Reset password with `session_version` revocation, Email verification, Logout) + 6-screen parent onboarding flow (`/src/pages/ParentOnboardingView.tsx`) + strict owner-only private profile photos.\n- **Step 4**: Responsive Parent Dashboard (`/src/pages/ParentDashboardView.tsx`, `/src/pages/parent/ParentActivityStudio.tsx`, `/src/pages/parent/ParentSecondaryViews.tsx`) with desktop left sidebar (`lg+`), compact mobile header + fixed bottom nav (`< lg`), all 7 Today sections, Activities library, Progress & Feedback, Parenting Guides, Notifications, Profile, and Settings.\n\n**CURRENT TASK \342\200\224 STEP 5 (IN PROGRESS): Build the structured daily learning journey (`My Plan`)**\n- **Main page: `My Plan`** must display:\n  - Current baby age\n  - Current learning week\n  - Today\'s date\n  - Daily completion progress\n  - List of activities for the day\n- **Activity distribution**: Cover the 6 development domains (Cognitive, Language & communication, Physical, Social & emotional, Sensory, Early independence & everyday skills) without forcing every domain into every single day (realistic daily workload of 2\342\200\2233 calm activities; expert-reviewed age-appropriate framing, without unverified claims).\n- **Activity card design**: Each card must show:\n  - Activity title\n  - Development domain\n  - Estimated duration\n  - Difficulty or preparation level (`no_prep` / `quick_setup` / `guided_prep`)\n  - Required materials\n  - Completion status with **clear visual differences for all 5 states**:\n    1. `Not started` (`not_started`)\n    2. `In progress` (`in_progress`)\n    3. `Completed` (`completed`)\n    4. `Submitted for review` (`submitted_for_review`)\n    5. `Reviewed` (`reviewed`)\n  - CTA to view/open/resume activity\n- **Journey experience**: Parent can:\n  - View today\'s activities\n  - View upcoming activities (subsequent days in their baby\'s age-group plan)\n  - View previously completed activities (persistent historical log)\n  - Open activity details (`ParentActivityStudio`)\n  - Resume an unfinished activity (`in_progress` highlight + direct Resume CTA)\n- **Mandatory Business Rules**:\n  1. Activities must be strictly filtered by the baby\'s age group.\n  2. Daily plans must not duplicate activities unexpectedly.\n  3. Completion must be persisted.\n  4. A completed activity must NOT be marked as reviewed unless a real `submission_reviews` record exists.\n  5. Changing the baby\'s age must NOT silently rewrite historical records.\n\n## 2. Progress\n### Completed in Step 5 (Batch 1 \342\200\224 Shared Types, Schema, Multi-Day Seed & Repository Business Rules DONE)\n1. `/src/shared/types.ts`:\n   - Added `ActivityPrepLevel = \'no_prep\' | \'quick_setup\' | \'guided_prep\'` and `JourneyDisplayStatus = \'not_started\' | \'in_progress\' | \'completed\' | \'submitted_for_review\' | \'reviewed\'`.\n   - Added `prepLevel` to `ActivitySummary`, `displayStatus` to `JourneyActivityItem` and `LastActivityResume`.\n   - Added `UpcomingPlanDay`, `CompletedHistoryItem`, and extended `TodayJourneyResponse` with `learningWeek` (`weekNumber`, `totalStageWeeks`, `stageLabel`, `todayDateIso`), `upcomingDays`, `inProgressItems`, and `completedHistory`.\n2. `/server/db/schema.ts`:\n   - Added idempotent column migrations: `activities.prep_level`, `activity_completions.age_group_id_snapshot`, `activity_completions.age_group_label_snapshot`.\n   - Added idempotent backfill SQL setting `age_group_id_snapshot` and `age_group_label_snapshot` for existing `activity_completions` rows.\n3. `/server/db/seed.ts`:\n   - Added `ensureStructuredDailyPlans(db)` called on every boot inside `seedDatabaseIfEmpty(db)` (so both existing `./data/littlesteps.db` and fresh DBs are enriched safely without wiping user data).\n   - Added 6 domain-balancing published activities (including `act_ext_6_9m_social` so `6-9m` covers all 6 domains across Days 1\342\200\2233 without unexpected duplicates) and Day 2 upcoming plans for `0-3m`, `3-6m`, `9-12m`, and `12-15m`, plus realistic `prep_level` values on all activities.\n4. `/server/repositories/index.ts`:\n   - Mapped `prepLevel` in `listActivities` and `getActivityDetail`.\n   - Enforced all 5 Step 5 business rules:\n     - `upsertDailyPlan`: deduplicates `activityIds` and only inserts activities matching `params.ageGroupId`.\n     - `getJourneyForChild`: deduplicates by `activity.id`, strictly skips any activity where `activity.ageGroupId !== child.activeAgeGroupId || activity.status !== \'published\'`, computes `learningWeek`, `upcomingDays`, `inProgressItems`, and `completedHistory`.\n     - `resolveEffectiveDisplayStatus`: returns `\'reviewed\'` ONLY if `latestSubmission?.review` exists, `\'submitted_for_review\'` ONLY if active `queued`/`in_review` submission exists, `\'completed\'`, `\'in_progress\'`, or `\'not_started\'`.\n     - `upsertActivityCompletion`: refuses to mark `\'reviewed\'` unless a real `submission_reviews` record exists; snapshots immutable `age_group_id_snapshot` and `age_group_label_snapshot` on insert so later baby DOB updates never rewrite history.\n     - `listCompletedHistoryForChild`: reads historical completions across all age groups using the preserved snapshot columns.\n\n### Still Remaining for Step 5 (Batch 2 \342\200\224 UI Components, API Guard & Verification)\n- **NOT YET EDITED**:\n  1. `/server/routes/api.ts`: Check `PUT /admin/daily-plans` (also validate no duplicate `activityIds` cleanly with a 400 error or deduplication) and `POST /completions` (already restricted to `z.enum([\'started\', \'completed\'])` so parents can never directly spoof `\'reviewed\'`).\n  2. `/src/design-system/ActivityCard.tsx` (or a dedicated Step 5 `JourneyActivityCard` in `/src/pages/parent/MyPlanSection.tsx` + enhanced `ActivityCard`): Update `ActivityCard` to optionally display `prepLevel` label (e.g., `No prep`, `2-min setup`, `Guided setup`) and visually differentiate all 5 `JourneyDisplayStatus` states (`not_started`, `in_progress`, `completed`, `submitted_for_review`, `reviewed`) with distinct card accent borders, tinted headers/footers, status icons, badges, and contextual CTA labels.\n  3. `/src/pages/parent/MyPlanSection.tsx` (NEW file to create): Full dedicated Step 5 **My Plan** experience displaying:\n     - **Header summary strip**: Current baby age (`Aarav \302\267 7 months \302\267 6\342\200\2239 months stage`), Current learning week (`Week X of Y \302\267 6\342\200\2239 months`), Today\'s readable date (`Friday, 20 Nov 2026`), and Daily completion progress (`X of Y completed` + linear/ring `ProgressIndicator`).\n     - **Resume Unfinished Activity callout** (when `journey.inProgressItems.length > 0`): prominent peach-accent card allowing one-tap resume of any unfinished `in_progress` activity.\n     - **Sub-navigation tabs** (using Design System `Tabs`):\n       - **Today\'s Activities** (with day switcher for available days in the age-group plan + 5-state visually distinct cards showing title, domain, duration, preparation level, materials, status, and CTA)\n       - **Upcoming Days** (`journey.upcomingDays` showing future scheduled dates, day focus note, domain tags, duration, preparation level, materials, and `\"Preview Activity\"` button)\n       - **Completed History** (`journey.completedHistory` showing all previously completed activities with completion date, reflection notes, preserved historical age-group badge e.g. `Completed in 6\342\200\2239 months`, real review score if reviewed, and `\"Revisit Activity\"` button \342\200\224 proving changing baby\'s age never rewrites historical records!)\n     - **Domain Coverage strip**: Quiet visual note showing how the week\'s plan distributes across the 6 development domains without overloading any single day (plus a calm note that activities are structured for age appropriateness, without making unverified clinical claims).\n  4. `/src/pages/ParentDashboardView.tsx`:\n     - Replace the simple inline `section === \'my-plan\'` block with `<MyPlanSection ... />`.\n     - Also upgrade `renderActivityCardForJourneyItem` on the `Today` view to pass `displayStatus` and `prepLevel` so both `Today` and `My Plan` share the exact same 5-state visual distinction and preparation level!\n  5. **NOT YET VERIFIED**: Step 5 Batch 1 edits have NOT yet been compiled, linted, restarted, or runtime-tested.\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n- **Design System exact prop names** (verified in previous turns):\n  - `ToastTone`: `\'info\' | \'success\' | \'warning\' | \'error\'` (NOT `\'danger\'`).\n  - `BadgeTone`: `\'sage\' | \'peach\' | \'lavender\' | \'neutral\' | \'danger\'` (NOT `\'cream\'`).\n  - `ButtonVariant`: `\'primary\' | \'secondary\' | \'subtle\' | \'danger\'` (NOT `\'ghost\'`).\n  - `AgeGroupSelector`: props are `selectedSlug`, `onSelect`, `label?`, `allowAll?`.\n  - `ConfirmDialog`: props are `open`, `onClose`, `onConfirm`, `title`, `message`, `confirmLabel?`, `destructive?`, `loading?`.\n  - `Tabs`: inspect `/src/design-system/Tabs.tsx` before using it in `MyPlanSection.tsx` so prop names match on the first try.\n- **Responsive Breakpoint Alignment**: Desktop sidebar is `hidden lg:flex`, `MobileBottomNav` is `lg:hidden` (fixed at `1024px` so tablet widths `768\342\200\2231023px` never lose navigation).\n- **Seeded Demo Accounts** (password `LittleSteps123!`):\n  - Parent: `meera@littlesteps.in` (child `ch_aarav_01`, Aarav, 7 months, `6-9m`, has 1 pre-seeded reviewed activity `act_05` Household Texture Basket with 88% instruction-match score)\n  - Reviewer: `ananya.reviewer@littlesteps.in`\n  - Admin: `kavita.admin@littlesteps.in`\n\n## 4. Errors & Fixes\n- **Resolved in Step 3**:\n  - `TopBarProps` required `activeNavId` and `onSelectNav` \342\200\224 fixed in `src/App.tsx`.\n  - `Badge tone=\"cream\"` and `Button variant=\"ghost\"` invalid \342\200\224 fixed to `tone=\"neutral\"` and `variant=\"subtle\"`.\n- **Resolved in Step 4**:\n  - `ToastTone` expects `\'error\'` (not `\'danger\'`), `AgeGroupSelector` expects `selectedSlug`/`onSelect`, `ConfirmDialog` expects `message`/`destructive` \342\200\224 all fixed in `ParentDashboardView.tsx` and `ParentSecondaryViews.tsx`.\n  - `MobileBottomNav` had `md:hidden` while desktop sidebar was `lg:flex` \342\200\224 aligned `MobileBottomNav` to `lg:hidden`.\n- No unresolved errors exist; Step 5 Batch 1 has not been compiled yet.\n\n## 5. Active Context\n- Server runs on port `3000` (`tsx server.ts`).\n- After completing Step 5 Batch 2 edits, `compile_applet` + `lint_applet` must pass cleanly, then `restart_dev_server` must run so Express applies the new `schema.ts` migrations (`prep_level`, `age_group_id_snapshot`, `age_group_label_snapshot`) and `ensureStructuredDailyPlans(db)` enrichment!\n- Notice `/src/design-system/__tests__/designSystem.test.tsx` tests `ActivityCard` \342\200\224 if we add optional props (`prepLevelLabel?`, `displayStatus?`, `secondaryMeta?`, `cardToneClass?`) to `ActivityCard`, keep them strictly optional with backward-compatible defaults so all 7 existing Design System tests keep passing unchanged!\n\n## 6. Next Steps (In Priority Order)\n1. **Inspect `/src/design-system/Tabs.tsx`** (one quick `view_file`) to confirm exact `Tabs` props before writing `MyPlanSection.tsx`.\n2. **Enhance `/src/design-system/ActivityCard.tsx`** with backward-compatible optional props:\n   - `prepLevelLabel?: string` (shown cleanly in the unboxed metadata line alongside domain, age group, and duration \342\200\224 e.g. `Sensory \302\267 6\342\200\2239 months \302\267 6 min \302\267 2-min setup`)\n   - `statusState?: JourneyDisplayStatus` (`\'not_started\' | \'in_progress\' | \'completed\' | \'submitted_for_review\' | \'reviewed\'`) applying distinct, warm Montessori visual styling for all 5 states (subtle left/top accent border, soft surface tint or badge tone, distinct icon: `CircleDashed` / `PlayCircle` / `CheckCircle2` / `UploadCloud` / `Award`, and primary vs secondary button hierarchy).\n3. **Create `/src/pages/parent/MyPlanSection.tsx`**:\n   - Displays all required **My Plan** elements:\n     - Current baby age (`child.displayName \302\267 child.ageInMonths months \302\267 child.ageGroupLabel`)\n     - Current learning week (`Week {learningWeek.weekNumber} of {learningWeek.totalStageWeeks} \302\267 {learningWeek.stageLabel}`)\n     - Today\'s formatted date (`learningWeek.todayDateIso` formatted cleanly e.g., `Fri, 20 Nov 2026`)\n     - Daily completion progress bar + ring (`completedTodayCount` of `totalTodayCount`, percentage `tabular-nums`)\n     - Resume unfinished activity card when `inProgressItems.length > 0`\n     - Tabs switching smoothly between:\n       1. **Today\'s Activities** (with day selector pills `Day 1`, `Day 2`, `Day 3`, focus note, and 5-state visually distinct `ActivityCard` grid)\n       2. **Upcoming Activities** (`upcomingDays` grouped by upcoming date/day with focus note, domain, duration, preparation level, materials, and `\"Preview Activity\"` CTA)\n       3. **Completed History** (`completedHistory` showing persisted completion date, reflection note, immutable stage snapshot badge `Completed in {ageGroupLabelSnapshot}`, status badge (`Completed` / `Submitted for review` / `Reviewed \302\267 XX%`), and `\"Revisit Activity\"` CTA)\n     - 5-state visual legend (quiet, compact, zero clutter) and realistic domain-balance note (highlighting that activities span the 6 domains across the week without forcing all 6 into one overwhelming day).\n4. **Update `/src/pages/ParentDashboardView.tsx`**:\n   - Import and render `<MyPlanSection ... />` for `section === \'my-plan\'`.\n   - Add helper `formatPrepLevel(level)` (`no_prep` \342\206\222 `\'No prep\'`, `quick_setup` \342\206\222 `\'2-min setup\'`, `guided_prep` \342\206\222 `\'Guided setup\'`) and pass `prepLevelLabel` + `statusState={item.displayStatus}` into `renderActivityCardForJourneyItem` (used in `Today` and `My Plan`), and update `ActivitiesLibrarySection` in `/src/pages/parent/ParentSecondaryViews.tsx` to also pass `prepLevelLabel`.\n5. **Tighten `/server/routes/api.ts`** on `PUT /admin/daily-plans` so duplicate `activityIds` in a request are rejected or cleanly prevented (and check `saveActivity` in `server/repositories/index.ts` accepts optional `prepLevel` if needed).\n6. **Verify Everything End-to-End**:\n   - Co-execute `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` (must pass with 0 TypeScript errors).\n   - Call `restart_dev_server` so Express runs new SQLite migrations and `ensureStructuredDailyPlans`.\n   - Run `npx tsx --test src/design-system/__tests__/designSystem.test.tsx` AND a live Step 5 end-to-end verification script against `http://localhost:3000/api/v1` testing ALL 5 business rules:\n     1. Activities in `GET /journey/:childId/today` all match `child.activeAgeGroupId` (zero cross-age leaks) and zero duplicate activity IDs in a day.\n     2. `learningWeek`, `upcomingDays`, `completedHistory`, and `prepLevel` are returned accurately; `6-9m` spans all 6 domains across Days 1\342\200\2233.\n     3. Marking an activity `\'started\'` appears in `inProgressItems` with `displayStatus === \'in_progress\'`.\n     4. Marking an activity `\'completed\'` persists across reload with `displayStatus === \'completed\'` \342\200\224 and NEVER becomes `\'reviewed\'` unless a real review exists! (Also verify attempting `status: \'reviewed\'` via `POST /completions` is rejected with `400`).\n     5. **Age-change immutability test**: Create a temporary child at `6-9m`, complete a `6-9m` activity, then `PATCH /children/:id` DOB so the child moves to `9-12m` \342\206\222 verify `GET /journey/:childId/today` now serves `9-12m` activities for Today & Upcoming Days while `completedHistory` STILL preserves the original `6-9m` completion record with `ageGroupLabelSnapshot === \'6\342\200\2239 months\'` unchanged! Clean up the temporary test child afterward so demo data stays spotless.\n\n## 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- Strict TypeScript (`strict: true`), Tailwind CSS v4 (`@import \"tailwindcss\";` in `src/index.css`), WCAG 2.2 AA contrast, `>= 44px` touch targets, warm Montessori editorial tokens (`sage`, `cream`, `offwhite`, `surface`, `peach`, `lavender`, `charcoal`, `muted`).\n- Never use `window.alert`, `window.confirm`, or `window.open`.\n- Never make unverified medical/clinical claims or invent testimonials/stats/certifications.\n- Keep the final response concise, scannable, and free of internal file paths or hype.\n</summary>"
