      text: "# STEP 0 \342\200\224 Understand LittleSteps and prepare the project\n\nAct as a senior product architect, UI/UX designer, and full-stack software engineer.\n\nI want to build a platform called **LittleSteps**.\n\n## Product vision\n\nLittleSteps is a parenting and early-childhood development platform that helps mothers and caregivers support their babies from birth to 2 years through structured, age-appropriate daily activities.\n\nThe platform should guide mothers step by step. It should not overwhelm them with too much information.\n\n## Target audience\n- Primary users: Mothers and caregivers.\n- Children\'s age: 0\342\200\22324 months.\n- Initial market: India.\n- Future market: Global.\n- Initial platform: Responsive web application.\n- Future platform: Android and iOS applications.\n\n## Core product concept\n\nThe platform follows a structured daily learning journey.\n\nEach day, a mother receives age-appropriate activities covering:\n1. Cognitive development\n2. Language and communication\n3. Physical development\n4. Social and emotional development\n5. Sensory development\n6. Early independence and everyday skills\n\nMothers can watch instructional videos, read simple guidelines, perform activities with their babies, and record or upload videos of their activities.\n\nA reviewer can assess whether the caregiver followed the activity instructions and provide feedback with a percentage-based instruction-match score.\n\nThis score must evaluate the caregiver\'s demonstrated activity execution, NOT the baby\'s intelligence, development level, or health.\n\n## Age groups\n\nCreate these age groups:\n- 0\342\200\2233 months\n- 3\342\200\2236 months\n- 6\342\200\2239 months\n- 9\342\200\22312 months\n- 12\342\200\22315 months\n- 15\342\200\22318 months\n- 18\342\200\22321 months\n- 21\342\200\22324 months\n\n## Your task\n\nBefore writing application code:\n\n1. Inspect the existing project and identify its current framework and dependencies.\n2. Recommend a scalable technical architecture.\n3. Define the main application modules.\n4. Define the database entities and relationships.\n5. Define parent, reviewer, and admin roles.\n6. Define the complete user journeys.\n7. Propose a maintainable folder structure.\n8. Identify security and privacy requirements, especially for children\'s videos.\n9. Break development into small, independently testable milestones.\n\n## Important rules\n\n- Do not start implementing the entire application.\n- Do not replace existing project configuration without explaining why.\n- Do not assume that mock functionality is production-ready.\n- Keep the architecture modular and easy to extend.\n- Use TypeScript and strict typing if the existing stack supports it.\n- Ask me before making major architectural decisions that cannot easily be reversed.\n\n## Expected output\n\nProvide the architecture, module breakdown, database design, folder structure, user journeys, and implementation plan.\n\nWait for my approval before starting Step 1."
    }
