  planner_response {
    response: "Step 5 \342\200\224 the structured daily learning journey (**My Plan**) \342\200\224 is implemented and verified.\n\n### What\342\200\231s Built\n- **Dedicated `My Plan` Experience**\n  - Header summary showing your baby\342\200\231s current age and stage, current learning week (`Week X of Y`), today\342\200\231s formatted date, and daily completion progress (both ring and linear progress indicators).\n  - **Resume Unfinished Activity** callout whenever any activity is currently `In progress`, allowing one-tap return to the activity guide.\n  - **Journey Tabs**:\n    - **Today\342\200\231s Activities**: Day selector across the baby\342\200\231s active age-group plan, focus note, balanced 2\342\200\2233 activity daily workload spanning all six development areas across the week without crowding all six into one day, and a quiet 5-state status guide.\n    - **Upcoming Days**: Multi-day forward look showing scheduled dates, day focus notes, activity domains, durations, preparation levels, required materials, and a **Preview Activity** action.\n    - **Completed History**: Persistent log of previously completed activities displaying completion dates, caregiver reflection notes, status/review scores, and preserved stage badges (e.g., *Completed in 6\342\200\2239 months*).\n- **5-State Visual Activity Cards**\n  - Updated activity cards display title, development domain, age stage, estimated duration, preparation level (*No prep*, *2-min setup*, *Guided setup*), and required household materials.\n  - Distinct visual treatments (accent border, subtle surface tint, icon, badge tone, and contextual button label) differentiate all five states: **Not started**, **In progress**, **Completed**, **Submitted for review**, and **Reviewed**.\n- **Enforced Business Rules (Backend + Database)**\n  - **Strict age-group filtering**: Daily and upcoming plans only serve published activities matching the baby\342\200\231s active age group.\n  - **No unexpected duplicates**: Both API validation and repository logic prevent duplicate activities within a daily plan.\n  - **Persistent completions & real review gating**: Completions persist in SQLite, direct attempts to mark an activity as `reviewed` without a real reviewer record are rejected, and `Reviewed` status is derived strictly from actual `submission_reviews` records.\n  - **Immutable history across age changes**: Updating a baby\342\200\231s date of birth refreshes Today and Upcoming plans to the new age group while preserving the original stage snapshot and notes on all past completions.\n\n### Verification\n- TypeScript build and lint (`tsc --noEmit`) passed with zero errors.\n- All 7 Design System unit tests passed.\n- End-to-end API tests confirmed age-group filtering, 6-domain multi-day coverage, duplicate rejection, in-progress resumption, review-status gating, and historical snapshot immutability when changing a child\342\200\231s age."
    message_id: "9hIBa5CVDqvQz7IP-OmJyQs"
    modified_response: "Step 5 \342\200\224 the structured daily learning journey (**My Plan**) \342\200\224 is implemented and verified.\n\n### What\342\200\231s Built\n- **Dedicated `My Plan` Experience**\n  - Header summary showing your baby\342\200\231s current age and stage, current learning week (`Week X of Y`), today\342\200\231s formatted date, and daily completion progress (both ring and linear progress indicators).\n  - **Resume Unfinished Activity** callout whenever any activity is currently `In progress`, allowing one-tap return to the activity guide.\n  - **Journey Tabs**:\n    - **Today\342\200\231s Activities**: Day selector across the baby\342\200\231s active age-group plan, focus note, balanced 2\342\200\2233 activity daily workload spanning all six development areas across the week without crowding all six into one day, and a quiet 5-state status guide.\n    - **Upcoming Days**: Multi-day forward look showing scheduled dates, day focus notes, activity domains, durations, preparation levels, required materials, and a **Preview Activity** action.\n    - **Completed History**: Persistent log of previously completed activities displaying completion dates, caregiver reflection notes, status/review scores, and preserved stage badges (e.g., *Completed in 6\342\200\2239 months*).\n- **5-State Visual Activity Cards**\n  - Updated activity cards display title, development domain, age stage, estimated duration, preparation level (*No prep*, *2-min setup*, *Guided setup*), and required household materials.\n  - Distinct visual treatments (accent border, subtle surface tint, icon, badge tone, and contextual button label) differentiate all five states: **Not started**, **In progress**, **Completed**, **Submitted for review**, and **Reviewed**.\n- **Enforced Business Rules (Backend + Database)**\n  - **Strict age-group filtering**: Daily and upcoming plans only serve published activities matching the baby\342\200\231s active age group.\n  - **No unexpected duplicates**: Both API validation and repository logic prevent duplicate activities within a daily plan.\n  - **Persistent completions & real review gating**: Completions persist in SQLite, direct attempts to mark an activity as `reviewed` without a real reviewer record are rejected, and `Reviewed` status is derived strictly from actual `submission_reviews` records.\n  - **Immutable history across age changes**: Updating a baby\342\200\231s date of birth refreshes Today and Upcoming plans to the new age group while preserving the original stage snapshot and notes on all past completions.\n\n### Verification\n- TypeScript build and lint (`tsc --noEmit`) passed with zero errors.\n- All 7 Design System unit tests passed.\n- End-to-end API tests confirmed age-group filtering, 6-domain multi-day coverage, duplicate rejection, in-progress resumption, review-status gating, and historical snapshot immutability when changing a child\342\200\231s age."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
    thinking_signature: "\022\354\002\n\351\002\001i\024}\023\251s}l\\\375y\326H\332\216(E\034\351x\230u\334\364\312Dm\262\r\3500\"\263\251\v\306\2325\303(\207\362%\372r\343\373\377\304\243\3024\214\346\343\304)P\b*\222\214\234\232\000:\241\373F\n\000\352\275=?\3437iop\"LB\234\374\235p\241Hl\335\177\257\346\202L\002\256\346\360\226\316\210N\257\261\342\376\006\220\245\211A@+\a\213n\t\030\214\245W\374{\355\rf\n\024\v\004 i\t\271\350`\277\033\252\375\345.\326\362V\235bz d\321f-*\314\274{\362\320i3\301\366\367\003\251y\362;\372\307hx \277c\324l}\271\350\346\243\327K\004kR\330\321\203D\205\250)\277\243HE\207\v&\000\264\336\214\224Dr3\212\005\347<\364F\346\262\003\006!(R\3771\305\324v\324\267%\264\327\273m\231[JN\203H\376u\271m\214zR\266C\202A\253bNP\306z`1Kv\361\367\016=\206\305\347\336\203\224\237\256\233]\250@\031\241Q-\237j\244l\356\235\244C\361\333\002\302\303;\257\362;\214OJ\253\234\234\021\373\312)\237\372\221\351yV\211\'M!@\033\300\303\345\026\030\217\263,v\256 \350=\234\362\242[2\223\250N\371\272\370\342Li\r\272.\n\205o\221\224\240$"
