  user_input {
    user_response: "# STEP 7 \342\200\224 Build caregiver video recording and submission\n\nBuild the video submission feature.\n\nThis is an important differentiator of LittleSteps.\n\nA mother should be able to record herself performing an activity with her baby or upload an existing video.\n\n## User journey\n\n1. Parent opens an activity.\n2. Parent reads the instructions.\n3. Parent performs the activity.\n4. Parent clicks \"Record Activity\" or \"Upload Video\".\n5. Parent records or selects a video.\n6. Parent previews the video.\n7. Parent can replace or remove it.\n8. Parent provides an optional note.\n9. Parent confirms consent.\n10. Parent submits for review.\n\n## UI requirements\n\nCreate a simple upload page with:\n- Large recording button.\n- Upload from device option.\n- Video preview.\n- File size and format guidance.\n- Upload progress.\n- Cancel and retry actions.\n- Optional notes field.\n- Consent checkbox.\n- Submit button.\n\nDo not request unnecessary permissions.\n\n## Submission states\n\n- Draft.\n- Uploading.\n- Submitted.\n- Under review.\n- Reviewed.\n- Changes requested.\n- Failed.\n\nShow clear status messages.\n\n## Data requirements\n\nEvery submission must be linked to:\n- Parent ID.\n- Child ID.\n- Activity ID.\n- Activity version.\n- Submission timestamp.\n- Video storage reference.\n- Consent record.\n- Review status.\n\n## Security requirements\n\nThis feature handles videos of children.\n\nTherefore:\n- Never make child videos publicly accessible.\n- Use private object storage in production.\n- Use short-lived signed URLs.\n- Enforce ownership and reviewer authorization on the server.\n- Validate file type, size, and content.\n- Provide secure deletion workflows.\n- Do not store real child videos in insecure public folders or local mock storage.\n\nIf production video storage is not configured, implement a clearly labelled demo mode and do not pretend that uploads are securely stored.\n\n## Expected output\n\nA functional and privacy-conscious video submission workflow, including upload progress and clear submission states."
    items {
      text: "# STEP 7 \342\200\224 Build caregiver video recording and submission\n\nBuild the video submission feature.\n\nThis is an important differentiator of LittleSteps.\n\nA mother should be able to record herself performing an activity with her baby or upload an existing video.\n\n## User journey\n\n1. Parent opens an activity.\n2. Parent reads the instructions.\n3. Parent performs the activity.\n4. Parent clicks \"Record Activity\" or \"Upload Video\".\n5. Parent records or selects a video.\n6. Parent previews the video.\n7. Parent can replace or remove it.\n8. Parent provides an optional note.\n9. Parent confirms consent.\n10. Parent submits for review.\n\n## UI requirements\n\nCreate a simple upload page with:\n- Large recording button.\n- Upload from device option.\n- Video preview.\n- File size and format guidance.\n- Upload progress.\n- Cancel and retry actions.\n- Optional notes field.\n- Consent checkbox.\n- Submit button.\n\nDo not request unnecessary permissions.\n\n## Submission states\n\n- Draft.\n- Uploading.\n- Submitted.\n- Under review.\n- Reviewed.\n- Changes requested.\n- Failed.\n\nShow clear status messages.\n\n## Data requirements\n\nEvery submission must be linked to:\n- Parent ID.\n- Child ID.\n- Activity ID.\n- Activity version.\n- Submission timestamp.\n- Video storage reference.\n- Consent record.\n- Review status.\n\n## Security requirements\n\nThis feature handles videos of children.\n\nTherefore:\n- Never make child videos publicly accessible.\n- Use private object storage in production.\n- Use short-lived signed URLs.\n- Enforce ownership and reviewer authorization on the server.\n- Validate file type, size, and content.\n- Provide secure deletion workflows.\n- Do not store real child videos in insecure public folders or local mock storage.\n\nIf production video storage is not configured, implement a clearly labelled demo mode and do not pretend that uploads are securely stored.\n\n## Expected output\n\nA functional and privacy-conscious video submission workflow, including upload progress and clear submission states."
    }
  }
}
