  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Step 7 Threats**\n\nI\'m diving into a threat model and gap analysis specifically for \"Build caregiver video recording and submission\" (STEP 7). I\'m looking at all the requirements and assessing potential vulnerabilities. My focus is on internal threats to the system. I\'m aiming for a comprehensive assessment.\n\n\n**Defining Data Requirements**\n\nI\'ve been examining the data requirements for each video submission, specifically focusing on what needs to be linked. I\'ve confirmed `parentUserId`, `childId`, `activityId`, and timestamp are already present. However, I found a gap: the `activity_version` is missing! I\'m planning to address this by adding `activity_version` to both the `activities` and `video_submissions` tables, with a default of 1, incremented on activity updates. We can then add a `storage_provider` column, also.\n\n\n**Refining Data Linkages**\n\nI\'m now focusing on linking key data points to our video submissions. I\'ve partially linked the consent record, noting that the `recordUserConsent` function needs to return the consent ID and that the `video_submissions` table needs a foreign key. I also plan to add `consentRecordId` and `consentGrantedAt` to the `VideoSubmissionSummary`. I\'m also mapping review states to a more human-readable `submissionState`.\n\n\n**Defining Submission States**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the submission states. There\'s \"reviewed\" with feedback, \"changes requested\" for resubmissions (with clear communication to the parent), and \"failed\" for upload issues (with retry and cancel actions). The server will track these states as `reviewed`, `resubmit_requested`, and `failed`, respectively. The parent should always see their clip status.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Prioritizing Storage Mode Clarity**\n\nI\'m tackling a critical security requirement: honest disclosure of demo storage mode. I\'m focusing on adding a `storage.getStorageStatus()` function that will provide detailed storage mode information. This includes the mode (production or demo), provider label, configuration status, and any necessary warnings. I\'ll be inspecting `server/storage/mediaStorage.ts` and `.env.example` to implement this. This will expose the real status to the user.\n\n\n**Clarifying Storage Status**\n\nI\'m working on clarifying the storage status in the UI, particularly for the demo mode. The logic checks `process.env.OBJECT_STORAGE_BUCKET` and `process.env.OBJECT_STORAGE_PROVIDER` to determine if production cloud object storage (like GCS or S3) is configured. Since it\'s not in the local SQLite prototype, the mode is `demo_local_vault` and `isProductionConfigured` is `false`. I plan to expose this via `GET /api/v1/submissions/storage-status` (authenticated), including `storageMode` in submission responses. The UI, specifically `VideoCaptureUploader` and `SecureVideoPlayer`, will then display an honest \"Demo Mode Notice\" when `mode === \'demo_local_vault\'` to avoid misleading users.\n\n\n**Strengthening Security Measures**\n\nI\'m now focused on reinforcing the existing security architecture. I\'m verifying path confinement by hardening the `resolveSafePath` function with a strict trailing separator check. I\'m also confirming that `private_media/` remains completely isolated. I\'m reviewing the implementation of short-lived HMAC-SHA256 signed stream URLs, ensuring RBAC re-verification. I am also working on ephemeral CSPRNG fallbacks for session secrets. I\'ll replace hardcoded dev fallback strings with random bytes.\n\n\n**Enhancing Security Protocols**\n\nI\'m now implementing crucial security updates. I\'ve upgraded the JWT signing key generation in `server/security/crypto.ts` with `crypto.randomBytes(32).toString(\'hex\')` to replace literal fallback strings. I\'m also adding file type validation, size checks, and binary magic-byte verification to ensure video integrity. Finally, I\'ve confirmed that parents can only control their videos, and reviewers can manage submissions in the review queue. I\'m also preparing secure deletion workflows.\n\n\n**Defining Feedback Persistence**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the preservation of written coaching feedback, specifically within the new UI. I\'ve pinpointed the key UI updates needed for `ParentActivityStudio.tsx` and `VideoCaptureUploader.tsx`. My focus is on ensuring a smooth user experience and secure, minimal permissions for video recording and upload. I\'m making it so that the user grants the requested permissions only at the point of video capture.\n\n\n**Refining UI Design**\n\nI\'m now overhauling the user interface of `VideoCaptureUploader.tsx`. My current focus is ensuring all elements required for video submission are present. This means implementing a clear Submission Status Header, an honest Storage Mode Banner in the demo, and a Large \"Record Activity\" button. I\'m updating Step-0 class names to the Step 1 Design System tokens to make the UI consistent.\n\n\n**Designing Submission Controls**\n\nI\'m now detailing the video submission components. I\'ve added clear file size and format guidance next to the picker. I\'ve included a video preview with native controls, duration, file-size readout, and \"Replace Video\" and \"Remove Video\" buttons. I\'ve also incorporated an optional caregiver notes field with placeholder text and an explicit consent checkbox linked to a consent record.\n\n\n"
