  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Implementing Parallel Processes**\n\nI\'m making good progress! I\'ve decided to implement Batch 1, focusing on backend, schema, security, storage mode, and shared types in parallel. I\'ll start with `/src/shared/types.ts` to add `VideoStorageMode` and `VideoStorageStatusResponse`. This feels like a great way to kick things off.\n\n\n**Extending Data Structures**\n\nI\'m now extending data structures and database schemas. I\'ve added a `version: number` field to `ActivitySummary` and incorporated all the necessary linked fields to `VideoSubmissionSummary` as per Step 7 requirements, including fields for parent user, activity version, storage reference, storage mode, consent, and change request notes. Also, I\'ve added idempotent column migrations to the database schema.\n\n\n**Strengthening Security Measures**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing security enhancements. I\'m adding CSPRNG to `/VIDEO_TOKEN_SECRET` with an in-memory fallback, and strengthening `validateVideoMagicBytes` to prevent MIME spoofing. This is crucial for maintaining data integrity. I\'m also bolstering `resolveSafePath` with `path.resolve` and a boundary check in `/server/storage/mediaStorage.ts`.\n\n\n\n**Refining Data Retrieval**\n\nI\'m now refining data retrieval and API endpoints. I\'ve updated `listActivities` and `getActivityDetail` to map the `version` field and increment it during updates. I\'ve also updated `createVideoSubmission` to store `activityVersion`, `storageProvider`, and `consentRecordId`. Now, I\'m updating `mapSubmissionRow` and related SQL joins to include key fields like `parentUserId`, `activityVersion`, and `consentGrantedAt`, and I\'ve added a new endpoint for reviewers to request changes with a helpful note. Finally, I\'ve added a storage status endpoint and graceful error handling for file uploads, including returning a `413` status for files exceeding the size limit.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "2BUBa-2FPMSOjMcPuM2aoQ8"
