  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Implementing Parallel Processes**\n\nI\'m currently focused on parallelizing the implementation of Batch 2, specifically the frontend API and the caregiver video submission workflow. I\'ve begun by updating `/src/lib/api.ts` to include `getVideoStorageStatus()`, which will call `GET /api/v1/submissions/storage-status`. I\'m also upgrading `uploadSubmission`.\n\n\n**Refining Component Interactions**\n\nI\'m now integrating the updated API methods, particularly `getVideoStorageStatus()`, into `/src/components/VideoCaptureUploader.tsx`. I\'m working on the Step 7 rebuild with the Montessori Design System components. I\'ve added support for `initialMode` to streamline the user flow and minimize prompts. Finally, I\'m implementing the \"Honest Demo Storage Mode Banner\" using the fetched `getVideoStorageStatus()`.\n\n\n**Defining Submission Status States**\n\nI\'m now detailing the user interface requirements, specifically focusing on a 7-state submission status header and step banner. These states are: Draft, Uploading, Submitted, Under Review, Reviewed, Changes Requested, and Failed. Each state will have a corresponding visual representation and associated actions for the user. I\'m also planning the design for the record activity button, which must be large and touch-friendly.\n\n\n**Designing Submission Components**\n\nI\'m currently structuring the video submission components. I\'ve defined upload options, including \"Upload from Device\" and \"Create Demo Clip\" buttons, along with a file size/format guide. I\'m also implementing the video preview, optional notes field, explicit consent checkbox, and the \"Submit for Review\" action. A confirmation stage will show key metadata.\n\n\n**Structuring Activity Interactions**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the initial activity screen. I\'m adding a welcoming layout with a clear call to action, providing options to either record or upload a video. If a submission exists, I\'ll present a Submission Status Card displaying server states and metadata, including the reviewer\'s feedback if changes are needed, and a button to re-record or re-upload. I\'ll also add a confirmation for video deletion.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "yBYBa-qOA765sOIPwfLT-Ao"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_4033236578715606332"
      name: "multi_replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"Description\":\"Add video storage status endpoint, abortable upload progress support, and reviewer change-request client method to api.ts.\", \"Instruction\":\"Import VideoStorageStatusResponse; add getVideoStorageStatus; add optional AbortSignal to uploadSubmissionVideo; add requestSubmissionChanges.\", \"ReplacementChunks\":[{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"EndLine\":23, \"ReplacementContent\":\"  UserProfile,\\n  UserRole,\\n  VideoStorageStatusResponse,\\n  VideoSubmissionSummary,\\n} from \'../shared/types\';\", \"StartLine\":19, \"TargetContent\":\"  UserProfile,\\n  UserRole,\\n  VideoSubmissionSummary,\\n} from \'../shared/types\';\"}, {\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"EndLine\":260, \"ReplacementContent\":\"  // Submissions & Private Video Streaming\\n  getVideoStorageStatus: () =>\\n    requestJson<VideoStorageStatusResponse>(\'/api/v1/submissions/storage-status\'),\\n\\n  uploadSubmissionVideo: (\\n    params: {\\n      childId: string;\\n      activityId: string;\\n      file: Blob;\\n      filename: string;\\n      durationSeconds: number;\\n      caregiverNotes: string;\\n      consentConfirmed: boolean;\\n    },\\n    onProgress?: (percent: number) => void,\\n    signal?: AbortSignal\\n  ): Promise<{ submission: VideoSubmissionSummary; storageStatus?: VideoStorageStatusResponse }> =>\\n    new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\\n      if (signal?.aborted) {\\n        reject(new ApiError(\'Upload cancelled.\', 499));\\n        return;\\n      }\\n\\n      const formData = new FormData();\\n      formData.append(\'video\', params.file, params.filename);\\n      formData.append(\'childId\', params.childId);\\n      formData.append(\'activityId\', params.activityId);\\n      formData.append(\'durationSeconds\', String(params.durationSeconds));\\n      formData.append(\'caregiverNotes\', params.caregiverNotes);\\n      formData.append(\'consentConfirmed\', params.consentConfirmed ? \'true\' : \'false\');\\n\\n      const xhr = new XMLHttpRequest();\\n      xhr.open(\'POST\', \'/api/v1/submissions\', true);\\n      xhr.withCredentials = true;\\n\\n      const handleAbort = () => {\\n        xhr.abort();\\n      };\\n      signal?.addEventListener(\'abort\', handleAbort, { once: true });\\n\\n      const cleanup = () => {\\n        signal?.removeEventListener(\'abort\', handleAbort);\\n      };\\n\\n      xhr.upload.onprogress = (ev) => {\\n        if (ev.lengthComputable && onProgress) {\\n          onProgress(Math.min(99, Math.round((ev.loaded / ev.total) * 100)));\\n        }\\n      };\\n\\n      xhr.onload = () => {\\n        cleanup();\\n        try {\\n          const parsed = JSON.parse(xhr.responseText || \'{}\') as {\\n            submission?: VideoSubmissionSummary;\\n            storageStatus?: VideoStorageStatusResponse;\\n            error?: string;\\n          };\\n          if (xhr.status >= 200 && xhr.status < 300 && parsed.submission) {\\n            onProgress?.(100);\\n            resolve({ submission: parsed.submission, storageStatus: parsed.storageStatus });\\n          } else {\\n            reject(new ApiError(parsed.error || \'Upload failed. Please try again.\', xhr.status));\\n          }\\n        } catch {\\n          reject(new ApiError(\'Unexpected server response during upload.\', xhr.status));\\n        }\\n      };\\n      xhr.onabort = () => {\\n        cleanup();\\n        reject(new ApiError(\'Upload cancelled. Your clip is still ready if you want to retry.\', 499));\\n      };\\n      xhr.onerror = () => {\\n        cleanup();\\n        reject(new ApiError(\'Network error while uploading video. Please check your connection and retry.\', 0));\\n      };\\n      xhr.send(formData);\\n    }),\", \"StartLine\":209, \"TargetContent\":\"  // Submissions & Private Video Streaming\\n  uploadSubmissionVideo: (\\n    params: {\\n      childId: string;\\n      activityId: string;\\n      file: Blob;\\n      filename: string;\\n      durationSeconds: number;\\n      caregiverNotes: string;\\n      consentConfirmed: boolean;\\n    },\\n    onProgress?: (percent: number) => void\\n  ): Promise<{ submission: VideoSubmissionSummary }> =>\\n    new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\\n      const formData = new FormData();\\n      formData.append(\'video\', params.file, params.filename);\\n      formData.append(\'childId\', params.childId);\\n      formData.append(\'activityId\', params.activityId);\\n      formData.append(\'durationSeconds\', String(params.durationSeconds));\\n      formData.append(\'caregiverNotes\', params.caregiverNotes);\\n      formData.append(\'consentConfirmed\', params.consentConfirmed ? \'true\' : \'false\');\\n\\n      const xhr = new XMLHttpRequest();\\n      xhr.open(\'POST\', \'/api/v1/submissions\', true);\\n      xhr.withCredentials = true;\\n\\n      xhr.upload.onprogress = (ev) => {\\n        if (ev.lengthComputable && onProgress) {\\n          onProgress(Math.round((ev.loaded / ev.total) * 100));\\n        }\\n      };\\n\\n      xhr.onload = () => {\\n        try {\\n          const parsed = JSON.parse(xhr.responseText || \'{}\') as {\\n            submission?: VideoSubmissionSummary;\\n            error?: string;\\n          };\\n          if (xhr.status >= 200 && xhr.status < 300 && parsed.submission) {\\n            resolve({ submission: parsed.submission });\\n          } else {\\n            reject(new ApiError(parsed.error || \'Upload failed.\', xhr.status));\\n          }\\n        } catch {\\n          reject(new ApiError(\'Unexpected server response during upload.\', xhr.status));\\n        }\\n      };\\n      xhr.onerror = () => reject(new ApiError(\'Network error while uploading video.\', 0));\\n      xhr.send(formData);\\n    }),\"}, {\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"EndLine\":298, \"ReplacementContent\":\"        method: \'POST\',\\n        body: JSON.stringify(payload),\\n      }\\n    ),\\n  requestSubmissionChanges: (submissionId: string, note: string) =>\\n    requestJson<{ ok: boolean; detail: ReviewerSubmissionDetail | null }>(\\n      `/api/v1/reviewer/submissions/${submissionId}/request-changes`,\\n      {\\n        method: \'POST\',\\n        body: JSON.stringify({ note }),\\n      }\\n    ),\", \"StartLine\":292, \"TargetContent\":\"        method: \'POST\',\\n        body: JSON.stringify(payload),\\n      }\\n    ),\"}], \"TargetFile\":\"/src/lib/api.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Updating frontend submission API methods\", \"toolSummary\":\"Update frontend API client\"}"
