  planner_response {
    response: "Step 7 \342\200\224 caregiver video recording, upload, and submission \342\200\224 is built and verified.\n\n### What\342\200\231s Built\n- **End-to-End Caregiver Recording & Upload Flow**\n  - From any activity detail view, parents can tap **Record Activity** or **Upload Video** right after completing the step-by-step instructions.\n  - **Minimal permissions**: Camera and microphone access are requested only when the parent explicitly taps **Record Activity** (with automatic video-only fallback if a microphone is unavailable), and tracks are released immediately when recording stops or cancels.\n  - **Upload studio UI**: Large **Record Activity** button, **Upload from Device** option (`MP4`, `WebM`, `MOV` up to `50 MB` and `2 minutes`), clear format/size guidance, a **3-second demo sample clip** generator for camera-free testing, native video preview with **Replace Video** and **Remove** actions, optional caregiver notes (`600` chars), explicit consent checkbox, live **Upload Progress** bar with **Cancel Upload** (aborting the active transfer) and **Retry Upload** on failure, and **Submit for Review**.\n- **All 7 Submission States**\n  - Clearly labelled status badges and plain-language guidance for **Draft**, **Uploading**, **Submitted**, **Under review**, **Reviewed**, **Changes requested** (displaying the reviewer\342\200\231s request note and a quick **Submit Updated Clip** action), and **Failed** (preserving the selected clip and notes for retry).\n- **Complete Data Linkage**\n  - Every submission records and returns its linked **Parent ID**, **Child ID**, **Activity ID**, snapshotted **Activity Version** (auto-incremented when activities are updated), **Submission Timestamp**, opaque **Storage Reference**, **Consent Record ID & Timestamp**, and **Review Status**.\n- **Transparent Demo Storage Disclosure**\n  - Because production cloud object storage (GCS/S3) is not configured in this local prototype, the server explicitly reports **Demo Storage Mode** and the upload studio displays a clear banner advising caregivers to use the 3-second test clip or non-sensitive sample videos until private cloud object storage is configured.\n\n### Verified Safeguards\n- **Strict file and content validation**: Uploads enforce non-empty files, a `50 MB` ceiling, allowed video types (`MP4`, `WebM`, `MOV`), and matching binary container signatures on the server so disguised or mismatched files are rejected.\n- **Private access and signed links**: Uploaded clips are stored strictly outside public web directories with confined file paths, streamed only via short-lived (5-minute) signed URLs with `no-store` and `nosniff` headers, and every stream and deletion is logged.\n- **Server-side ownership and deletion controls**: Protected routes verify sign-in and role permissions\342\200\224only the owning parent and authorized reviewers can request a stream token, reviewers cannot delete clips, and parents can permanently delete their uploaded video at any time (immediately returning `410 Gone` for future stream requests while keeping written feedback intact).\n\n### Verification\n- Build and TypeScript lint (`tsc --noEmit`) passed cleanly with zero errors.\n- End-to-end API checks passed for storage-status disclosure, consent enforcement, binary/MIME rejection, linked metadata persistence, short-lived signed streaming, role access control, reviewer change requests, and permanent video deletion."
    message_id: "ARkBa9DHJ7qt1MkPubqp4AY"
    modified_response: "Step 7 \342\200\224 caregiver video recording, upload, and submission \342\200\224 is built and verified.\n\n### What\342\200\231s Built\n- **End-to-End Caregiver Recording & Upload Flow**\n  - From any activity detail view, parents can tap **Record Activity** or **Upload Video** right after completing the step-by-step instructions.\n  - **Minimal permissions**: Camera and microphone access are requested only when the parent explicitly taps **Record Activity** (with automatic video-only fallback if a microphone is unavailable), and tracks are released immediately when recording stops or cancels.\n  - **Upload studio UI**: Large **Record Activity** button, **Upload from Device** option (`MP4`, `WebM`, `MOV` up to `50 MB` and `2 minutes`), clear format/size guidance, a **3-second demo sample clip** generator for camera-free testing, native video preview with **Replace Video** and **Remove** actions, optional caregiver notes (`600` chars), explicit consent checkbox, live **Upload Progress** bar with **Cancel Upload** (aborting the active transfer) and **Retry Upload** on failure, and **Submit for Review**.\n- **All 7 Submission States**\n  - Clearly labelled status badges and plain-language guidance for **Draft**, **Uploading**, **Submitted**, **Under review**, **Reviewed**, **Changes requested** (displaying the reviewer\342\200\231s request note and a quick **Submit Updated Clip** action), and **Failed** (preserving the selected clip and notes for retry).\n- **Complete Data Linkage**\n  - Every submission records and returns its linked **Parent ID**, **Child ID**, **Activity ID**, snapshotted **Activity Version** (auto-incremented when activities are updated), **Submission Timestamp**, opaque **Storage Reference**, **Consent Record ID & Timestamp**, and **Review Status**.\n- **Transparent Demo Storage Disclosure**\n  - Because production cloud object storage (GCS/S3) is not configured in this local prototype, the server explicitly reports **Demo Storage Mode** and the upload studio displays a clear banner advising caregivers to use the 3-second test clip or non-sensitive sample videos until private cloud object storage is configured.\n\n### Verified Safeguards\n- **Strict file and content validation**: Uploads enforce non-empty files, a `50 MB` ceiling, allowed video types (`MP4`, `WebM`, `MOV`), and matching binary container signatures on the server so disguised or mismatched files are rejected.\n- **Private access and signed links**: Uploaded clips are stored strictly outside public web directories with confined file paths, streamed only via short-lived (5-minute) signed URLs with `no-store` and `nosniff` headers, and every stream and deletion is logged.\n- **Server-side ownership and deletion controls**: Protected routes verify sign-in and role permissions\342\200\224only the owning parent and authorized reviewers can request a stream token, reviewers cannot delete clips, and parents can permanently delete their uploaded video at any time (immediately returning `410 Gone` for future stream requests while keeping written feedback intact).\n\n### Verification\n- Build and TypeScript lint (`tsc --noEmit`) passed cleanly with zero errors.\n- End-to-end API checks passed for storage-status disclosure, consent enforcement, binary/MIME rejection, linked metadata persistence, short-lived signed streaming, role access control, reviewer change requests, and permanent video deletion."
