  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 2
    session_summary: "<summary>\n## 1. Task Overview\nWe are building **LittleSteps**, a parenting and early-childhood development web platform (0\342\200\22324 months, India-first, global-ready) using React + Vite + Tailwind CSS v4 + Express (`/api/v1`) + SQLite (`better-sqlite3`, WAL mode, foreign keys ON).\n\nCompleted previous steps (all built, linted, and E2E verified):\n- **Steps 0\342\200\2234**: Architecture, reusable warm Montessori Design System (`/src/design-system/*`, 7 passing unit tests), 9-page public website, full auth + 6-screen parent onboarding, and responsive Parent Dashboard.\n- **Step 5**: Structured daily learning journey (`My Plan`, `/src/pages/parent/MyPlanSection.tsx`, 5-state visual `ActivityCard`, multi-day plans across 6 domains, immutable stage history on age change).\n- **Step 7**: Caregiver video recording & upload workflow (`/src/components/VideoCaptureUploader.tsx`, `/src/pages/parent/ParentActivityStudio.tsx`, `/src/components/SecureVideoPlayer.tsx`, `GET /api/v1/submissions/storage-status` honest Demo Storage Mode disclosure, MIME-matched magic-byte validation, activity version & consent record linkage, abortable XHR progress, retry, secure deletion).\n\n**CURRENT TASK \342\200\224 STEP 8 (IN PROGRESS): Build the reviewer dashboard**\nAuthorized reviewers assess whether the caregiver followed the instructions for a particular activity (NEVER the baby\'s intelligence, health, or developmental level).\n\nRequired deliverables:\n1. **Reviewer Dashboard**:\n   - Summary KPIs: Total pending submissions (`queued`), Submissions under review (`in_review`), Completed reviews (`reviewed`), Recently submitted videos.\n   - Review queue displaying: **Parent reference** (privacy-minimized opaque reference, never email/phone/legal name), **Activity name**, **Submission date**, **Age group**, **Review status**, **Priority** (`high` / `normal` / `low`).\n2. **Review Details Page** displaying all 7 items:\n   1. Activity title and version (`vN`)\n   2. Original activity instructions (numbered steps + required materials)\n   3. Safety guidelines\n   4. Submitted video (`SecureVideoPlayer`)\n   5. Optional parent note\n   6. Evaluation checklist (per-activity weighted rubric)\n   7. Reviewer comments\n3. **Evaluation System & Exact Score Formula**:\n   - Per-activity weighted rubric configured by content admin / authorized reviewer.\n   - 4 ratings:\n     - `Met` (`\'met\'`) = `1`\n     - `Partially met` (`\'partially_met\'`) = `0.5`\n     - `Not met` (`\'not_met\'`, plus legacy `\'not_observed\'` mapped to `0`) = `0`\n     - `Not assessable` (`\'not_assessable\'`) = excluded from applicable weight, with a required explanation!\n   - Exact formula: `Instruction Match Percentage = (Weighted points earned / Applicable weighted points) \303\227 100`.\n   - If insufficient evidence (explicitly marked Not Assessable, or `applicableTotal <= 0`, or `applicableTotal < maxTotal * 0.5`), mark as **\"Not Assessable\"** (`isAssessable: false`, `instructionMatchScorePct: null`) instead of generating a misleading percentage.\n4. **All 5 Review Submission Actions**:\n   - Save a draft (`draft`) \342\200\224 saved privately, NOT visible to parent until published.\n   - Submit / update evaluation (`publish`) \342\200\224 computes score server-side and publishes to parent.\n   - Add feedback (criteria-wise explanations, positive observations, areas to improve, reviewer comments).\n   - Request another submission (`resubmit_requested` with explanation note).\n   - Mark evidence insufficient (`not_assessable` published outcome with clear reason).\n5. **Parent Result View** (in `ProgressAndFeedbackSection` & `ParentActivityStudio`):\n   - Instruction-match percentage (where assessable) OR **\"Not Assessable\"** with reason.\n   - Criteria-wise feedback (including `Not met` and `Not assessable` explanations).\n   - Positive observations (`strengthsNote`).\n   - Areas to improve (`coachingTip`).\n   - Reviewer comments (`reviewerComments`).\n   - Review date (`submittedAt`).\n6. **Security & Audit**:\n   - Only authorized reviewers can access submissions assigned or permitted to them (e.g., if Reviewer A actively claims a submission, Reviewer B gets `403` on detail/stream/mutation; parents get `403` on all reviewer routes).\n   - Every review action (`draft_saved`, `published`, `updated`, `marked_not_assessable`, `changes_requested`) is recorded in `review_audit_history` with full JSON snapshot.\n   - Parents cannot edit published reviews.\n   - Review edits increment `version` and preserve complete prior history in `review_audit_history`.\n\n## 2. Progress\n### Completed in Step 8 (Batch 1 \342\200\224 Types, Score Formula & SQLite Schema Migrations DONE)\n1. `/src/shared/types.ts`:\n   - Updated `RubricAchievementLevel` to `\'met\' | \'partially_met\' | \'not_met\' | \'not_observed\' | \'not_assessable\'`.\n   - Added `ReviewPublicationStatus = \'draft\' | \'published\'`, `QueuePriority = \'high\' | \'normal\' | \'low\'`.\n   - Extended `ReviewRubricScoreDetail` with `explanation: string | null`.\n   - Added `ReviewHistoryEntry` and `ReviewerDashboardSummary`.\n   - Extended `SubmissionReviewDetail` with `reviewStatus`, `version`, `isAssessable`, `notAssessableReason`, `instructionMatchScorePct: number | null`, `applicableWeightPoints`, `earnedWeightPoints`, `reviewerComments`.\n   - Extended `ReviewerQueueItem` with `parentReference`, `activityVersion`, `priority`, `hasDraftReview`, `isAssessable`.\n   - Extended `ReviewerSubmissionDetail` with `submission.changeRequestNote`, `submission.storageMode`, `submission.storageReference`, and `history: ReviewHistoryEntry[]`.\n2. `/src/shared/domain.ts`:\n   - Updated `getRubricMultiplier` to return `number | null` (`1`, `0.5`, `0`, or `null` for `\'not_assessable\'`).\n   - Updated `calculateInstructionMatchScore` to return `{ isAssessable, scorePct, earnedTotal, applicableTotal, maxTotal, excludedCount }`, excluding `not_assessable` criteria from `applicableTotal` and returning `isAssessable: false, scorePct: null` when `applicableTotal <= 0 || applicableTotal < maxTotal * 0.5`.\n3. `/server/db/schema.ts`:\n   - Updated `CREATE TABLE submission_reviews` (nullable `instruction_match_score_pct`, `is_assessable`, `not_assessable_reason`, `reviewer_comments`, `review_status`, `version`).\n   - Updated `CREATE TABLE review_rubric_scores` (allows `\'met\', \'partially_met\', \'not_met\', \'not_observed\', \'not_assessable\'` + `explanation TEXT`).\n   - Added `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS review_audit_history` + index `idx_review_history_sub`.\n   - Added safe transactional SQLite in-place table upgrade (`submission_reviews_v2` / `review_rubric_scores_v2`) so existing `./data/littlesteps.db` migrates cleanly without losing seeded data!\n\n### Still Remaining for Step 8 (Batch 2 \342\200\224 Repository, Routes, API Client, Reviewer UI, Parent Feedback UI & Verification)\n- **NOT YET EDITED**:\n  1. `/server/repositories/index.ts`\n  2. `/server/routes/api.ts`\n  3. `/src/lib/api.ts`\n  4. `/src/pages/ReviewerWorkbenchView.tsx`\n  5. `/src/pages/parent/ParentSecondaryViews.tsx` (Parent Result view in `ProgressAndFeedbackSection`)\n  6. `/src/pages/parent/ParentActivityStudio.tsx` & `/src/pages/parent/MyPlanSection.tsx` (handle `instructionMatchScorePct === null` when a published review is `\"Not Assessable\"`)\n  7. **NOT YET COMPILED, LINTED, RESTARTED, OR E2E TESTED** since Batch 1 edits.\n\n### Skills Read\n- Read `/skills/system_skills/securecoder_persona/SKILL.md` (apply all Tier 2 checks: parameterized SQL, no literal secrets, RBAC & assignment checks, safe React bindings, plain-language security summary in final chat).\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n- **Important Breaking Type Change from Batch 1**:\n  - `SubmissionReviewDetail.instructionMatchScorePct` is now `number | null` (null when `isAssessable === false`), and `getRubricMultiplier` now returns `number | null`.\n  - Every consumer that reads `review.instructionMatchScorePct` or calls `getRubricMultiplier` must handle `null` cleanly! Specifically check:\n    - `/server/repositories/index.ts` (lines ~1365 notifications, ~1528 `getReviewDetailForSubmission`, ~1986 `submitRubricReview`)\n    - `/src/pages/parent/MyPlanSection.tsx` (`getJourneyStatusMeta` \342\200\224 if `review && !review.isAssessable`, show `\'Reviewed \302\267 Not Assessable\'`)\n    - `/src/pages/parent/ParentActivityStudio.tsx` (status text when `latestSubmission.review` is Not Assessable)\n    - `/src/pages/parent/ParentSecondaryViews.tsx` (`ProgressAndFeedbackSection` \342\200\224 show all 6 parent result fields + `\"Not Assessable\"` badge when `!sub.review.isAssessable`)\n    - `/src/pages/ParentJourneyView.tsx` (legacy file still in repo \342\200\224 check with `tsc --noEmit` via `lint_applet` so it doesn\'t break build!)\n- **Privacy-Minimized Parent Reference**:\n  - Generate deterministically from `parent_user_id` (e.g., `PAR-${parentUserId.replace(/[^a-z0-9]/gi, \'\').slice(-6).toUpperCase()}`) \342\200\224 never expose parent email, phone, or legal name to reviewers.\n- **Draft Privacy Boundary**:\n  - `getReviewDetailForSubmission(submissionId, includeDraft = false)`: MUST default to `includeDraft = false` (only `review_status = \'published\'`) for all parent-facing queries (`mapSubmissionRow`, `getJourneyForChild`, `listCompletedHistoryForChild`), while `getReviewerSubmissionDetail` passes `includeDraft = true` so the assigned reviewer can resume their draft!\n- **Reviewer Assignment Authorization**:\n  - On `GET /reviewer/submissions/:id`, `POST /reviewer/submissions/:id/review`, `POST /reviewer/submissions/:id/request-changes`, and `GET /submissions/:id/stream-token` (when role is `reviewer`): if `submission.assigned_reviewer_id` is non-null AND `submission.assigned_reviewer_id !== req.authUser.id` AND `submission.review_status === \'in_review\'`, return `403 Forbidden`! Admins retain oversight read-only access.\n- **Seeded Demo Accounts** (password `LittleSteps123!`):\n  - Parent: `meera@littlesteps.in`\n  - Reviewer: `ananya.reviewer@littlesteps.in`\n  - Admin: `kavita.admin@littlesteps.in`\n\n## 4. Errors & Fixes\n- **Resolved earlier**:\n  - Step 5: `seedDatabaseIfEmpty` returned early on existing DB before calling `ensureStructuredDailyPlans(db)` \342\200\224 fixed in `/server/db/seed.ts`.\n  - Step 7: `configuredProvider` TS narrowing in `mediaStorage.ts` and optional defaults for `childName`/`activityVersion` on `VideoCaptureUploader` \342\200\224 fixed and verified with `compile_applet` + `lint_applet`.\n  - Earlier in Step 8: attempted to `view_file` `/src/pages/ReviewerDashboardView.tsx` which did not exist; the actual filename is `/src/pages/ReviewerWorkbenchView.tsx`.\n- **No unresolved runtime errors**, though `compile_applet` + `lint_applet` will naturally show the expected `null`/type call sites until Batch 2 updates `repositories/index.ts`, `routes/api.ts`, and the UI files.\n\n## 5. Active Context\n- Dev server runs on port `3000` (`tsx server.ts`).\n- SQLite DB is at `./data/littlesteps.db`; schema migrations run automatically on server restart.\n- `ReviewerWorkbenchView.tsx` currently uses legacy Step-0 Tailwind classes (`border-stone`, `bg-linen`, `bg-oat`, `text-ink`, `text-olive`, `bg-eucalyptus`). Rebuilding it with the approved Design System (`Card`, `Badge`, `Button`, `Tabs`, `Select`, `EmptyState`, `Skeleton`, `ConfirmDialog`, semantic tokens `surface`, `cream`, `offwhite`, `sage`, `peach`, `lavender`, `danger`, `charcoal`, `muted`, `border`) will unify it visually with the rest of LittleSteps.\n\n## 6. Next Steps (In Priority Order)\n1. **Update `/server/repositories/index.ts`**:\n   - Import `QueuePriority`, `ReviewHistoryEntry`, `ReviewerDashboardSummary`, `ReviewPublicationStatus`, and `calculateInstructionMatchScore` from `../../src/shared/domain`.\n   - Update `getReviewDetailForSubmission(submissionId, includeDraft = false)`: filter `AND sr.review_status = \'published\'` unless `includeDraft === true`; map `reviewStatus`, `version`, `isAssessable`, `notAssessableReason`, `instructionMatchScorePct`, `applicableWeightPoints`, `earnedWeightPoints`, `reviewerComments`, and `explanation` on each rubric score.\n   - Add `listReviewHistory(submissionId): ReviewHistoryEntry[]` querying `review_audit_history` joined with `users`.\n   - Add `appendReviewAuditHistory(...)` helper called on every draft save, publish, edit, insufficient-evidence mark, and change request.\n   - Update `requestSubmissionChanges` to also append a `\'changes_requested\'` record to `review_audit_history`.\n   - Add `getReviewerDashboardSummary()` + update `listReviewerQueue` to compute `parentReference` (`PAR-...`), `activityVersion`, `priority` (`high` if pending/in_review > 24h or expiring in <= 5 days; `normal` if active; `low` if reviewed), `hasDraftReview`, `isAssessable`, and return `summary` (`totalPending`, `underReview`, `completedReviews`, `changesRequested`, `recentSubmissions`).\n   - Update `getReviewerSubmissionDetail(submissionId)` to include `parentReference`, `activityVersion`, `priority`, `hasDraftReview`, `isAssessable`, `changeRequestNote`, `storageMode`, `storageReference`, `review: getReviewDetailForSubmission(submissionId, true)`, and `history: listReviewHistory(submissionId)`.\n   - Upgrade `submitRubricReview` to support:\n     - `mode: \'draft\' | \'publish\' | \'not_assessable\'`\n     - `reviewerComments?: string | null`\n     - `notAssessableReason?: string | null`\n     - `criterionRatings`: `{ criterionId, achievedLevel, explanation?: string | null }` (require non-empty `explanation` when `achievedLevel === \'not_assessable\'` on publish!)\n     - Server-side score calculation using `calculateInstructionMatchScore` (or forcing `isAssessable = false, scorePct = null` when `mode === \'not_assessable\'`).\n     - When `mode === \'draft\'`: keep `video_submissions.review_status = \'in_review\'`, save `submission_reviews.review_status = \'draft\'`, log `\'draft_saved\'` in `review_audit_history`, do NOT mark parent completion as `\'reviewed\'`.\n     - When `mode === \'publish\'` or `\'not_assessable\'`: increment `version` if already published, save `submission_reviews.review_status = \'published\'`, update `video_submissions.review_status = \'reviewed\'`, update `activity_completions.status = \'reviewed\'`, and log `\'published\'` / `\'updated\'` / `\'marked_not_assessable\'` in `review_audit_history` with full snapshot JSON!\n   - Update notification text in `getJourneyForChild` when `sub.review` exists and `!sub.review.isAssessable` (show `\'Marked Not Assessable\'` instead of `${null}%`).\n\n2. **Update `/server/routes/api.ts`**:\n   - Update `reviewSubmitSchema`:\n     - `mode: z.enum([\'draft\', \'publish\', \'not_assessable\']).optional().default(\'publish\')`\n     - `strengthsNote`: required (`>= 10` chars) for `\'publish\'`, optional for `\'draft\'`/`\'not_assessable\'`\n     - `coachingTip`: required (`>= 10` chars) for `\'publish\'`, optional for `\'draft\'`/`\'not_assessable\'`\n     - `reviewerComments`: optional `max(1200)`\n     - `notAssessableReason`: required (`>= 10` chars) when `mode === \'not_assessable\'`\n     - `evaluationScopeAcknowledged`: `z.boolean()` (must be `true` when `mode !== \'draft\'`)\n     - `criterionRatings`: array with `achievedLevel: z.enum([\'met\', \'partially_met\', \'not_met\', \'not_observed\', \'not_assessable\'])` and optional `explanation: z.string().max(400).optional().nullable()`.\n   - Update `GET /reviewer/queue` to return `{ summary, queue }` (supporting `status` filter including `\'resubmit_requested\'`).\n   - Enforce reviewer assignment authorization (`assigned_reviewer_id && assigned_reviewer_id !== user.id && review_status === \'in_review\'` -> `403`) on `GET /reviewer/submissions/:id`, `POST /reviewer/submissions/:id/review`, `POST /reviewer/submissions/:id/request-changes`, and `GET /submissions/:id/stream-token` (when role is `\'reviewer\'`).\n\n3. **Update `/src/lib/api.ts`**:\n   - Update `getReviewerQueue` return type to `{ summary: ReviewerDashboardSummary; queue: ReviewerQueueItem[] }`.\n   - Update `submitReview` payload to support `mode`, `strengthsNote`, `coachingTip`, `reviewerComments`, `notAssessableReason`, `evaluationScopeAcknowledged`, and `criterionRatings` with `explanation`.\n\n4. **Rebuild `/src/pages/ReviewerWorkbenchView.tsx`** (using Design System components & Montessori editorial tokens):\n   - **Dashboard View**:\n     - Non-diagnostic mandate callout banner.\n     - 4 summary KPI cards (`Pending Review`, `Under Review`, `Completed Reviews`, `Changes Requested`).\n     - **Recently Submitted Videos** strip (quick open cards).\n     - **Review Queue Table** with filters (`All`, `Pending`, `Under Review`, `Changes Requested`, `Reviewed` + age-group selector) showing: **Parent Reference**, **Activity Name & Version**, **Age Group**, **Submitted Date**, **Status**, **Priority** badge, **Result** (`XX%` or `Not Assessable` or `Draft`), and **Action** button.\n   - **Review Details Split-Screen Page** displaying all 7 required elements:\n     - Left column:\n       1. Activity title & version (`vN`) + domain/age stage + parent reference\n       2. Submitted video (`SecureVideoPlayer` with `storageMode`)\n       3. Optional parent note card (when present)\n       4. Original activity instructions (numbered steps + materials)\n       5. Safety guidelines card (warm peach tone)\n     - Right column:\n       6. **Evaluation Checklist**: per-activity weighted criteria with 4 selectable ratings (`Met (1)`, `Partial (0.5)`, `Not met (0)`, `Not assessable`), inline explanation input when `Not assessable` is selected, and live weighted score readout (`XX%` with `earned / applicable pts` OR **`Not Assessable`** when insufficient evidence).\n       7. **Feedback & Reviewer Comments**: Positive observations (`strengthsNote`), Areas to improve (`coachingTip`), Additional reviewer comments (`reviewerComments`), non-diagnostic scope checkbox.\n       - **All 5 Actions**:\n         - **Save Draft** button\n         - **Submit / Update Evaluation** primary button\n         - **Mark Evidence Insufficient (Not Assessable)** modal/panel with reason input\n         - **Request Another Submission** modal/panel with gentle note input\n     - Bottom section: **Review Audit History** showing immutable versioned log (`draft_saved`, `published`, `updated`, `marked_not_assessable`, `changes_requested`) with timestamps & actor names.\n\n5. **Update Parent Result Views** (`/src/pages/parent/ParentSecondaryViews.tsx`, `/src/pages/parent/ParentActivityStudio.tsx`, `/src/pages/parent/MyPlanSection.tsx`, and `/src/pages/ParentJourneyView.tsx` if needed for TS):\n   - In `ProgressAndFeedbackSection` (`ParentSecondaryViews.tsx`), display all 6 required parent result items:\n     - Instruction-match percentage OR **`Not Assessable`** badge + `notAssessableReason`\n     - Criteria-wise feedback (`Met`, `Partially met`, `Not met`, `Not assessable` + excluded explanation)\n     - Positive observations (`strengthsNote`)\n     - Areas to improve (`coachingTip`)\n     - Reviewer comments (`reviewerComments` block when present)\n     - Review date (`submittedAt` formatted + reviewer name + `vN` if edited)\n   - Ensure `MyPlanSection.tsx` and `ParentActivityStudio.tsx` render `\"Reviewed \302\267 Not Assessable\"` cleanly when `review.instructionMatchScorePct === null`.\n\n6. **Verify End-to-End**:\n   - Co-execute `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` (`tsc --noEmit` must pass with 0 errors).\n   - Call `restart_dev_server` so SQLite table upgrades (`submission_reviews`, `review_rubric_scores`, `review_audit_history`) run cleanly.\n   - Run an exhaustive Step 8 E2E test script against `http://localhost:3000/api/v1` verifying:\n     1. Reviewer dashboard `GET /reviewer/queue` returns `summary` (`totalPending`, `underReview`, `completedReviews`, `recentSubmissions`) and queue items with `parentReference` (`PAR-...`, no PII), `activityVersion`, and `priority`.\n     2. Parent cannot access reviewer endpoints or edit published reviews (`403`).\n     3. Create a temp submission -> Reviewer claims (`in_review`) -> **Save Draft** (`mode: \'draft\'`) -> verify parent still sees NO published review (`review === null`) while reviewer sees the draft AND `review_audit_history` has `\'draft_saved\'`.\n     4. Reviewer publishes with mixed 4-level ratings (`met`, `partially_met`, `not_met`, `not_assessable` with explanation) -> verify exact weighted formula `round((earned / applicable) * 100)` excluding `not_assessable`, AND parent receives score, criteria-wise feedback + explanation, positive observations, areas to improve, reviewer comments, and review date!\n     5. Reviewer edits the published review -> verify `version` increments to `2` AND `review_audit_history` preserves both `v1` (`published`) and `v2` (`updated`)!\n     6. Reviewer marks another submission as **Not Assessable** (`mode: \'not_assessable\'` or >50% weight `not_assessable`) -> verify `isAssessable === false`, `instructionMatchScorePct === null`, `notAssessableReason` saved, and logged as `\'marked_not_assessable\'`!\n     7. Reviewer requests another submission (`POST /reviewer/submissions/:id/request-changes`) -> verify `resubmit_requested` + audit log entry.\n     8. Clean up temporary test child/submissions so demo data stays clean.\n\n## 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- Strict TypeScript (`strict: true`), Tailwind CSS v4 (`@import \"tailwindcss\";`), WCAG 2.2 AA contrast, `>= 44px` touch targets, warm Montessori editorial tokens.\n- Never evaluate baby intelligence, health, or developmental level \342\200\224 caregiver instruction execution only.\n- Never expose parent PII (email, phone, legal name) to reviewers.\n- Never use `window.alert`, `window.confirm`, or `window.open`.\n- Include 2\342\200\2233 concise plain-language security safeguard bullets in the final chat response without internal security branding or jargon.\n</summary>"
