  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Executing Batch 2 Now**\n\nI\'ve achieved complete clarity on all files involved. My focus is now on the clean and systematic execution of Batch 2. Currently, I\'m updating `/server/repositories/index.ts`. First, I\'m carefully reviewing all required changes. Specifically, I\'m adding `QueuePriority` to the imports section of the file.\n\n\n**Adding New Functions**\n\nI\'m now integrating new functionalities into `/server/repositories/index.ts`. I am currently focusing on importing `calculateInstructionMatchScore` from `../../src/shared/domain`. Also, I\'m adding `formatParentReference` with a deterministic, opaque reference for parent user IDs. Lastly, I\'m working on `computeQueuePriority` to manage queue priority based on various conditions.\n\n\n**Refining Review Details**\n\nI\'m now refining the logic for displaying review details. My current focus is on the conditional formatting of review summaries. I am formatting the review detail summary string based on the `isAssessable` flag and the `instructionMatchScorePct`. Further, I\'m working to update `getReviewDetailForSubmission` query with applicable and earned weight points based on `scoreRows`. I am also mapping the fields.\n\n\n**Mapping Data, Tracking History**\n\nI\'m currently focused on mapping fields for review details, including `instructionMatchScorePct`, `applicableWeightPoints`, and `earnedWeightPoints`. I\'m also adding `strengthsNote`, `coachingTip`, and `reviewerComments`. Further, I\'m incorporating audit history by adding `appendReviewAuditHistory` and `listReviewHistory` functions. I\'m ensuring all actions are recorded with JSON snapshots for complete review edit history. Finally, I\'m updating `requestSubmissionChanges` to log change requests in audit history and also adding `getReviewerDashboardSummary`.\n\n\n**Calculating Queue Metrics**\n\nI\'m now calculating queue metrics by querying the `video_submissions` table, excluding deleted entries. I am counting the pending, in-review, completed, and changes-requested submissions based on their review status. Further, I am focusing on recent submissions by ordering the top 5 most recent submissions by `created_at` descending. Finally, I\'m working to update `listReviewerQueue` query, selecting the necessary data and adjusting the display of `instructionMatchScorePct` based on the review status.\n\n\n**Defining Submission Details**\n\nI\'m now defining the structure for reviewer submission details. I\'m selecting fields such as `parent_user_id`, `activity_version`, and review status. I\'m also including `parentReference`, `activityVersion`, `priority`, and other key data points. Further, I\'m integrating review history and details. I\'m also working to upgrade `submitRubricReview` to support new parameters.\n\n\n**Validating Rubric Details**\n\nI am now focusing on validation rules for rubric details. I\'m checking for the reviewer assignment and authorization, and throwing errors when conditions aren\'t met. I am validating rubric criteria upon \'publish\', ensuring non-empty explanations for criteria marked as \'not_assessable\'. Furthermore, I\'m working on computing scores using `calculateInstructionMatchScore` based on various `mode` and `isAssessable` conditions.\n\n\n**Implementing Review Updates**\n\nI\'m now implementing the review updates. I\'m focusing on handling \'draft\', \'publish\', and \'not_assessable\' states. Specifically, I\'m ensuring review statuses are updated correctly, audit history is logged, and versions are managed. I\'m also ensuring the associated submission and activity statuses are also updated, and preserving a clear error when trying to downgrade a published review.\n\n\n"
