  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Data Structures**\n\nI\'m currently updating `/server/routes/api.ts` to include a new `mode` field within the `reviewSubmitSchema`. This field, which is a `z.enum`, will accept values such as \'draft\', \'publish\', or \'not_assessable\', to enable better data management.\n\n\n**Implementing Validation Rules**\n\nI\'ve added several new fields, with appropriate defaults, to the data schema. Specifically, I\'m working with `strengthsNote`, `coachingTip`, `reviewerComments`, `notAssessableReason`, `evaluationScopeAcknowledged`, and `criterionRatings`. I\'m using `.superRefine()` to enforce several validation rules, including a check for `evaluationScopeAcknowledged` based on the `mode`, and required length checks for key fields when publishing. I\'m ensuring that data integrity is maintained at every stage.\n\n\n**Enforcing Access Controls**\n\nI\'m now integrating robust authorization checks. I\'ve implemented `canReviewerAccessSubmission` to restrict reviewer access based on roles and submission assignments, denying access if a reviewer tries to access a submission not explicitly assigned to them when it is under review. This is being applied to several endpoints, including those for stream tokens, review retrieval, and submission/request changes.\n\n\n\n"
    message_id: "WB4Ba6-jCYuLqtsP48zj6AM"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_16923254338776320672"
      name: "multi_replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"Description\":\"Upgrade reviewer API routes with 4-level rubric + draft/publish/not_assessable schema, dashboard summary payload, and strict reviewer assignment authorization.\", \"Instruction\":\"Update reviewSubmitSchema, stream-token RBAC, and reviewer queue/detail/review/request-changes endpoints in server/routes/api.ts.\", \"ReplacementChunks\":[{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"EndLine\":120, \"ReplacementContent\":\"const reviewSubmitSchema = z\\n  .object({\\n    mode: z.enum([\'draft\', \'publish\', \'not_assessable\']).optional().default(\'publish\'),\\n    strengthsNote: z.string().max(1000).optional().default(\'\'),\\n    coachingTip: z.string().max(1000).optional().default(\'\'),\\n    reviewerComments: z.string().max(1200).optional().nullable(),\\n    notAssessableReason: z.string().max(600).optional().nullable(),\\n    evaluationScopeAcknowledged: z.boolean().optional().default(false),\\n    criterionRatings: z\\n      .array(\\n        z.object({\\n          criterionId: z.string().min(1),\\n          achievedLevel: z.enum([\\n            \'met\',\\n            \'partially_met\',\\n            \'not_met\',\\n            \'not_observed\',\\n            \'not_assessable\',\\n          ]),\\n          explanation: z.string().max(400).optional().nullable(),\\n        })\\n      )\\n      .optional()\\n      .default([]),\\n  })\\n  .superRefine((data, ctx) => {\\n    if (data.mode !== \'draft\' && !data.evaluationScopeAcknowledged) {\\n      ctx.addIssue({\\n        code: z.ZodIssueCode.custom,\\n        message: \'Please confirm this evaluation assesses caregiver instruction execution only.\',\\n        path: [\'evaluationScopeAcknowledged\'],\\n      });\\n    }\\n    if (data.mode === \'publish\') {\\n      if (data.strengthsNote.trim().length < 10) {\\n        ctx.addIssue({\\n          code: z.ZodIssueCode.custom,\\n          message: \'Please share positive caregiver observations (at least 10 characters).\',\\n          path: [\'strengthsNote\'],\\n        });\\n      }\\n      if (data.coachingTip.trim().length < 10) {\\n        ctx.addIssue({\\n          code: z.ZodIssueCode.custom,\\n          message: \'Please share one practical area to improve (at least 10 characters).\',\\n          path: [\'coachingTip\'],\\n        });\\n      }\\n      if (data.criterionRatings.length === 0) {\\n        ctx.addIssue({\\n          code: z.ZodIssueCode.custom,\\n          message: \'Please evaluate the activity rubric criteria before publishing.\',\\n          path: [\'criterionRatings\'],\\n        });\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (data.mode === \'not_assessable\') {\\n      if ((data.notAssessableReason?.trim().length ?? 0) < 10) {\\n        ctx.addIssue({\\n          code: z.ZodIssueCode.custom,\\n          message:\\n            \'Please provide a clear explanation (at least 10 characters) of why evidence is insufficient.\',\\n          path: [\'notAssessableReason\'],\\n        });\\n      }\\n    }\\n  });\", \"StartLine\":105, \"TargetContent\":\"const reviewSubmitSchema = z.object({\\n  strengthsNote: z.string().min(10, \'Please share a warm, specific strength note.\').max(1000),\\n  coachingTip: z.string().min(10, \'Please share one practical next-time tip.\').max(1000),\\n  evaluationScopeAcknowledged: z.literal(true, {\\n    message: \'Please confirm this evaluation assesses caregiver instruction execution only.\',\\n  }),\\n  criterionRatings: z\\n    .array(\\n      z.object({\\n        criterionId: z.string().min(1),\\n        achievedLevel: z.enum([\'met\', \'partially_met\', \'not_observed\']),\\n      })\\n    )\\n    .min(1),\\n});\"}, {\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"EndLine\":824, \"ReplacementContent\":\"      // Strict RBAC ownership / assignment enforcement\\n      const reviewerAssignedElsewhere =\\n        user.role === \'reviewer\' &&\\n        Boolean(sub.assigned_reviewer_id) &&\\n        sub.assigned_reviewer_id !== user.id &&\\n        sub.review_status === \'in_review\';\\n\\n      const allowed =\\n        (user.role === \'parent\' && sub.parent_user_id === user.id) ||\\n        (user.role === \'reviewer\' && !reviewerAssignedElsewhere) ||\\n        user.role === \'admin\';\\n\\n      if (!allowed) {\\n        res.status(403).json({\\n          error: reviewerAssignedElsewhere\\n            ? \'This submission is actively assigned to another reviewer.\'\\n            : \'Not authorized to access this video.\',\\n        });\\n        return;\\n      }\", \"StartLine\":811, \"TargetContent\":\"      // Strict RBAC ownership / assignment enforcement\\n      const allowed =\\n        (user.role === \'parent\' && sub.parent_user_id === user.id) ||\\n        user.role === \'reviewer\' ||\\n        user.role === \'admin\';\\n\\n      if (!allowed) {\\n        res.status(403).json({ error: \'Not authorized to access this video.\' });\\n        return;\\n      }\"}, {\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"EndLine\":1030, \"ReplacementContent\":\"  // ======================== REVIEWER WORKBENCH ========================\\n\\n  router.get(\\n    \'/reviewer/queue\',\\n    requireAuth,\\n    requireRole(\'reviewer\', \'admin\'),\\n    (req: AuthenticatedRequest, res) => {\\n      const status = typeof req.query.status === \'string\' ? req.query.status : \'all\';\\n      const ageGroupSlug =\\n        typeof req.query.ageGroupSlug === \'string\' ? req.query.ageGroupSlug : \'all\';\\n      const summary = repo.getReviewerDashboardSummary();\\n      const queue = repo.listReviewerQueue({\\n        status: status as \'queued\' | \'in_review\' | \'reviewed\' | \'resubmit_requested\' | \'all\',\\n        ageGroupSlug,\\n      });\\n      res.json({ summary, queue });\\n    }\\n  );\\n\\n  router.post(\\n    \'/reviewer/submissions/:id/claim\',\\n    requireAuth,\\n    requireRole(\'reviewer\'),\\n    (req: AuthenticatedRequest, res) => {\\n      const claimed = repo.claimSubmissionForReviewer(req.params.id, req.authUser!.id);\\n      if (!claimed) {\\n        res.status(409).json({\\n          error: \'This submission is already assigned to another reviewer or completed.\',\\n        });\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      const detail = repo.getReviewerSubmissionDetail(req.params.id);\\n      res.json(detail);\\n    }\\n  );\\n\\n  router.get(\\n    \'/reviewer/submissions/:id\',\\n    requireAuth,\\n    requireRole(\'reviewer\', \'admin\'),\\n    (req: AuthenticatedRequest, res) => {\\n      const rawSub = repo.findSubmissionRawById(req.params.id);\\n      if (!rawSub) {\\n        res.status(404).json({ error: \'Submission not found.\' });\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      if (\\n        req.authUser!.role === \'reviewer\' &&\\n        rawSub.assigned_reviewer_id &&\\n        rawSub.assigned_reviewer_id !== req.authUser!.id &&\\n        rawSub.review_status === \'in_review\'\\n      ) {\\n        res.status(403).json({\\n          error: \'This submission is actively assigned to another reviewer.\',\\n        });\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      const detail = repo.getReviewerSubmissionDetail(req.params.id);\\n      if (!detail) {\\n        res.status(404).json({ error: \'Submission not found.\' });\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      res.json(detail);\\n    }\\n  );\\n\\n  router.post(\\n    \'/reviewer/submissions/:id/review\',\\n    requireAuth,\\n    requireRole(\'reviewer\'),\\n    (req: AuthenticatedRequest, res) => {\\n      const rawSub = repo.findSubmissionRawById(req.params.id);\\n      if (!rawSub) {\\n        res.status(404).json({ error: \'Submission not found.\' });\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      if (\\n        rawSub.assigned_reviewer_id &&\\n        rawSub.assigned_reviewer_id !== req.authUser!.id &&\\n        rawSub.review_status === \'in_review\'\\n      ) {\\n        res.status(403).json({\\n          error: \'This submission is actively assigned to another reviewer.\',\\n        });\\n        return;\\n      }\\n\\n      const parsed = reviewSubmitSchema.safeParse(req.body);\\n      if (!parsed.success) {\\n        res.status(400).json({ error: parsed.error.issues[0]?.message || \'Invalid review input.\' });\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      try {\\n        const review = repo.submitRubricReview({\\n          submissionId: req.params.id,\\n          reviewerUserId: req.authUser!.id,\\n          mode: parsed.data.mode,\\n          strengthsNote: parsed.data.strengthsNote,\\n          coachingTip: parsed.data.coachingTip,\\n          reviewerComments: parsed.data.reviewerComments,\\n          notAssessableReason: parsed.data.notAssessableReason,\\n          criterionRatings: parsed.data.criterionRatings,\\n        });\\n        const detail = repo.getReviewerSubmissionDetail(req.params.id);\\n        res.status(201).json({ review, detail });\\n      } catch (err) {\\n        const msg = err instanceof Error ? err.message : \'Unable to submit review.\';\\n        res.status(400).json({ error: msg });\\n      }\\n    }\\n  );\\n\\n  router.post(\\n    \'/reviewer/submissions/:id/request-changes\',\\n    requireAuth,\\n    requireRole(\'reviewer\'),\\n    (req: AuthenticatedRequest, res) => {\\n      const rawSub = repo.findSubmissionRawById(req.params.id);\\n      if (!rawSub) {\\n        res.status(404).json({ error: \'Submission not found.\' });\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      if (\\n        rawSub.assigned_reviewer_id &&\\n        rawSub.assigned_reviewer_id !== req.authUser!.id &&\\n        rawSub.review_status === \'in_review\'\\n      ) {\\n        res.status(403).json({\\n          error: \'This submission is actively assigned to another reviewer.\',\\n        });\\n        return;\\n      }\\n\\n      const schema = z.object({\\n        note: z\\n          .string()\\n          .min(10, \'Please share a clear, gentle explanation of what to re-record.\')\\n          .max(600),\\n      });\\n      const parsed = schema.safeParse(req.body);\\n      if (!parsed.success) {\\n        res.status(400).json({ error: parsed.error.issues[0]?.message || \'Invalid note.\' });\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      const updated = repo.requestSubmissionChanges(\\n        req.params.id,\\n        req.authUser!.id,\\n        parsed.data.note\\n      );\\n      if (!updated) {\\n        res.status(409).json({\\n          error:\\n            \'Could not request changes for this submission (it may already be reviewed, deleted, or claimed by another reviewer).\',\\n        });\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      const detail = repo.getReviewerSubmissionDetail(req.params.id);\\n      res.json({ ok: true, detail });\\n    }\\n  );\", \"StartLine\":924, \"TargetContent\":\"  // ======================== REVIEWER WORKBENCH ========================\\n\\n  router.get(\\n    \'/reviewer/queue\',\\n    requireAuth,\\n    requireRole(\'reviewer\', \'admin\'),\\n    (req: AuthenticatedRequest, res) => {\\n      const status = typeof req.query.status === \'string\' ? req.query.status : \'all\';\\n      const ageGroupSlug =\\n        typeof req.query.ageGroupSlug === \'string\' ? req.query.ageGroupSlug : \'all\';\\n      const queue = repo.listReviewerQueue({\\n        status: status as \'queued\' | \'in_review\' | \'reviewed\' | \'all\',\\n        ageGroupSlug,\\n      });\\n      res.json({ queue });\\n    }\\n  );\\n\\n  router.post(\\n    \'/reviewer/submissions/:id/claim\',\\n    requireAuth,\\n    requireRole(\'reviewer\'),\\n    (req: AuthenticatedRequest, res) => {\\n      const claimed = repo.claimSubmissionForReviewer(req.params.id, req.authUser!.id);\\n      if (!claimed) {\\n        res.status(409).json({\\n          error: \'This submission is already assigned to another reviewer or completed.\',\\n        });\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      const detail = repo.getReviewerSubmissionDetail(req.params.id);\\n      res.json(detail);\\n    }\\n  );\\n\\n  router.get(\\n    \'/reviewer/submissions/:id\',\\n    requireAuth,\\n    requireRole(\'reviewer\', \'admin\'),\\n    (req: AuthenticatedRequest, res) => {\\n      const detail = repo.getReviewerSubmissionDetail(req.params.id);\\n      if (!detail) {\\n        res.status(404).json({ error: \'Submission not found.\' });\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      res.json(detail);\\n    }\\n  );\\n\\n  router.post(\\n    \'/reviewer/submissions/:id/review\',\\n    requireAuth,\\n    requireRole(\'reviewer\'),\\n    (req: AuthenticatedRequest, res) => {\\n      const parsed = reviewSubmitSchema.safeParse(req.body);\\n      if (!parsed.success) {\\n        res.status(400).json({ error: parsed.error.issues[0]?.message || \'Invalid review input.\' });\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      try {\\n        const review = repo.submitRubricReview({\\n          submissionId: req.params.id,\\n          reviewerUserId: req.authUser!.id,\\n          strengthsNote: parsed.data.strengthsNote,\\n          coachingTip: parsed.data.coachingTip,\\n          criterionRatings: parsed.data.criterionRatings,\\n        });\\n        res.status(201).json({ review });\\n      } catch (err) {\\n        const msg = err instanceof Error ? err.message : \'Unable to submit review.\';\\n        res.status(400).json({ error: msg });\\n      }\\n    }\\n  );\\n\\n  router.post(\\n    \'/reviewer/submissions/:id/request-changes\',\\n    requireAuth,\\n    requireRole(\'reviewer\'),\\n    (req: AuthenticatedRequest, res) => {\\n      const schema = z.object({\\n        note: z\\n          .string()\\n          .min(10, \'Please share a clear, gentle explanation of what to re-record.\')\\n          .max(600),\\n      });\\n      const parsed = schema.safeParse(req.body);\\n      if (!parsed.success) {\\n        res.status(400).json({ error: parsed.error.issues[0]?.message || \'Invalid note.\' });\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      const updated = repo.requestSubmissionChanges(\\n        req.params.id,\\n        req.authUser!.id,\\n        parsed.data.note\\n      );\\n      if (!updated) {\\n        res.status(409).json({\\n          error: \'Could not request changes for this submission (it may be reviewed, deleted, or claimed by another reviewer).\',\\n        });\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      const detail = repo.getReviewerSubmissionDetail(req.params.id);\\n      res.json({ ok: true, detail });\\n    }\\n  );\"}], \"TargetFile\":\"/server/routes/api.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Updating reviewer API routes and authorization\", \"toolSummary\":\"Update reviewer API routes\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\206\034\n\203\034\001i\024}\023\242\240\2027\333\367\270\245\240\003\307\nfX\v\036\377,\234pZH\230\026\302\317:\237\246\247\353NY~.k\270?\372\370ws\345\243/_N\2363\230\214M>K\210R=\334K\235B$bm\f\256\326\371\257.(RfUJA#\362\034o8\333MoE\f$t~\325\036\004\231\340\037\307YB-\370\024T\363^\371\002\323P\271=S~\246\242\2240\344\000\214\310%y\247\357\234P\334\201\350\256\315\214/\373\"Br]%\f\254\276\025[*\277?\277mLY\270\266y\006\345TE\265\327~o\031\266\006\021\255\033\274\267\351\016\001\257i[\221P\206R#\302[i\242\222\346\371:.\272A}\242\375+\220\311\241\240;\245\347ky\360\006gGn\222\024\246A\236\311\\\303N\377\211\307\\\b\\\351\371\266\260\022>#\022\364\324\022\244\305\351\370\264n?33Ax\227\340u_%\365\fd\200\353C\002|`x\251\217\330\344\bK2\271\021s\024(\023\207%\247\217/\3506\250\371+\rn_\'c\2531\\\323\313L\231\'\211-\341\016Czm\315vk:\223:\357\247akc\316\334\313\255\345S\326>\a\247\275\273\333\335\"\330\376\252\334\326w\307\205\350\352\r\226p\231\324\243\276\306\2715\a\255m\356\2430s\277\213di\327q\302@G\314k\265F\323\236\022\201\314\227\327q\b\000\004\332S\266\001\237\225\314\222\226\201\301\224\266R\3768S\247+F,\3225\177\205\301\\-4!\034\35779\343\006\343E\224B\267Z\223e\334.\204\277\002f\3609U(\307\332n\357\263[\372\v\024\232B]7\272\340!\334\225\370\345\a%4\306\345\025\360j\202\0253e\3403\235d\323\355\016\227\366\374\277P\3100=\370\274\303\230\241\326\207[v\327\025(\356\375\307\344\237\001\272\267$k\270\305\004d\177\312\017\344\275\240\313:\276_,_\360\3462\337\227\004\236\00649N\202\ay\262FnI\177\341\311\371_\347\034Mna0\250\020\331\254\237\246\306s\342\247\200p\303\"M\243\305\222\374\023\tCm\377D\363\315\317\021}\365\317\265\214\002\035%\325\222\177\023\231\333j\342{&\t\016~w\215\341-\311\3610\310c\237\267\243AN\\\302j\026I\363\223wY\253~<\304\215\266\316\346\000\350\271D\352\342\353\343er\223\207\254k\262d\301\326\240\377^\277\360G\177N\005F\316`\304\245\346\354\363a\221\276\223\255O^\271w.\220\003\001\267\226\342\3437\317\222\313L\3