  planner_response {
    response: "Step 8 is complete. LittleSteps now includes a dedicated **Reviewer Dashboard**, weighted caregiver evaluation workbench, immutable review history, and updated parent feedback result views.\n\n### What Was Built\n\n- **Reviewer Dashboard & Queue**\n  - Displays summary KPIs for **Pending Submissions**, **Under Review**, **Completed Reviews**, and **Changes Requested**, alongside a **Recently Submitted Videos** section.\n  - Review queue table with status and age-group filters displaying privacy-minimized **Parent Reference** (`PAR-XXXXXX`), **Activity Name & Version**, **Age Group**, **Submission Date**, **Review Status**, **Priority** (`High` / `Normal` / `Low`), and evaluation result.\n  - Clear non-diagnostic policy banner reminding reviewers to assess caregiver instruction execution only\342\200\224never the baby\342\200\231s intelligence, health, or developmental level.\n\n- **Split-Screen Review Details & 4-Level Weighted Rubric**\n  - Displays all required context: activity title and version (`vN`), original step-by-step instructions and required materials, safety guidelines, private submitted video stream, optional parent note, per-activity weighted evaluation checklist, and reviewer comments.\n  - Supports all four rubric ratings: **Met (`1`)**, **Partially met (`0.5`)**, **Not met (`0`)**, and **Not assessable** (excluded from the denominator with a required explanation).\n  - Calculates `Instruction Match Percentage = (Weighted points earned / Applicable weighted points) \303\227 100` server-side and automatically marks clips as **Not Assessable** (without a misleading percentage) when insufficient weighted criteria can be evaluated.\n\n- **All Five Review Workflows & Audit History**\n  - **Save Draft**: Saves work privately while keeping the submission under review and hidden from parents until published.\n  - **Submit / Update Evaluation**: Publishes feedback to the parent; editing a published review increments its version (`v2`, `v3`, \342\200\246) while preserving prior snapshots.\n  - **Add Structured Feedback**: Positive observations, areas to improve, optional reviewer comments, and per-criterion notes.\n  - **Mark Evidence Insufficient**: Publishes a clear **Not Assessable** outcome with an explanation instead of a score.\n  - **Request Another Submission**: Sends gentle re-recording guidance and transitions the submission to **Changes Requested**.\n  - **Review Audit History**: Every draft save, publication, revision, insufficient-evidence ruling, and resubmission request is recorded in an immutable timeline.\n\n- **Updated Parent Result View**\n  - Shows the instruction-match percentage (or **Not Assessable** with the reviewer\342\200\231s explanation), criteria-wise feedback with notes, positive observations, areas to improve, reviewer comments, and review date.\n\n### Security & Privacy Safeguards\n\n- **Strict role and assignment boundaries**: Only authorized reviewers can claim and evaluate submissions; submissions actively claimed by one reviewer return `403 Forbidden` to other reviewers, and parents are blocked from accessing reviewer queues or modifying published evaluations.\n- **Privacy-minimized reviewer queues**: Parent names, emails, and phone numbers are omitted from reviewer responses in favor of an opaque parent reference (`PAR-XXXXXX`), and draft reviews remain hidden from parents until published.\n- **Immutable audit trail**: Every video open/stream and every review action (including edits to published reviews) is recorded with actor, timestamp, version, and snapshot metadata so historical evaluations cannot be silently overwritten."
    thinking: "**Analyzing Reviewer Data**\n\nI\'ve just reviewed the data output regarding RBAC and the Reviewer Dashboard. It looks like everything is functioning correctly there, with zero pending and under-review items, but one completed review. The draft privacy boundary is also verified, ensuring reviewers only see the appropriate content. I\'m moving on to consider point 4.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "riEBa_j-IKbVz7IPuYWRoQ4"
    modified_response: "Step 8 is complete. LittleSteps now includes a dedicated **Reviewer Dashboard**, weighted caregiver evaluation workbench, immutable review history, and updated parent feedback result views.\n\n### What Was Built\n\n- **Reviewer Dashboard & Queue**\n  - Displays summary KPIs for **Pending Submissions**, **Under Review**, **Completed Reviews**, and **Changes Requested**, alongside a **Recently Submitted Videos** section.\n  - Review queue table with status and age-group filters displaying privacy-minimized **Parent Reference** (`PAR-XXXXXX`), **Activity Name & Version**, **Age Group**, **Submission Date**, **Review Status**, **Priority** (`High` / `Normal` / `Low`), and evaluation result.\n  - Clear non-diagnostic policy banner reminding reviewers to assess caregiver instruction execution only\342\200\224never the baby\342\200\231s intelligence, health, or developmental level.\n\n- **Split-Screen Review Details & 4-Level Weighted Rubric**\n  - Displays all required context: activity title and version (`vN`), original step-by-step instructions and required materials, safety guidelines, private submitted video stream, optional parent note, per-activity weighted evaluation checklist, and reviewer comments.\n  - Supports all four rubric ratings: **Met (`1`)**, **Partially met (`0.5`)**, **Not met (`0`)**, and **Not assessable** (excluded from the denominator with a required explanation).\n  - Calculates `Instruction Match Percentage = (Weighted points earned / Applicable weighted points) \303\227 100` server-side and automatically marks clips as **Not Assessable** (without a misleading percentage) when insufficient weighted criteria can be evaluated.\n\n- **All Five Review Workflows & Audit History**\n  - **Save Draft**: Saves work privately while keeping the submission under review and hidden from parents until published.\n  - **Submit / Update Evaluation**: Publishes feedback to the parent; editing a published review increments its version (`v2`, `v3`, \342\200\246) while preserving prior snapshots.\n  - **Add Structured Feedback**: Positive observations, areas to improve, optional reviewer comments, and per-criterion notes.\n  - **Mark Evidence Insufficient**: Publishes a clear **Not Assessable** outcome with an explanation instead of a score.\n  - **Request Another Submission**: Sends gentle re-recording guidance and transitions the submission to **Changes Requested**.\n  - **Review Audit History**: Every draft save, publication, revision, insufficient-evidence ruling, and resubmission request is recorded in an immutable timeline.\n\n- **Updated Parent Result View**\n  - Shows the instruction-match percentage (or **Not Assessable** with the reviewer\342\200\231s explanation), criteria-wise feedback with notes, positive observations, areas to improve, reviewer comments, and review date.\n\n### Security & Privacy Safeguards\n\n- **Strict role and assignment boundaries**: Only authorized reviewers can claim and evaluate submissions; submissions actively claimed by one reviewer return `403 Forbidden` to other reviewers, and parents are blocked from accessing reviewer queues or modifying published evaluations.\n- **Privacy-minimized reviewer queues**: Parent names, emails, and phone numbers are omitted from reviewer responses in favor of an opaque parent reference (`PAR-XXXXXX`), and draft reviews remain hidden from parents until published.\n- **Immutable audit trail**: Every video open/stream and every review action (including edits to published reviews) is recorded with actor, timestamp, version, and snapshot metadata so historical evaluations cannot be silently overwritten."
