  user_input {
    user_response: "# STEP 9 \342\200\224 Build progress tracking and activity history\n\nCreate the progress section for parents.\n\nThe purpose is to help mothers understand their participation and learning journey.\n\nDo not present activity completion or review scores as a medical or developmental assessment of the baby.\n\n## Progress dashboard\n\nShow:\n- Activities completed.\n- Activities remaining.\n- Weekly activity consistency.\n- Domain-wise activity participation.\n- Submitted videos.\n- Reviewed activities.\n\n## Activity history\n\nCreate filters for:\n- Date range.\n- Development domain.\n- Completion status.\n- Review status.\n\nEach activity history item should open its details and related review.\n\n## Review history\n\nShow:\n- Activity name.\n- Submission date.\n- Review date.\n- Instruction-match percentage, when assessable.\n- Reviewer feedback.\n\n## Visual design\n\nUse:\n- Simple charts.\n- Clear progress bars.\n- Friendly illustrations.\n- Descriptive labels.\n- Helpful empty states.\n\nAvoid complicated statistics and competitive leaderboards.\n\n## Expected output\n\nA useful progress dashboard that reflects actual activity and submission records."
    items {
      text: "# STEP 9 \342\200\224 Build progress tracking and activity history\n\nCreate the progress section for parents.\n\nThe purpose is to help mothers understand their participation and learning journey.\n\nDo not present activity completion or review scores as a medical or developmental assessment of the baby.\n\n## Progress dashboard\n\nShow:\n- Activities completed.\n- Activities remaining.\n- Weekly activity consistency.\n- Domain-wise activity participation.\n- Submitted videos.\n- Reviewed activities.\n\n## Activity history\n\nCreate filters for:\n- Date range.\n- Development domain.\n- Completion status.\n- Review status.\n\nEach activity history item should open its details and related review.\n\n## Review history\n\nShow:\n- Activity name.\n- Submission date.\n- Review date.\n- Instruction-match percentage, when assessable.\n- Reviewer feedback.\n\n## Visual design\n\nUse:\n- Simple charts.\n- Clear progress bars.\n- Friendly illustrations.\n- Descriptive labels.\n- Helpful empty states.\n\nAvoid complicated statistics and competitive leaderboards.\n\n## Expected output\n\nA useful progress dashboard that reflects actual activity and submission records."
    }
  }
