  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Framing Learning Journeys**\n\nI\'m now deeply immersed in designing Step 9, focusing specifically on how mothers understand their participation and learning journeys. The goal is to frame this information in a non-diagnostic way, making the information clear and easy to understand. I want to convey an element of warmth and clarity, to achieve an outstanding design!\n\n\n**Refining Engagement Metrics**\n\nI\'ve been working on how to present activity engagement metrics without making them feel clinical or competitive. My focus is on providing clear, non-judgmental visualizations that highlight activity completion, consistency (weekly and monthly), and participation across different domains. I\'m also including counts for submitted videos and caregiver reviews, ensuring these are integrated into an accessible and supportive interface.\n\n\n**Detailing Activity History**\n\nI\'m now detailing the activity history functionality, incorporating the necessary filters: date range, development domain, completion status, and review status. Each history item will open a modal with activity details, the parent\'s reflection, and the linked video preview. I\'m focusing on a clean and dedicated Activity History & Review Detail Modal with all the relevant data.\n\n\n**Constructing Review Histories**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the review history section, aiming for a comprehensive display of submitted and reviewed videos. I\'m prioritizing five key data points for each record: the activity name (including version and domain/age stage), submission and review dates, instruction-match percentage (or a clear \"Not Assessable\" indicator), and detailed reviewer feedback. This feedback will include positive observations, areas needing improvement, reviewer comments, and a breakdown based on specific criteria. Each entry will also feature a private video preview and a \"Delete Video Now\" option for privacy.\n\n\n"
