  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Illustration Match**\n\nI\'m pleased with the illustration\'s alignment with the brand\'s aesthetic. Now, I\'m shifting my focus towards carefully constructing the backend and frontend components, and shared types required to implement step 9.\n\n\n**Defining Data Interfaces**\n\nI\'ve been working on defining strongly typed interfaces for the dedicated progress endpoint within `/src/shared/types.ts`. I\'ve added the `ActivityHistoryRecord` and `WeeklyConsistency` interfaces, ensuring robust data structures for activity history, which includes comprehensive details like completion status, display status, and caregiver notes. The goal is cleaner, more predictable data flow across the application.\n\n\n**Constructing API Responses**\n\nI\'m now focused on fleshing out the structure of the API responses. I\'m building out data models for weekly consistency trends and parent progress overviews, including the necessary fields for child profiles, activity summaries, and progress bars. I am paying close attention to the `WeeklyConsistencyBucket`, `ParentProgressOverviewResponse`, and associated types, and I\'m ensuring all calculations are correct, such as for weekly consistency percentages and the number of active days.\n\n\n**Implementing Data Filtering**\n\nI\'m now implementing the data filtering logic within the `getParentProgressOverview` function. I\'m focusing on handling query parameters such as `dateFrom`, `dateTo`, `domainId`, `completionStatus`, and `reviewStatus`, and the respective interactions and filtering of data from `activityHistory`, and `reviewHistory`. I\'m using strictly parameterized SQLite queries to ensure data integrity and security, computing counts directly from the underlying data sources, and ensuring that draft reviews are excluded from parent visibility. I am carefully constructing and filtering for the parent\'s progress overview now.\n\n\n**Calculating Progress Summaries**\n\nI\'m now implementing the calculation of weekly bars and other progress summaries within the API route. I\'m focusing on accurately computing `weeklyDailyBars`, `activeDaysThisWeek`, and the 4-week `weeklyConsistencyTrend`. I\'m also determining counts for submitted videos, reviewed activities, and pending reviews. The process involves fetching and filtering `activityHistory` (completions, submissions, and reviews) from the database and applying the specified filters (`dateFrom`, `dateTo`, `domainId`, `completionStatus`, and `reviewStatus`). Finally, I\'m fetching and attaching related `reviewHistory`.\n\n\n**Validating Request Parameters**\n\nI\'m now verifying child ownership, and have built a guard that returns a `404` if the child isn\'t associated with the authenticated parent. I\'m also validating the optional query filters, such as `dateFrom`, `dateTo`, `domainId`, `completionStatus`, and `reviewStatus`, using Zod, ensuring that the data conforms to the required format. My next step will be to define and implement the new API endpoint in `api.ts`.\n\n\n**Constructing the Dashboard**\n\nI\'m now integrating the data into a new 6-metric progress dashboard. I\'m focusing on crafting a clean grid layout for the `Activities Completed` and `Activities Remaining` metrics. I\'m also preparing for the `Weekly Consistency` metric, aiming for a clear display of active days. The goal is to present key progress insights with simplicity and clarity.\n\n\n**Designing Dashboard Metrics**\n\nI\'m now integrating the calculated data into the dashboard\'s design. I\'ve defined the metrics to include Weekly Consistency, Domains Explored, Submitted Videos, and Reviewed Activities. I\'m focusing on ensuring these metrics are clear and easily understandable within the existing dashboard layout.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "2iIBa4DUN4-mmtkP_YLoqAE"
