  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Function Call**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the method call, specifically `repo.findChildByIdForParent(req.params.childId, req.authUser!.id)`. That\'s a good place to start the in-depth analysis. My next step involves adding a new route `GET /api/v1/progress/:childId` to the `/server/routes/api.ts` file, and creating a corresponding page at `/src/pages/parent/Progress`.\n\n\n**Designing the Dashboard Section**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in designing `/src/pages/parent/ProgressDashboardSection.tsx` and wiring it into the parent dashboard. I\'m focusing on the non-diagnostic framing of the section, ensuring the header and subtitle explain its purpose as reflective everyday participation and caregiver coaching. I\'m incorporating the editorial journey header with the friendly Montessori illustration, and will use a client-side ES import with a fallback container for the image.\n\n\n**Constructing the Progress Dashboard**\n\nI\'m currently structuring the ProgressDashboardSection into a balanced 2-column split. The left side will hold a stage overview and progress bar, while the right side will feature a Montessori watercolor illustration. I\'m focusing on the dashboard overview, specifically the layout of the six cards displaying key metrics. I will be incorporating summaries, which are real data from the API endpoint. I\'m also preparing for the three segmented views - Overview, Activity History, and Review History.\n\n\n**Defining Activity Visualization**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the visual representation of activity progress. I\'m focusing on the `weeklyDailyBars` chart, ensuring its accessibility with `aria-label` and tabular data. Next, I am working on the calming 4-week horizontal strips (`weeklyConsistencyTrend`), displaying \"X of 7 active days\" and \"Y activities\" to encourage participation. The \"Domain-Wise Activity Participation\" section is next, with progress bars for all six domains and action buttons. Finally, I will be working on the filters in Tab 2, specifically Date Range, Development Domain, and Completion Status, to allow for specific views.\n\n\n**Refining Filter Functionality**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the activity history filters. I\'ve designed a \"Review Status\" dropdown with options like \"Pending review\" and \"Reviewed.\" I\'ve added a prominent \"Reset Filters\" button. The activity history list is also coming along nicely, with clear indicators of activity titles, domains, and statuses. Clicking an item will open the detailed Activity History and Related Review Detail Modal.\n\n\n**Expanding Review History**\n\nI\'ve completed the implementation of the Review History tab. It now meticulously displays all submitted and reviewed video records, clearly labeled with activity names (including version and domain/age stage), submission and review dates (formatted for readability with the locale), instruction-match percentage (when assessable, or a \"Not Assessable\" message with explanation). Each entry includes reviewer feedback (positive observations, areas for improvement, comments, and criterion-wise feedback). I\'ve also incorporated the SecureVideoPlayer, \"Open Activity Guide\" and the video-deleting feature with a `ConfirmDialog`. I\'ve added a primary CTA to open the activity guides, and a helpful empty state is displayed when the filters return no results.\n\n"
    message_id: "lyMBa7fuHPWtz7IPgajuqQU"
