  planner_response {
    response: "Step 9 is complete. Parents now have a dedicated **Progress, Activity History, and Review History** section backed by real activity completion, video submission, and published review records.\n\n### What Was Built\n\n- **Progress Dashboard (`Overview` tab)**\n  - Warm Montessori editorial header banner with a custom mother-and-baby watercolor illustration, stage participation progress bar, and explicit non-diagnostic framing clarifying that participation and coaching notes are never medical or developmental assessments of the baby.\n  - Six participation summary cards reflecting real database records: **Activities Completed**, **Activities Remaining**, **Weekly Consistency** (active days out of 7), **Domain Participation** (areas explored out of 6), **Submitted Videos**, and **Reviewed Activities**.\n  - **Weekly Activity Consistency** simple 7-day bar chart paired with a calm **Four-Week Gentle Rhythm** view\342\200\224avoiding complicated statistics or competitive leaderboards.\n  - **Domain-Wise Activity Participation** grid displaying individual progress bars across all six early-childhood development areas with one-click exploration.\n\n- **Filterable Activity History (`Activity History` tab)**\n  - Supports all four required filters powered by the new authenticated `GET /api/v1/progress/:childId` endpoint: **Date range** (`All time`, `Last 7 days`, `Last 30 days`, or `Custom date range`), **Development domain**, **Completion status**, and **Review status**.\n  - Clicking any history record opens a detail modal showing the recorded date, immutable age-stage snapshot, caregiver reflection notes, linked private video submission, and full related caregiver review\342\200\224plus an **Open Full Activity Guide** action to jump directly back into the activity studio.\n  - Includes descriptive empty states with one-click filter reset.\n\n- **Review History (`Review History` tab)**\n  - Lists submitted and reviewed activity clips with **activity name**, **submission date**, **review date**, **instruction-match percentage** when assessable (or **Not Assessable** with explanation), complete **reviewer feedback** (positive observations, areas to improve, reviewer comments, and criteria-wise breakdown), private playback, and permanent video deletion controls.\n\n### Security & Privacy Safeguards\n\n- **Strict parent ownership enforcement**: The progress endpoint validates the authenticated parent session and verifies ownership of the requested child profile before returning any completion, video, or review history, while blocking other roles (`403`) and unauthenticated requests (`401`).\n- **Draft review isolation & validated filters**: Filter query parameters are validated against strict date and enum schemas with parameterized SQL queries, and unpublished reviewer drafts remain excluded from parent progress and review history responses."
    message_id: "xyUBa__bEqjpz7IP5f2n8As"
    modified_response: "Step 9 is complete. Parents now have a dedicated **Progress, Activity History, and Review History** section backed by real activity completion, video submission, and published review records.\n\n### What Was Built\n\n- **Progress Dashboard (`Overview` tab)**\n  - Warm Montessori editorial header banner with a custom mother-and-baby watercolor illustration, stage participation progress bar, and explicit non-diagnostic framing clarifying that participation and coaching notes are never medical or developmental assessments of the baby.\n  - Six participation summary cards reflecting real database records: **Activities Completed**, **Activities Remaining**, **Weekly Consistency** (active days out of 7), **Domain Participation** (areas explored out of 6), **Submitted Videos**, and **Reviewed Activities**.\n  - **Weekly Activity Consistency** simple 7-day bar chart paired with a calm **Four-Week Gentle Rhythm** view\342\200\224avoiding complicated statistics or competitive leaderboards.\n  - **Domain-Wise Activity Participation** grid displaying individual progress bars across all six early-childhood development areas with one-click exploration.\n\n- **Filterable Activity History (`Activity History` tab)**\n  - Supports all four required filters powered by the new authenticated `GET /api/v1/progress/:childId` endpoint: **Date range** (`All time`, `Last 7 days`, `Last 30 days`, or `Custom date range`), **Development domain**, **Completion status**, and **Review status**.\n  - Clicking any history record opens a detail modal showing the recorded date, immutable age-stage snapshot, caregiver reflection notes, linked private video submission, and full related caregiver review\342\200\224plus an **Open Full Activity Guide** action to jump directly back into the activity studio.\n  - Includes descriptive empty states with one-click filter reset.\n\n- **Review History (`Review History` tab)**\n  - Lists submitted and reviewed activity clips with **activity name**, **submission date**, **review date**, **instruction-match percentage** when assessable (or **Not Assessable** with explanation), complete **reviewer feedback** (positive observations, areas to improve, reviewer comments, and criteria-wise breakdown), private playback, and permanent video deletion controls.\n\n### Security & Privacy Safeguards\n\n- **Strict parent ownership enforcement**: The progress endpoint validates the authenticated parent session and verifies ownership of the requested child profile before returning any completion, video, or review history, while blocking other roles (`403`) and unauthenticated requests (`401`).\n- **Draft review isolation & validated filters**: Filter query parameters are validated against strict date and enum schemas with parameterized SQL queries, and unpublished reviewer drafts remain excluded from parent progress and review history responses."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
    thinking_signature: "\022\230\003\n\225\003\001i\024}\023\341$\245\271\363\222\351\3178\317\372\034\210\374\210B\215\334\r\024\2334@\347\242\n\322\231\035\235\at9\'\325\326\265|\004\203\037M\aQ r\317\275C\241\312>\254\263x\270\250\225\306\307\353\254:\300_qO&Gr\314\'\351C\335T\275\031\247\t\333/\2000\321BSk?Sj\"_\020!\307\030\t4\211-u\223I\023\342g\241\311\322J\024\276\317\203\344FF\234\261\250v]\270\217Z\314DCf\365\343\2278\326CK7\aQ\t\2379\375\317\302(\275\301\365z\225\314x\343\351\3263^\232\324\\\202)\264\373\347\253h\250x\322\226\307kS\203\377\r\374#~\311\261\250\352a\276\222\257eW\224\261\034\353\vr\332q[\246\242H\"\222\206\226\356\216\211\237\a\220\000/\252(\'QQ{\275\247>un\n\344\345:\216\255\270\321\260\205\261g\024\234\263\02194\345\034\355\3464\370\357V\260\364\276\'\000\222Y\004\'\250\273\327\371\226o\220\256\344?#c\250!\222\324\244\003\347?[\315\267\"R\241\026\037\355\260:\335^#P\333\246\377\v\346\037\366\023\256\316-D\233\275Sj\231L\2204\246.\313\341\354x;\245\026iKW\205\334\222\347\312\004\245\2605\371C\3124\267\025\322\306*\324\030L\363\254\232\234\'P\036\302o\224E\250\323/H\001\333\251\023!\263\342|l\252f\2450_\262*`\207\362\235\221\272\003\341\215\036\025\252\264n\352E\364N\320"
