  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Visualizing Structure**\n\nI\'m imagining a clean architecture: the `ParentDashboardView` owning its sidebar/mobile nav, and now I\'m thinking of how an `AdminConsoleView` could have a refined Montessori-editorial 256px desktop. This feels elegant and modular.\n\n\n**Architecting The Admin Modules**\n\nI\'m now integrating a responsive mobile drawer for all nine admin modules, ensuring seamless access across devices. Further, I\'m meticulously mapping every requirement of the admin dashboard build to avoid oversights. The goal is complete modularity and ease-of-use.\n\n\n**Defining Data Persistence**\n\nI\'m solidifying the data persistence strategy now. I\'ve designed an `activity_versions` table for immutable snapshots of activities and rubrics on creation/update. It\'s crucial for version control and audits. Further, I\'m integrating this with existing `video_submissions`, keeping them linked to the exact activity version at the time of submission. I\'m also now building the `admin_audit_logs` table for comprehensive action tracking.\n\n\n**Defining Admin Controls**\n\nI\'m now detailing the database schema for enhanced admin capabilities. I\'m adding `reviewer_permissions_json` to the `users` table, enabling admins to fully manage reviewer accounts and permissions. This will streamline reviewer activation, age group assignments, and specialty notes. I\'m also preparing the endpoints for 9 admin modules and ensuring they\'re gated for admin access.\n\n\n**Detailing Module APIs**\n\nI\'m now diving into the API design for the age group, domain, and activity management modules. I\'m focusing on GET, POST, PUT, and PATCH operations. For activities, I\'m working with versions for immutable data. I\'m defining the database schema, including audit logging for every change in these modules. I\'m building out full field definitions for activity management and handling archival, deletion, and versioning.\n\n\n**Refining Content Creation**\n\nI\'m now detailing an activity\'s core components: an instructional video URL, safety guidelines, rubric criteria that validates to 100 points, and the current status. I\'ve designed a preview modal to render the activity for parents/reviewers exactly, with a \"Confirm & Publish\" button. Editing creates new versions, preserving older ones and linking to existing submissions.\n\n\n\n**Expanding Admin Functionality**\n\nI\'m now implementing APIs for reviewer and submission management, including endpoints for creating, updating, and managing reviewer accounts. I\'ve designed a searchable, sortable, filterable table for submissions with comprehensive actions. The goal is complete admin control. I\'m focusing on user management endpoints next.\n\n\n**Designing Admin DataTables**\n\nI\'m now implementing searchable, sortable, filterable tables for managing all user roles and audit logs. I\'m focusing on unified and paginated audit trails for admin actions, review history, and media privacy access. I\'m building a reusable UI pattern, ensuring a consistent interface with live search and column sorting, with clear ascending/descending toggles.\n\n\n**Implementing UI/UX**\n\nI\'m now integrating filter controls for status, age group, domain, role, and log category to the data tables. I\'m also adding confirmation dialogs for all destructive actions to prevent accidental changes. I\'ll need to provide clear inline validation messages and informative toast notifications to enhance the user experience.\n\n\n**Finalizing Data Implementation**\n\nI\'m now implementing all repository methods with automatic activity version snapshots on create/update. Also, I\'m setting up `logAdminAudit(...)` for every admin mutation and `getUnifiedAuditLogs(...)` for comprehensive tracking. The API routes will be gated behind `requireAuth` and `requireRole(\'admin\')`, complete with Zod validation, self-lockout protection, and audit logging. Concurrently, I\'m building typed client methods for all nine admin modules. Finally, I\'m integrating the reusable table component and each of the specific admin modules. I\'m focusing on the Activity Manager, implementing the Preview and Version History Modals.\n\n\n"
